{"level":30,"time":1778187586605,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KqJdFN7JvgVK59m5kuXUCg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"5d620cdb-67a3-4a00-881f-83a4a595d34f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187586607,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ihvKU2F2FgdEwaX6aeJex","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n     2→\n     3→This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n    11→- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n    12→- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n    13→- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n    14→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n    15→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n    16→- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n    20→- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n    21→- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"da91e663-f9b3-406e-8827-394a5ad5e483","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187586609,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wmwwLMKM9vQqS2FQXdP6s","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n     2→\n     3→Provides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n    11→*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n    12→*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n    13→*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n    14→*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n    15→*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n    16→*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n    21→*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n    22→*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n    23→*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n    24→*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n    25→\n    26→**Plant List Schedules**\n    27→*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n    28→*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n    29→*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n    30→*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n    32→\n    33→**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n    34→*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n    35→*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n    36→*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n    37→*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n    38→*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n    39→\n    40→**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n    46→- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n    47→- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n    48→- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"2c307e94-e5c3-4226-a298-03dcfade532e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-35/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n\nProvides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n\n**Plant List Schedules**\n*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n\n**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n\n**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187586611,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019LeVVbuoQhmPxUhf2NC6NA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n     2→\n     3→Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    18→*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    19→*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n    20→*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n    22→*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n    23→*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    28→    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"2c76c6d4-36e9-431c-9e40-bab77fe9a70d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
