{"level":30,"time":1778187595670,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23TQDTTE5B0M5P9A0FAANB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see from Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) that it shows \"underground electric lines\" in the description. Block 3 of Sheet 21 mentions \"electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters.\" \n\nAnd from Sheet 9 blocks, I see: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\" This suggests the project may be transitioning from overhead to underground service, or there may be existing overhead lines.\n\nBut the key question is: are there EXISTING overhead electric lines on or near the site that the project needs to maintain clearances from? Or is the project proposing only underground service?\n\nThe facts.md mentioned that there are 5' electric easements on the plat (Easement 7 & 8), but these are just recorded easements - they don't necessarily mean overhead lines exist.\n\nI need to check:\n1. Does the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) show any overhead electric poles or lines?\n2. Does the utility plan (Sheet 19) show any overhead facilities?\n3. Are there any building elevation sheets that would show overhead clearances?\n\nLet me check Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and any building elevation sheets.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"5e1df2cf-7b17-435e-9adf-46372a491aa5"}
