{"level":30,"time":1778187600186,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nzby5b3xpUf1pav2whebv2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 4 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This is a detailed site plan drawing showing an existing conditions survey. It includes property lines, buildings (existing slabs), trees, fences, utilities, and topographic contours. Key features include 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' on the left side, 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION' in the center, and 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS' on the right.\n     4→\n     5→The drawing represents an existing conditions survey of a property. It features detailed topographic contours, various trees marked with identifiers (e.g., +4046, +4047), and a large structure footprint labeled 'SLAB F.F.E.-686.8' within 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION VOL. 73, PG. 76 P.R.T.C.TX'. The property is bordered by 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' to the west. Various utility lines, fences (chain link, wood, crete), and easements are depicted. Adjacent properties include 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS VOL. 64, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX' and a property labeled 'WILLIAM LANCE COMSBIE, JR. (1.957 AC.) VOL. 5139, PG. 563 D.R.T.C.TX'. A scale bar and north arrow are present on the left side.\n     6→\n     7→## Block 2: notes — List of cities where Bleyl Engineering operates.\n     8→\n     9→Austin Bryan Conroe Houston\n    10→\n    11→## Block 3: notes — Information regarding the coordinate system and bearing basis used for the survey.\n    12→\n    13→BEARING BASIS:\n    14→BEARINGS, DISTANCES AND COORDINATES ARE\n    15→BASED ON THE TEXAS COORDINATE SYSTEM\n    16→OF 1983 (NAD83) CENTRAL ZONE, GRID.\n    17→\n    18→## Block 5: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n    19→\n    20→JOB NUMBER: 20240953\n    21→\n    22→## Block 8: notes — Certification statement and signature of the Registered Professional Land Surveyor who performed the survey.\n    23→\n    24→THIS SURVEY WAS PERFORMED WITHOUT THE BENEFIT OF A CURRENT\n    25→TITLE COMMITMENT AND THERE MAY BE EASEMENTS, BUILDING LINES,\n    26→CONDITIONS, OR RESTRICTIONS OF RECORD NOT SHOWN OR NOTED\n    27→HEREON.\n    28→DATE OF SURVEY: DECEMBER 27, 2024\n    29→RYAN T. LENZ\n    30→REGISTERED PROFESSIONAL LAND SURVEYOR NO. 7624\n    31→SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.\n    32→TBPELS FIRM No. 10089000\n    33→4150 FREIDRICH LANE, SUITE A-1\n    34→AUSTIN, TEXAS 78744\n    35→(512) 443-1174\n    36→\n    37→## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n    38→\n    39→LEGEND\n    40→\n    41→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n    42→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n    43→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n    44→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n    45→- MAG NAIL SET\n    46→- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n    47→- NAIL FOUND\n    48→- 60D NAIL FOUND\n    49→- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n    50→- IRON PIPE FOUND\n    51→- MAG NAIL FOUND\n    52→- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n    53→- WATER METER\n    54→- WATER VALVE\n    55→- SPRINKLE FOUND\n    56→- WOOD FENCE\n    57→- UTILITY POLE\n    58→- WIRE FENCE\n    59→- LIGHT POLE\n    60→- CRETE FENCE\n    61→- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n    62→- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n    63→- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n    64→- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n    65→- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n    66→- W.L. WATER LINE\n    67→- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n    68→- T.L. TOWN LOT\n    69→- C.I. CURB INLET\n    70→- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n    71→- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n    72→- - CLEAN-OUT\n    73→- - FIRE HYDRANT\n    74→- - AIR CONDITIONER\n    75→- - SIGN POST\n    76→- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n    77→- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    78→- R.P.R.T.C.TX.