{"level":30,"time":1778187619477,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine this landscape plan and identify: 1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If so, where are they located and how are they labeled? 2) Where are trees shown and what symbols are used to mark them? 3) What is the spatial relationship between the overhead electric lines (if present) and any proposed trees? 4) Are any trees shown near property boundaries or existing structures where overhead lines might run?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided landscape plan document, here are the findings addressing your specific questions:\n\n**1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If so, where are they located and how are they labeled?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are shown on this plan. They are located running horizontally along the bottom (southern) perimeter of the property boundary. The lines are indicated by a solid line interrupted periodically by the text label exactly reading: **\"- OHE -\"**\n\n**2) Where are trees shown and what symbols are used to mark them?**\nTrees are shown predominantly along all four perimeters of the site (north/top, south/bottom, east/right, and west/left), as well as within specific interior zones such as the shaded area on the left side of the buildings.\nThe symbols used to mark them generally consist of large circles. Specific variations include:\n*   Plain circles.\n*   Circles with an \"X\" or crosshair marking the center point.\n*   Circles with smaller internal circles.\nMany tree symbols are accompanied by small circular tags containing letters to denote their type. According to the text located below the \"KEY NOTES:\" section, these include:\n*   **\"ST - STREET YARD TREE...\"**\n*   **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE...\"**\n*   **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**\n*   **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**\n\n**3) What is the spatial relationship between the overhead electric lines (if present) and any proposed trees?**\nThere is a direct conflict/overlap shown between the marked overhead electric lines and several trees. Along the bottom boundary, the line labeled **\"- OHE -\"** runs directly through the center of at least five tree symbols. Several of the trees located directly on this \"- OHE -\" line are labeled with a circled **\"M\"** (which the legend identifies as a \"MITIGATION TREE\") and another is marked with an \"X\" symbol inside a circle.\n\n**4) Are any trees shown near property boundaries or existing structures where overhead lines might run?**\nYes, significant numbers of trees are shown directly adjacent to the property boundaries. \n*   **Southern Boundary:** As noted above, a row of trees is placed directly in the path of the documented **\"- OHE -\"** line running along the bottom property edge.\n*   **Other Boundaries:** Numerous trees are also located tightly along the northern (top), eastern (right), and western (left) property boundaries, though no \"- OHE -\" lines are explicitly marked along those specific edges on this sheet. \n*   The main building structures are centrally located, and while there are trees near them (especially in the western \"STREET YARD\"), the only explicitly marked overhead line (\"- OHE -\") is constrained to the southern boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1401,"outputTokens":592,"totalTokens":3509,"reasoningTokens":1516},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention