anting restrictions near utilities.\n\n5.  **What trees are shown near the overhead lines, if any? Are they labeled with species or size information that would indicate if they are utility-compatible?**\n    There are several proposed trees (represented by circular symbols) shown directly adjacent to, and in some cases overlapping, the \"- OHE -\" line along the southern boundary.\n    *   These trees do **not** have specific species or size labels attached to them on this sheet.\n    *   Some trees have standard legend tags (e.g., one near the bottom right is labeled with an \"M\"). According to the legend below the Key Notes, \"M\" stands for **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n    *   Because there is no plant schedule, species callout, or mature height information provided on this specific sheet, it is impossible to determine from this page alone if the trees placed under or near the overhead lines are utility-compatible species."}]}
