{"level":30,"time":1778187631583,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YUKZmngKN6mLkwwg5x3bdA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a136e13c-2680-4375-811f-a5416413e77d","uuid":"06d22ba3-0537-4483-9ebd-30f5ae55cf56","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187632662,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical design plan and provide detailed information about:\n1. The number and locations of transformer pads shown on the site plan\n2. The proximity of transformer pads to buildings, parking areas, structures, and fences\n3. Any dimensions, clearances, or measurements indicated for transformer pads\n4. The labeling or identification of each transformer pad (e.g., \"TRANS-1\", \"XFMR\", specific equipment designations)\n5. Whether there are any access door orientations visible\n6. Any notations about clearances, utilities, or special requirements for the transformer pads\n7. The overall layout showing which buildings are served by which transformers\nPlease be specific about locations (e.g., \"between Building 1 and 2\", \"near southwest corner\", etc.) and note any visual indicators of pad dimensions or protection requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the \"Valley View Townhomes\" project, here is the information regarding the electrical transformer pads. \n\nThe electrical infrastructure is designated on the plan by blue lines and blue boxed symbols.\n\n**1. The number and locations of transformer pads shown on the site plan**\nThere are exactly **four (4)** transformer pads identified on this site plan. Their general locations are:\n*   **Pad 1 (West/Entrance):** Located on the far west side of the property line, near the main entrance drive and adjacent to a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Pad 2 (Mid-West):** Located centrally in the western half of the site, situated in the space between the southern end of Bldg. 2 and the northern end of Bldg. 8.\n*   **Pad 3 (Mid-East):** Located centrally in the eastern half of the site, situated in the open space bounded by Bldg. 4 to the west, Bldg. 5 to the north, and Bldg. 6 to the south.\n*   **Pad 4 (South-Central):** Located near the southern property boundary, situated in the space between the eastern end of Bldg. 8 and the southern end of Bldg. 7.\n\n**2. The proximity of transformer pads to buildings, parking areas, structures, and fences**\n*   **Pad 1:** Sits in a landscaped/open area near the street entrance curb. It is not immediately adjacent to any building walls or parking spaces.\n*   **Pad 2:** Located in the grassy area between Bldg. 2 (near Unit 201) and Bldg. 8 (near Unit 801). It is near the building footprints but not touching them. \n*   **Pad 3:** Located in a central open/grassy area. It is set back from the building footprints of Bldgs 4, 5, and 6. \n*   **Pad 4:** Located in an open area between Bldg. 7 (near Unit 703) and Bldg. 8 (near Unit 806). It is located very close to the southern property line which is indicated by a line style labeled \"Wood Fence\".\n\n**3. Any dimensions, clearances, or measurements indicated for transformer pads**\n*   There are **no numerical dimensions** (length x width) provided for the transformer pads on this specific sheet.\n*   There are **no clearance radii, safety zones, or setback measurements** drawn or labeled around any of the transformer pads. They are represented simply by solid blue rectangular outlines.\n\n**4. The labeling or identification of each transformer pad**\n*   All four pads are labeled identically. A leader line points to each blue rectangle with the exact text: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n*   There are no specific alphanumeric equipment designations (e.g., \"XFMR-1\", \"T-A\") provided for any of the individual pads.\n\n**5. Whether there are any access door orientations visible**\n*   **No access door orientations are visible.** The symbols are plain rectangles without any line weight variations, arrows, or text indicating which side the doors open or where the working clearance is required.\n\n**6. Any notations about clearances, utilities, or special requirements for the transformer pads**\n*   There are no general notes or specific callouts on this page detailing clearance requirements or specific installation instructions for the transformer pads.\n*   Next to **Pad 2**, there is a dashed box bounding the area of the pad and an adjacent Pull Box, accompanied by a label that reads **\"Vault Easement\"**.\n*   The \"Utility Notes\" in the bottom right corner are general (e.g., \"Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\") and do not specifically mention transformers.\n\n**7. The overall layout showing which buildings are served by which transformers**\nThe site uses a networked system where blue electrical lines connect Transformer Pads to \"Electrical Pull Box\" nodes, which then route to \"Electrical Meters\" located on the buildings. Based on tracing the primary routing of the blue lines from the pull boxes adjacent to the transformers:\n\n*   **Pad 1 (West Entrance):** The line connects from this pad to a pull box, then routes west off the property line, labeled **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. This appears to be the main feed tying the site into the municipal grid, rather than serving a specific building directly.\n*   **Pad 2 (Mid-West):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the west side of **Bldg. 2** (Units 201-204) and the west side of **Bldg. 8** (Units 801-804).\n*   **Pad 3 (Mid-East):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on **Bldg. 5** (Units 501-504), **Bldg. 6** (Units 601-603), and the eastern meter bank of **Bldg. 4** (near Units 403-404).\n*   **Pad 4 (South-Central):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on **Bldg. 7** (Units 701-704), the eastern meter bank of **Bldg. 8** (near Units 805-806), and lines also route northward from this area to serve the meters on **Bldg. 3** (Units 301-303), the western meter bank of **Bldg. 4** (near Units 401-402), and **Bldg. 1** (Units 102-104).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1481,"outputTokens":1277,"totalTokens":5318,"reasoningTokens":2560},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this electrical design plan and provide detailed information about:\n1. The number and locations of transformer pads shown on the site plan\n2. The proximity of transformer pads to buildings, parking areas, structures, and fences\n3. Any dimensions, clearances, or measurements indicated for transformer pads\n4. The labeling or identification of each transformer pad (e.g., \"TRANS-1\", \"XFMR\", specific equipment designations)\n5. Whether there are any access door orientations visible\n6. Any notations about clearances, utilities, or special requirements for the transformer pads\n7. The overall layout showing which buildings are served by which transformers\nPlease be specific about locations (e.g., \"between Building 1 and 2\", \"near southwest corner\", etc.) and note any visual indicators of pad dimensions or protection requirements."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"790d4c46-cd86-49b4-a255-a4397ca7ac09","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_BASELINE_V3","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-FizdhvCe9rj9cDB5mgwG5miU","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:00:32 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::z29bz-1778187592317-4cbd814a326c"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the \"Valley View Townhomes\" project, here is the information regarding the electrical transformer pads. \n\nThe electrical infrastructure is designated on the plan by blue lines and blue boxed symbols.\n\n**1. The number and locations of transformer pads shown on the site plan**\nThere are exactly **four (4)** transformer pads identified on this site plan. Their general locations are:\n*   **Pad 1 (West/Entrance):** Located on the far west side of the property line, near the main entrance drive and adjacent to a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Pad 2 (Mid-West):** Located centrally in the western half of the site, situated in the space between the southern end of Bldg. 2 and the northern end of Bldg. 8.\n*   **Pad 3 (Mid-East):** Located centrally in the eastern half of the site, situated in the open space bounded by Bldg. 4 to the west, Bldg. 5 to the north, and Bldg. 6 to the south.\n*   **Pad 4 (South-Central):** Located near the southern property boundary, situated in the space between the eastern end of Bldg. 8 and the southern end of Bldg. 7.\n\n**2. The proximity of transformer pads to buildings, parking areas, structures, and fences**\n*   **Pad 1:** Sits in a landscaped/open area near the street entrance curb. It is not immediately adjacent to any building walls or parking spaces.\n*   **Pad 2:** Located in the grassy area between Bldg. 2 (near Unit 201) and Bldg. 8 (near Unit 801). It is near the building footprints but not touching them. \n*   **Pad 3:** Located in a central open/grassy area. It is set back from the building footprints of Bldgs 4, 5, and 6. \n*   **Pad 4:** Located in an open area between Bldg. 7 (near Unit 703) and Bldg. 8 (near Unit 806). It is located very close to the southern property line which is indicated by a line style labeled \"Wood Fence\".\n\n**3. Any dimensions, clearances, or measurements indicated for transformer pads**\n*   There are **no numerical dimensions** (length x width) provided for the transformer pads on this specific sheet.\n*   There are **no clearance radii, safety zones, or setback measurements** drawn or labeled around any of the transformer pads. They are represented simply by solid blue rectangular outlines.\n\n**4. The labeling or identification of each transformer pad**\n*   All four pads are labeled identically. A leader line points to each blue rectangle with the exact text: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n*   There are no specific alphanumeric equipment designations (e.g., \"XFMR-1\", \"T-A\") provided for any of the individual pads.\n\n**5. Whether there are any access door orientations visible**\n*   **No access door orientations are visible.** The symbols are plain rectangles without any line weight variations, arrows, or text indicating which side the doors open or where the working clearance is required.\n\n**6. Any notations about clearances, utilities, or special requirements for the transformer pads**\n*   There are no general notes or specific callouts on this page detailing clearance requirements or specific installation instructions for the transformer pads.\n*   Next to **Pad 2**, there is a dashed box bounding the area of the pad and an adjacent Pull Box, accompanied by a label that reads **\"Vault Easement\"**.\n*   The \"Utility Notes\" in the bottom right corner are general (e.g., \"Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\") and do not specifically mention transformers.\n\n**7. The overall layout showing which buildings are served by which transformers**\nThe site uses a networked system where blue electrical lines connect Transformer Pads to \"Electrical Pull Box\" nodes, which then route to \"Electrical Meters\" located on the buildings. Based on tracing the primary routing of the blue lines from the pull boxes adjacent to the transformers:\n\n*   **Pad 1 (West Entrance):** The line connects from this pad to a pull box, then routes west off the property line, labeled **\"Underground Electric Line\"**. This appears to be the main feed tying the site into the municipal grid, rather than serving a specific building directly.\n*   **Pad 2 (Mid-West):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the west side of **Bldg. 2** (Units 201-204) and the west side of **Bldg. 8** (Units 801-804).\n*   **Pad 3 (Mid-East):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on **Bldg. 5** (Units 501-504), **Bldg. 6** (Units 601-603), and the eastern meter bank of **Bldg. 4** (near Units 403-404).\n*   **Pad 4 (South-Central):** Lines route from the pull box adjacent to this transformer to serve the **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on **Bldg. 7** (Units 701-704), the eastern meter bank of **Bldg. 8** (near Units 805-806), and lines also route northward from this area to serve the meters on **Bldg. 3** (Units 301-303), the western meter bank of **Bldg. 4** (near Units 401-402), and **Bldg. 1** (Units 102-104).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1481,"outputTokens":1277,"totalTokens":5318,"reasoningTokens":2560},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-