{"level":30,"time":1778187638055,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TEsagQz4HMMjaXkzZeaXVn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n     4→\n     5→[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→\n     8→## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n     9→\n    10→The plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n    11→\n    12→*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n    13→*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n    14→*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n    15→*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n    16→*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n    17→*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n    18→*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n    19→*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n    20→\n    21→## Block 3: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n    22→\n    23→Legal Description\n    24→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    25→\n    26→## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n    27→\n    28→Tree List\n    29→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    30→\n    31→## Block 5: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n    32→\n    33→Legend\n    34→[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n    35→[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n    36→[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n    37→700.00\n    38→699.50 Top of Curb\n    39→Bottom of Curb\n    40→[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n    41→[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\n    42→L= Level Landing\n    43→(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\n    44→Down [arrow] ADA Ramp\n    45→(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n    46→\n    47→## Block 6: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n    48→\n    49→Curb Note:\n    50→Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\n    51→away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n    52→\n    53→## Block 7: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n    54→\n    55→Benchmarks\n    56→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    57→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    58→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    59→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    60→\n    61→## Block 11: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n    62→\n    63→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\n    64→applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\n    65→submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    66→\n    67→## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n    68→\n    69→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\n    70→match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\n    71→locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\n    72→construction.\n    73→\n    74→## Block 14: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n    75→\n    76→Call Before You Dig!!\n    77→\n    78→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a136e13c-2680-4375-811f-a5416413e77d","uuid":"2cabc6a0-632a-4892-9f9b-63539dd6ecce","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n\n[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n\n## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n\nThe plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n\n*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n\n## Block 3: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n\nTree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 5: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n\nLegend\n[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n700.00\n699.50 Top of Curb\nBottom of Curb\n[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\nL= Level Landing\n(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\nDown [arrow] ADA Ramp\n(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n\n## Block 6: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n\nCurb Note:\nGrading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\naway from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n\n## Block 7: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\napplicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\nsubmittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\nmatch locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\nlocations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\nconstruction.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n\nCall Before You Dig!!\n\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187638057,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NpJw8bSoBVeeTSkHt79gWa","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    15→* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    16→* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n    17→* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    19→* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n    20→* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n    21→* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n    22→* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    23→* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    26→\n    27→* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    28→  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n    29→  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n    30→\n    31→* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n    32→  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n    33→  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n    34→\n    35→* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n    36→  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n    37→  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n    38→\n    39→* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n    40→  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n    41→  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n    42→\n    43→* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n    44→  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n    45→  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n    46→\n    47→* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n    48→  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n    49→  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n    50→\n    51→* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    52→  Provides surveyor reference points.\n    53→  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n    54→\n    55→* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n    56→  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n    57→  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n    58→\n    59→* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    60→  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n    61→  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a136e13c-2680-4375-811f-a5416413e77d","uuid":"5fbf759f-5e37-4ea5-b5d3-138999dd0c42","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n\nSite plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n\n**Key values**:\n* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n\n* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n\n* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n\n* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n\n* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n\n* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n\n* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n  Provides surveyor reference points.\n  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n\n* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n\n* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
