{"level":30,"time":1778187649683,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sbu7w6HDKAKxjNnWRR2ws5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n     2→\n     3→Construction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n    11→*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n    12→*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n    13→*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n    14→*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n    15→*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n    16→*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n    17→*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n    22→*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n    23→*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n    24→*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n    25→*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n    26→*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n    27→*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n    28→*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n    29→*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n    30→*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n    31→*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-11.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"f6e87618-3edc-4739-bbee-466d264af9ee","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-22/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n\nConstruction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n\n---\n\n- `block-11.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187649684,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B4a4pWsgY1oFUURBWpdbb1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 23 — Construction Details 2\n     2→\n     3→Standard construction details for water infrastructure, valves, and fire hydrants.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains \"Construction Details 2\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, specifically focusing on City of Austin standard details. It provides specifications, cross-sections, and installation procedures for typical gate valves (4\"-16\"), fire hydrant assemblies, and utility trenching with unfinished surfaces.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Gate Valves:**\n    11→    *   Clearance: 3\" - 5\"\n    12→    *   Concrete Block (for valves <12\"): 16\" x 16\" x 4\" minimum\n    13→    *   Concrete cradle: Minimum 2000 P.S.I., Class B\n    14→    *   Concrete pad patch: 3' x 3' minimum (Item 403S Class \"A\") with 5\" minimum depth and #5 rebar at mid-depth.\n    15→    *   Total depth of asphalt + concrete: 9\" minimum\n    16→    *   Stem extensions required when valves exceed 3' deep from finished grade; extension nut must be 12\" - 18\" from finished grade.\n    17→    *   Valve component weights: C7 Lid = 13 lbs, Reclaimed Lid = 15 lbs, C6 Frame = 23 lbs, Reclaimed Frame = 33 lbs, C5 Base = 76 lbs.\n    18→*   **Fire Hydrants:**\n    19→    *   Clearances: 3' around hydrant, minimum 18\" from face of curb to steamer nozzle.\n    20→    *   Distance from ADA/pedestrian elements: Minimum 4' from ramps, strictly >6\" from any sidewalk.\n    21→    *   Hydrant Bury Depth: 4' - 5'\n    22→    *   Drainage pit: 24\" diameter and 12\" deep below the hydrant bowl.\n    23→*   **Trenching (Unfinished Surface):**\n    24→    *   Minimum cover: 300 mm (12\")\n    25→    *   Bedding envelope below pipe: 150 mm (6\")\n    26→    *   Trench width: Pipe O.D. + 300 mm (12\") minimum to Pipe O.D. + 600 mm (24\") maximum.\n    27→\n    28→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 1:** diagram — Vertical and horizontal gate valve castings. **VISION** for assembly layout and concrete block placement; **READ** for notes on stem extensions and purple/reclaimed water specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 2:** diagram — Valve riser cross-sections in full depth concrete and unpaved areas. **VISION** for spatial layout of the concrete pad and rebar; **READ** for sub-grade and paving frame requirements.\n    32→*   **Block 3 & 23:** diagram & table — Top views and sections of valve lids, frames, and boots. **VISION** for dimensions (e.g., 7 1/2\" diameter C7 lid, 9 1/4\" square reclaimed frame); **READ** Block 23 for component weights and Block 3 notes for material requirements (ASTM A48, Grade 30B).\n    33→*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n    34→*   **Block 8:** diagram — Deep water main fire hydrant installations. **VISION** for pipe configurations, 90-degree bend setups, and restraint locations.\n    35→*   **Block 5:** diagram — Typical trench detail with unfinished surface. **VISION** for the cross-section profile; **READ** for exact depth and width dimensions for the bedding envelope.\n    36→*   **Block 6:** diagram — Optional one-piece valve casting installation. **VISION** for the step-by-step visual guide to raising and lowering the riser to final grade.\n    37→*   **Blocks 7 & 9:** notes — General fire hydrant installation notes (Note: these blocks are identical). **READ** for strict spacing requirements, 24\" drainage pit specifications, 8-mil poly-film wrap instructions, and pavement marker locations.\n    38→*   **Block 10:** notes — Valve pad and delineator requirements. **READ** for required asphalt/concrete depths and instructions on placing blue/purple delineator stakes in unpaved areas.\n    39→*   **Blocks 11, 12, 13:** notes — Text extracts duplicating the notes found within the diagrams of Blocks 1, 3, and 2 respectively. **READ** only if the text in the main diagrams is illegible.\n    40→*   **Block 14:** notes — References. **READ** for standard specification manual sections (Item 510).\n    41→*   **Blocks 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the PE seal, project tracking info, and standard City of Austin title blocks (511-AW-01, 511-AW-02, 510S-5) for each standard detail. No review action needed.\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-2.md` — diagram: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n    46→- `block-8.md` — diagram: Cross-section details for valve placement in full depth concrete and unpaved areas.\n    47→- `block-15.md` — notes: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n    48→\n    49→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    50→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"a21068a2-3d42-4f20-983f-c52bd9269e68","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 23 — Construction Details 2\n\nStandard construction details for water infrastructure, valves, and fire hydrants.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains \"Construction Details 2\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, specifically focusing on City of Austin standard details. It provides specifications, cross-sections, and installation procedures for typical gate valves (4\"-16\"), fire hydrant assemblies, and utility trenching with unfinished surfaces.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Gate Valves:**\n    *   Clearance: 3\" - 5\"\n    *   Concrete Block (for valves <12\"): 16\" x 16\" x 4\" minimum\n    *   Concrete cradle: Minimum 2000 P.S.I., Class B\n    *   Concrete pad patch: 3' x 3' minimum (Item 403S Class \"A\") with 5\" minimum depth and #5 rebar at mid-depth.\n    *   Total depth of asphalt + concrete: 9\" minimum\n    *   Stem extensions required when valves exceed 3' deep from finished grade; extension nut must be 12\" - 18\" from finished grade.\n    *   Valve component weights: C7 Lid = 13 lbs, Reclaimed Lid = 15 lbs, C6 Frame = 23 lbs, Reclaimed Frame = 33 lbs, C5 Base = 76 lbs.\n*   **Fire Hydrants:**\n    *   Clearances: 3' around hydrant, minimum 18\" from face of curb to steamer nozzle.\n    *   Distance from ADA/pedestrian elements: Minimum 4' from ramps, strictly >6\" from any sidewalk.\n    *   Hydrant Bury Depth: 4' - 5'\n    *   Drainage pit: 24\" diameter and 12\" deep below the hydrant bowl.\n*   **Trenching (Unfinished Surface):**\n    *   Minimum cover: 300 mm (12\")\n    *   Bedding envelope below pipe: 150 mm (6\")\n    *   Trench width: Pipe O.D. + 300 mm (12\") minimum to Pipe O.D. + 600 mm (24\") maximum.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1:** diagram — Vertical and horizontal gate valve castings. **VISION** for assembly layout and concrete block placement; **READ** for notes on stem extensions and purple/reclaimed water specifications.\n*   **Block 2:** diagram — Valve riser cross-sections in full depth concrete and unpaved areas. **VISION** for spatial layout of the concrete pad and rebar; **READ** for sub-grade and paving frame requirements.\n*   **Block 3 & 23:** diagram & table — Top views and sections of valve lids, frames, and boots. **VISION** for dimensions (e.g., 7 1/2\" diameter C7 lid, 9 1/4\" square reclaimed frame); **READ** Block 23 for component weights and Block 3 notes for material requirements (ASTM A48, Grade 30B).\n*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n*   **Block 8:** diagram — Deep water main fire hydrant installations. **VISION** for pipe configurations, 90-degree bend setups, and restraint locations.\n*   **Block 5:** diagram — Typical trench detail with unfinished surface. **VISION** for the cross-section profile; **READ** for exact depth and width dimensions for the bedding envelope.\n*   **Block 6:** diagram — Optional one-piece valve casting installation. **VISION** for the step-by-step visual guide to raising and lowering the riser to final grade.\n*   **Blocks 7 & 9:** notes — General fire hydrant installation notes (Note: these blocks are identical). **READ** for strict spacing requirements, 24\" drainage pit specifications, 8-mil poly-film wrap instructions, and pavement marker locations.\n*   **Block 10:** notes — Valve pad and delineator requirements. **READ** for required asphalt/concrete depths and instructions on placing blue/purple delineator stakes in unpaved areas.\n*   **Blocks 11, 12, 13:** notes — Text extracts duplicating the notes found within the diagrams of Blocks 1, 3, and 2 respectively. **READ** only if the text in the main diagrams is illegible.\n*   **Block 14:** notes — References. **READ** for standard specification manual sections (Item 510).\n*   **Blocks 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the PE seal, project tracking info, and standard City of Austin title blocks (511-AW-01, 511-AW-02, 510S-5) for each standard detail. No review action needed.\n\n---\n\n- `block-2.md` — diagram: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n- `block-8.md` — diagram: Cross-section details for valve placement in full depth concrete and unpaved areas.\n- `block-15.md` — notes: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187649686,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZyjhvHewcrWAmyxLnZuK9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 24 — Construction Details 3\n     2→\n     3→Standard construction details for water services and trench repairs.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides standard City of Austin construction details for water infrastructure and pavement repair. Its primary purpose is to specify the installation and abandonment requirements for water services and meters, as well as the structural layering and dimensional requirements for trench repair in existing asphaltic surfaces.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Trench Repair HMAC Surface:** Minimum 2\" (50 mm) Type \"D\" for local/residential streets; Minimum 3\" (75 mm) Type \"C\" for collector/arterial streets.\n    11→*   **Trench Repair Flexible Base:** Replace in kind plus 3\" (75 mm), but no less than 12\" (300 mm) total thickness. Maximum layer thickness is 12\" (300 mm).\n    12→*   **Trench Repair Saw Cut:** Minimum 12\" (300 mm) wider than undisturbed trench sides, with a minimum 6\" (150 mm) cut back on both sides of the trench.\n    13→*   **Trench Repair Minimum Cover:** 30\" (750 mm) over the utility line.\n    14→*   **Damaged Pavement (Outside Trench):** Replace with a base thickness of 10\" (250 mm) or match existing, whichever is greater.\n    15→*   **Tracer Tape Placement:** 12\" (300 mm) below subgrade over the centerline of the pipe, or 18\" (450 mm) below finished grade outside pavement limits.\n    16→*   **Water Tubing Cover:** Minimum 2' depth of cover behind curb and gutter.\n    17→*   **Water Tubing Bend Radii:** Minimum 3' radius for 1\" tubing; minimum 5' radius for 2\" tubing.\n    18→*   **Meter Box Placement:** Top of box should be 4\" above ground, located behind the curb next to the property line/easement, and no more than 36\" below final grade.\n    19→*   **Abandonment Removal Depth:** Remove all materials to 36\" below grade if a ball valve coupling does not exist.\n    20→\n    21→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    22→\n    23→*   **Blocks 1 & 5:** diagram — Trench Repair Cross-sections. Use VISION to examine the structural layers (HMAC, base, subgrade, bedding), cutback locations, and minimum dimensional callouts for asphalt trench repair.\n    24→*   **Block 14:** notes — Trench Repair Notes. READ the block content for specific pavement and base replacement thicknesses, asphalt material types based on street classification, concrete substitution allowances, and tracer tape placement requirements.\n    25→*   **Blocks 3 & 4:** diagram — Water Service Tap Details (Plan & Profile). Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, hardware orientation, and required clearances (e.g., 2' min, 4'-1/4\" min) relative to the right-of-way/easement lines.\n    26→*   **Block 13:** notes — Water Service Installation Notes. READ the block content for critical installation rules including wrapping requirements, minimum bend radii, meter box placement, and specific requirements for reclaimed water components (purple parts/paint).\n    27→*   **Block 16:** notes — Water Service Materials List. READ the block content for exact material specifications (splices, stops, valves, tubing) and the explicit division of items to be installed by the plumber versus those purchased from Austin Water.\n    28→*   **Block 2:** diagram — Abandonment of Services at the Main (Multiple Meters). Use VISION to observe the required locations for physical separation and the limits of material removal.\n    29→*   **Blocks 12 & 17:** notes — Abandonment of Services (Multiple Meters) Notes & Materials. READ the block content for the step-by-step procedural requirements, required removal depths (36\" below grade), polyethylene wrapping, and the required materials list (A-P).\n    30→*   **Blocks 15 & 18:** notes — Abandonment of Services (Single Meter) Notes & Materials. READ the block content for single-meter abandonment steps and materials, which largely mirror the multiple-meter requirements but exclude the tee/wye component.\n    31→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 19, 20:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. These blocks contain standard City of Austin detail title blocks, the primary sheet title block (Bleyl Engineering, Valley View Townhomes), and the engineer's seal.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-16.md` — notes: General notes for trench repair detailing saw cutting, maintenance for traffic, base replacement, HM\n    36→- `block-17.md` — notes: General notes providing instructions and specifications for water service installation, including wr\n    37→\n    38→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    39→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"48e74b05-3a49-47b9-a25d-ae27bd7c1e0f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-24/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 24 — Construction Details 3\n\nStandard construction details for water services and trench repairs.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides standard City of Austin construction details for water infrastructure and pavement repair. Its primary purpose is to specify the installation and abandonment requirements for water services and meters, as well as the structural layering and dimensional requirements for trench repair in existing asphaltic surfaces.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Trench Repair HMAC Surface:** Minimum 2\" (50 mm) Type \"D\" for local/residential streets; Minimum 3\" (75 mm) Type \"C\" for collector/arterial streets.\n*   **Trench Repair Flexible Base:** Replace in kind plus 3\" (75 mm), but no less than 12\" (300 mm) total thickness. Maximum layer thickness is 12\" (300 mm).\n*   **Trench Repair Saw Cut:** Minimum 12\" (300 mm) wider than undisturbed trench sides, with a minimum 6\" (150 mm) cut back on both sides of the trench.\n*   **Trench Repair Minimum Cover:** 30\" (750 mm) over the utility line.\n*   **Damaged Pavement (Outside Trench):** Replace with a base thickness of 10\" (250 mm) or match existing, whichever is greater.\n*   **Tracer Tape Placement:** 12\" (300 mm) below subgrade over the centerline of the pipe, or 18\" (450 mm) below finished grade outside pavement limits.\n*   **Water Tubing Cover:** Minimum 2' depth of cover behind curb and gutter.\n*   **Water Tubing Bend Radii:** Minimum 3' radius for 1\" tubing; minimum 5' radius for 2\" tubing.\n*   **Meter Box Placement:** Top of box should be 4\" above ground, located behind the curb next to the property line/easement, and no more than 36\" below final grade.\n*   **Abandonment Removal Depth:** Remove all materials to 36\" below grade if a ball valve coupling does not exist.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Blocks 1 & 5:** diagram — Trench Repair Cross-sections. Use VISION to examine the structural layers (HMAC, base, subgrade, bedding), cutback locations, and minimum dimensional callouts for asphalt trench repair.\n*   **Block 14:** notes — Trench Repair Notes. READ the block content for specific pavement and base replacement thicknesses, asphalt material types based on street classification, concrete substitution allowances, and tracer tape placement requirements.\n*   **Blocks 3 & 4:** diagram — Water Service Tap Details (Plan & Profile). Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, hardware orientation, and required clearances (e.g., 2' min, 4'-1/4\" min) relative to the right-of-way/easement lines.\n*   **Block 13:** notes — Water Service Installation Notes. READ the block content for critical installation rules including wrapping requirements, minimum bend radii, meter box placement, and specific requirements for reclaimed water components (purple parts/paint).\n*   **Block 16:** notes — Water Service Materials List. READ the block content for exact material specifications (splices, stops, valves, tubing) and the explicit division of items to be installed by the plumber versus those purchased from Austin Water.\n*   **Block 2:** diagram — Abandonment of Services at the Main (Multiple Meters). Use VISION to observe the required locations for physical separation and the limits of material removal.\n*   **Blocks 12 & 17:** notes — Abandonment of Services (Multiple Meters) Notes & Materials. READ the block content for the step-by-step procedural requirements, required removal depths (36\" below grade), polyethylene wrapping, and the required materials list (A-P).\n*   **Blocks 15 & 18:** notes — Abandonment of Services (Single Meter) Notes & Materials. READ the block content for single-meter abandonment steps and materials, which largely mirror the multiple-meter requirements but exclude the tee/wye component.\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 19, 20:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. These blocks contain standard City of Austin detail title blocks, the primary sheet title block (Bleyl Engineering, Valley View Townhomes), and the engineer's seal.\n\n---\n\n- `block-16.md` — notes: General notes for trench repair detailing saw cutting, maintenance for traffic, base replacement, HM\n- `block-17.md` — notes: General notes providing instructions and specifications for water service installation, including wr\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187653466,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify: 1) Location of parking areas and driveways relative to buildings, 2) Fire lanes (any marked with stripes or notes), 3) Sidewalks and pedestrian walkways, 4) Any retaining walls or fences, 5) Location of detention/biofiltration pond, 6) Property lines and existing right-of-way, 7) Any transformer pads if visible. Provide specific locations (e.g., \"northwest corner\", \"between Bldg 1 and Bldg 2\") for each feature.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the requested details. All transcribed text is quoted exactly as it appears.\n\n**1) Location of parking areas and driveways relative to buildings:**\n*   **Main Driveway:** A central driveway runs east-west through the middle of the site, separating the northern row of buildings from the southern row. It enters from the western boundary and is labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 1/335-2\".\n*   **Secondary Driveway/Access:** Another driveway enters from the western boundary further north, labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 4/335-2\". It leads to a turning area west of Bldg 1 and a \"2 - Point Access Gate\" near Bldg 3.\n*   **Parking Areas:** Surface parking spaces are arranged perpendicularly along the central east-west driveway. Specifically, they are located immediately south of Bldg 1, Bldg 2, Bldg 3, Bldg 4, and Bldg 5, and immediately north of Bldg 8, Bldg 7, and Bldg 6.\n*   **Parking Data:** The \"Parking Data\" table indicates \"10 Surface/ 78 Garage\" spaces provided.\n\n**2) Fire lanes (any marked with stripes or notes):**\n*   **Striped Areas:** Striped zones (typically indicating no parking/fire lanes or turning radii clear zones) are visible at various points within the main driveways. Specifically, stripes are visible at the western ends of the parking rows, in the turnaround area north of Bldg 1, and at the eastern end of the central driveway between Bldg 5 and Bldg 6.\n*   **Notes:** There is a label that appears to read \"Fire\" with an arrow pointing toward a striped area at the eastern edge of the central driveway, near the southeast corner of Bldg 5.\n\n**3) Sidewalks and pedestrian walkways:**\n*   **Western Perimeter:** A sidewalk runs north-south along the western property line/street frontage, labeled \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dt. 4/335-2\" (this label appears twice, near both driveway entrances).\n*   **Northern Perimeter:** A path runs east-west along the northern boundary, north of buildings 1 through 4, labeled in multiple segments as \"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\".\n*   **Internal Pathways:** Sidewalks connect the building entrances to the parking areas. There is an internal sidewalk running north-south between Bldg 2 and Bldg 3 labeled \"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ.) See Dtl 4/335-2\". Sidewalks also frame the \"Common Open Space\" located between the northern and southern building rows.\n\n**4) Any retaining walls or fences:**\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Retaining walls are noted near the northeast corner/detention pond, labeled \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"Concrete Retaining Wall\". A \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" is also labeled here.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Along the eastern edge behind Bldg 5 and Bldg 6, there are labels stating \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\". A \"Wood Fence\" line is indicated running along this eastern boundary.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Along the southern edge, there are multiple retaining wall notes. From west to east, they read: \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\", \"Concrete Retaining Wall\", and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\" (this last note appears twice).\n*   **Fence Note:** There is a \"Fence Note\" in the bottom right quadrant of the document providing construction details.\n\n**5) Location of detention/biofiltration pond:**\n*   **Location:** The pond is located in the northeast corner of the site plan.\n*   **Label:** It is explicitly labeled \"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\".\n\n**6) Property lines and existing right-of-way:**\n*   **Right-of-Way:** The existing right-of-way is located along the western boundary of the site. It contains an \"Existing Water Line\" and a \"Wastewater Easement\".\n*   **Property Lines:** The property boundary encloses the site. The northern boundary includes a bearing and distance label reading \"N 62° 02' 28'' E 119.59'\". The southern boundary includes a label reading \"N 62° 36' 57'' W 414.24'\".\n\n**7) Any transformer pads if visible:**\n*   **Location:** A transformer pad is visible near the western edge of the property, located just north of the southern \"Construct Type II Driveway\" entrance, west of Bldg 8.\n*   **Label:** It is enclosed in a square and labeled \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\". Directly adjacent to it is a note reading \"Tree Well need to look up approp. detail\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1425,"outputTokens":1051,"totalTokens":4580,"reasoningTokens":2104},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values e