{"level":30,"time":1778187656224,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LND2tPqGJNMKuwnHyWwWEN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 25 — Construction Details 4\n     2→\n     3→Standard details, plan, and section views for fire line meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides City of Austin standard construction details for a 6\", 8\", or 10\" fire line meter vault installation for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a comprehensive plan layout, vertical cross-sections, a material schedule, and specifications for vault dimensions based on meter size.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   Applicable Meter Sizes: 6\", 8\", or 10\"\n    11→*   Vault Dimensions (Inside): 8' x 12' (for 6\" meter), 10' x 12' (for 8\" meter), 10' x 15' (for 10\" meter)\n    12→*   Access Hatch Size: 48\" x 72\"\n    13→*   Minimum Clearances: 18\" clearance between vault wall and bypass piping/meter components\n    14→*   Gasket Specification: Full face 1/8\" thick red rubber\n    15→*   Pipe Material: Ductile Iron Class 53\n    16→*   Fasteners: 5/8\" diameter x 8\" long stainless steel wedge-all anchors\n    17→*   City of Austin Standard Number: 512-AW-02 (Adopted 03/10/2025)\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 3**: drawing — Plan view of the pipe system layout within the concrete vault. Use VISION to examine component placement, pipe routing, and minimum horizontal dimensional clearances.\n    22→*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n    23→*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n    24→*   **Block 6**: table — Vault Schedule. READ for exact inside vault dimensions and offset dimensions corresponding to the specific fire line meter size being installed.\n    25→*   **Block 7**: table — Fire Line Meter Material List. READ for specific component descriptions, sizes, material types, and approved City of Austin part designations (e.g., link-seal modular seals, dismantling joints).\n    26→*   **Block 4**: notes — General construction and installation notes. READ for material specifications on nuts/bolts, gaskets, bedding, encasement, and drainage slope requirements.\n    27→*   **Block 13**: text_block — \"Use of This Standard\". READ for stipulations regarding when a project-specific structural design is required versus when this standard can be directly applied.\n    28→*   **Blocks 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the main title (\"6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\"), standard identifier (512-AW-02), adoption date (03/10/2025), agency info (City of Austin Water), disclaimers, and the professional engineer's seal.\n    29→\n    30→---\n    31→\n    32→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    33→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"d362b12d-66a8-4cd2-a0fa-370c0f97ab2f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 25 — Construction Details 4\n\nStandard details, plan, and section views for fire line meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides City of Austin standard construction details for a 6\", 8\", or 10\" fire line meter vault installation for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a comprehensive plan layout, vertical cross-sections, a material schedule, and specifications for vault dimensions based on meter size.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   Applicable Meter Sizes: 6\", 8\", or 10\"\n*   Vault Dimensions (Inside): 8' x 12' (for 6\" meter), 10' x 12' (for 8\" meter), 10' x 15' (for 10\" meter)\n*   Access Hatch Size: 48\" x 72\"\n*   Minimum Clearances: 18\" clearance between vault wall and bypass piping/meter components\n*   Gasket Specification: Full face 1/8\" thick red rubber\n*   Pipe Material: Ductile Iron Class 53\n*   Fasteners: 5/8\" diameter x 8\" long stainless steel wedge-all anchors\n*   City of Austin Standard Number: 512-AW-02 (Adopted 03/10/2025)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 3**: drawing — Plan view of the pipe system layout within the concrete vault. Use VISION to examine component placement, pipe routing, and minimum horizontal dimensional clearances.\n*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n*   **Block 6**: table — Vault Schedule. READ for exact inside vault dimensions and offset dimensions corresponding to the specific fire line meter size being installed.\n*   **Block 7**: table — Fire Line Meter Material List. READ for specific component descriptions, sizes, material types, and approved City of Austin part designations (e.g., link-seal modular seals, dismantling joints).\n*   **Block 4**: notes — General construction and installation notes. READ for material specifications on nuts/bolts, gaskets, bedding, encasement, and drainage slope requirements.\n*   **Block 13**: text_block — \"Use of This Standard\". READ for stipulations regarding when a project-specific structural design is required versus when this standard can be directly applied.\n*   **Blocks 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the main title (\"6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\"), standard identifier (512-AW-02), adoption date (03/10/2025), agency info (City of Austin Water), disclaimers, and the professional engineer's seal.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187656226,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D97zJMnDs9GQa5LAgCNrjN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 26 — Construction Details 5\n     2→\n     3→Standard details for wastewater service connections and sewer cleanouts.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides standard construction details and specifications for wastewater infrastructure for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily features City of Austin standard diagrams and notes covering single and double wastewater service connections, cleanout installations, concrete encasements, and procedures for tapping into existing lined pipes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Minimum Pipe Slope:** 1% (for service connections and cleanouts)\n    11→*   **Maximum Pipe Deflection/Slope:** 45° max (exceeding 45° requires deep service rules)\n    12→*   **Service Depth at Property Line:** 4' minimum, 6' maximum\n    13→*   **Minimum Cover Below Final Street Grade:** 42\"\n    14→*   **Pipe to Manhole Connector Limit:** Limits pipe slope into manhole to 12% max\n    15→*   **Sewer Cleanout Clearance:** Must be located a minimum of 6\" from all paved areas (sidewalks, driveways, parking lots)\n    16→*   **Cleanout Concrete Collar:** 6\" thickness\n    17→*   **Concrete Encasement for Slip-on Joints:** Minimum of 4\" on all sides (vertical rising section)\n    18→*   **Host Pipe Opening for Lined Pipe:** At least 2\" but no more than 3\" wider than the service adaptor diameter\n    19→*   **Core Hole Distance (Lined Pipe):** Edge must be at least 3' from the ends of the pipe, other connections, or fittings\n    20→*   **Encasement Sleeves:** 8\" PVC sleeve (if no pipe bells in riser); 10\" PVC sleeve (if pipe bells in riser)\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 7: notes — Subdivision Construction Requirements**\n    25→    READ the block content for critical specifications regarding wastewater tee connections, elastomeric gasket joints, grading/slopes (1% min to 45° max), bedding requirements (City of Austin Spec 510.3), and depth rules.\n    26→*   **Block 4: diagram & notes — Installation in Lined Pipe**\n    27→    READ for the 6-step installation procedure and 5 restricting notes (including the 12% max slope to manhole and 3' clearance rule). Use VISION to examine the host pipe, liner, and service adaptor configuration details (\"Detail A\" and \"Detail B\").\n    28→*   **Block 3: diagram — Single and Double Wastewater Service Connection**\n    29→    Use VISION to examine the plan and profile views, noting the 1% minimum slope, component layout at the property line/R.O.W., and placement of the 6\" two-way cleanouts.\n    30→*   **Block 6: diagram — Concrete Encasement for Service Connection**\n    31→    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout for pavement/curb and gutter sections versus deep service connections. READ to verify PVC sleeve sizing criteria (8\" or 10\") and Class A concrete specifications.\n    32→*   **Block 2: diagram — Typical Sewer Cleanout (Private Side)**\n    33→    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the main line, 45° Wye, cleanout riser, and 6\" concrete collar. READ the specific note regarding solvent-welded slip-on joints requiring 4\" concrete encasement.\n    34→*   **Block 1: diagram — Replacement for Existing Mains**\n    35→    Use VISION to examine the acceptable repair couplings and transition couplings for connecting SDR 26 PVC to existing PVC, concrete, clay, and AC mains.\n    36→*   **Block 5: diagram — Wastewater Cleanout Frame and Lid**\n    37→    Use VISION to understand the vertical arrangement of the PVC pipe, 6\"x6\" adapter, and the frame/lid in compacted natural ground.\n    38→*   **Block 10: notes — Cleanout Paving Restriction**\n    39→    READ for the specific rule prohibiting cleanout frames/lids in paved areas and the 6\" minimum distance requirement.\n    40→*   **Blocks 8, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18: tables — City of Austin Approval Blocks**\n    41→    READ to identify the specific City of Austin standard numbers applied here (520-AW-01C Sheets 1-4, and 520-AW-03).\n    42→*   **Blocks 9, 11, 12, 13, 19: various — Title, Administrative & Boilerplate**\n    43→    Contains the sheet title (\"Construction Details 5\"), project name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), sheet index (26 of 39), file paths, and the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers). No deep review required.\n    44→\n    45→---\n    46→\n    47→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    48→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"147c1814-1dab-4122-8a6c-7cd1a7f5272d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-26/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 26 — Construction Details 5\n\nStandard details for wastewater service connections and sewer cleanouts.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides standard construction details and specifications for wastewater infrastructure for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily features City of Austin standard diagrams and notes covering single and double wastewater service connections, cleanout installations, concrete encasements, and procedures for tapping into existing lined pipes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Minimum Pipe Slope:** 1% (for service connections and cleanouts)\n*   **Maximum Pipe Deflection/Slope:** 45° max (exceeding 45° requires deep service rules)\n*   **Service Depth at Property Line:** 4' minimum, 6' maximum\n*   **Minimum Cover Below Final Street Grade:** 42\"\n*   **Pipe to Manhole Connector Limit:** Limits pipe slope into manhole to 12% max\n*   **Sewer Cleanout Clearance:** Must be located a minimum of 6\" from all paved areas (sidewalks, driveways, parking lots)\n*   **Cleanout Concrete Collar:** 6\" thickness\n*   **Concrete Encasement for Slip-on Joints:** Minimum of 4\" on all sides (vertical rising section)\n*   **Host Pipe Opening for Lined Pipe:** At least 2\" but no more than 3\" wider than the service adaptor diameter\n*   **Core Hole Distance (Lined Pipe):** Edge must be at least 3' from the ends of the pipe, other connections, or fittings\n*   **Encasement Sleeves:** 8\" PVC sleeve (if no pipe bells in riser); 10\" PVC sleeve (if pipe bells in riser)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Subdivision Construction Requirements**\n    READ the block content for critical specifications regarding wastewater tee connections, elastomeric gasket joints, grading/slopes (1% min to 45° max), bedding requirements (City of Austin Spec 510.3), and depth rules.\n*   **Block 4: diagram & notes — Installation in Lined Pipe**\n    READ for the 6-step installation procedure and 5 restricting notes (including the 12% max slope to manhole and 3' clearance rule). Use VISION to examine the host pipe, liner, and service adaptor configuration details (\"Detail A\" and \"Detail B\").\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Single and Double Wastewater Service Connection**\n    Use VISION to examine the plan and profile views, noting the 1% minimum slope, component layout at the property line/R.O.W., and placement of the 6\" two-way cleanouts.\n*   **Block 6: diagram — Concrete Encasement for Service Connection**\n    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout for pavement/curb and gutter sections versus deep service connections. READ to verify PVC sleeve sizing criteria (8\" or 10\") and Class A concrete specifications.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Typical Sewer Cleanout (Private Side)**\n    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the main line, 45° Wye, cleanout riser, and 6\" concrete collar. READ the specific note regarding solvent-welded slip-on joints requiring 4\" concrete encasement.\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Replacement for Existing Mains**\n    Use VISION to examine the acceptable repair couplings and transition couplings for connecting SDR 26 PVC to existing PVC, concrete, clay, and AC mains.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Wastewater Cleanout Frame and Lid**\n    Use VISION to understand the vertical arrangement of the PVC pipe, 6\"x6\" adapter, and the frame/lid in compacted natural ground.\n*   **Block 10: notes — Cleanout Paving Restriction**\n    READ for the specific rule prohibiting cleanout frames/lids in paved areas and the 6\" minimum distance requirement.\n*   **Blocks 8, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18: tables — City of Austin Approval Blocks**\n    READ to identify the specific City of Austin standard numbers applied here (520-AW-01C Sheets 1-4, and 520-AW-03).\n*   **Blocks 9, 11, 12, 13, 19: various — Title, Administrative & Boilerplate**\n    Contains the sheet title (\"Construction Details 5\"), project name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), sheet index (26 of 39), file paths, and the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers). No deep review required.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}}}
