{"level":30,"time":1778187659134,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) to identify: 1) Are overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on this landscape plan? If yes, where are they located and what is their routing across the site? 2) Where are the proposed trees located on this plan? Identify any tree symbols and their proximity to the overhead electric lines. 3) Are there any clearance dimensions or notes referencing tree distances from utilities? 4) What utility lines are shown on this plan (water, storm drain, overhead electric)? Please provide specific spatial observations.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided document, here are the detailed observations responding to your queries.\n\n*Note: The prompt requests an examination of \"Sheet 31\", but the provided image is clearly labeled in the bottom right corner as \"Sheet No. 28 of 35\". The analysis below is based on the provided Sheet 28.*\n\n**1) Are overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on this landscape plan? If yes, where are they located and what is their routing across the site?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are shown on this plan. They are identified by a solid linetype with the text \"-OHE-\" embedded within it.\n*   **Location and Routing:** The \"-OHE-\" line runs horizontally along the lower (southern) edge of the property boundary. It traverses almost the entire width of the site from the left side (near the street labeled \"Valley View Road\") to the right side, running roughly parallel to the property line.\n\n**2) Where are the proposed trees located on this plan? Identify any tree symbols and their proximity to the overhead electric lines.**\nProposed trees are indicated by circular symbols of varying sizes, often with a cross or a dot in the center, and are scattered throughout the site. Major groupings include:\n*   Along the western edge (left side) adjacent to \"Valley View Road\", designated within areas marked \"H-2\" (STREET YARD).\n*   Along the northern edge (top side) of the property.\n*   Within the central island areas near the parking spaces.\n*   Along the southern edge (bottom side) of the property.\n*   **Proximity to OHE:** Several tree symbols are located directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the overhead electric lines. Specifically, along the bottom edge of the plan, the \"-OHE-\" line passes directly through the circular canopies of at least five separate trees. Labels near these specific trees include \"M\" (which the notes define as \"MITIGATION TREE\") and pointing to an area marked \"H-7\" (SOD).\n\n**3) Are there any clearance dimensions or notes referencing tree distances from utilities?**\nNo. A thorough review of the plan reveals no dimension lines indicating required clearances between proposed trees and the utility lines. Furthermore, a review of the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\" sections yields no text referencing tree distances, setbacks, or required clearances from utilities.\n\n**4) What utility lines are shown on this plan (water, storm drain, overhead electric)? Please provide specific spatial observations.**\nThe following utility and reference lines are visible on this plan:\n*   **Overhead Electric (\"-OHE-\"):** As noted above, this line runs continuously along the bottom (southern) boundary of the site.\n*   **Water (\"-W-\"):** A line labeled \"-W-\" runs horizontally through the central drive aisle of the townhome complex, traversing from the left edge of the site towards the right.\n*   **Storm Drain (\"-SD-\"):** A line labeled \"-SD-\" runs parallel to the water line, also horizontally through the central drive aisle. Additionally, there are specific stormwater management features labeled \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" located in the upper right quadrant of the site.\n*   **Limits of Construction (\"-LOC-\"):** While not a utility line, it is a heavily marked boundary line running around the perimeter of the primary work area.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1425,"outputTokens":721,"totalTokens":3860,"reasoningTokens":1714},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) to identify: 1) Are overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on this landscape plan? If yes, where are they located and what is their routing across the site? 2) Where are the proposed trees located on this plan? Identify