{"level":30,"time":1778187663314,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and identify:\n1. Are existing overhead electric poles or lines shown on this sheet?\n2. If so, where are they located on the property?\n3. Are any poles marked with specific symbols or labels?\n4. Are there any notations about electric easements or utility rights-of-way?\n5. How does the location of any overhead electric infrastructure relate to the existing structures and property boundaries?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the existing overhead electric facilities shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of \"Sheet 4 of 39 - Existing Conditions Survey,\" here are the observations regarding the existing overhead electric facilities:\n\n**1. Are existing overhead electric poles or lines shown on this sheet?**\nYes, existing overhead electric lines and power poles are clearly identified on this survey sheet.\n\n**2. If so, where are they located on the property?**\nBased on the North arrow (which points to the left side of the sheet), the overhead electric infrastructure is located in three primary areas:\n*   **Western Boundary (Bottom of image):** Running parallel to \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD.\"\n*   **Eastern Boundary (Top of image):** Running roughly parallel to the eastern property line (bearing S63°03'28\"E).\n*   **Interior Service Drop:** An overhead line crosses into the interior of the property from the eastern boundary to connect to the main structure.\n\n**3. Are any poles marked with specific symbols or labels?**\n*   **Poles:** The poles are marked with a specific symbol (a circle with a crosshair/X inside), which is defined in the LEGEND (top left) as \"POWER POLE.\"\n*   **Lines:** The overhead electric lines are depicted as dashed lines interspersed with the text \"**O.H.E.**\", which is defined in the LEGEND as \"O.H.E. - OVERHEAD ELECTRIC\".\n*   **Guy Wires:** At least one pole (located near the northeast corner, top left area of the plan) shows an attached guy wire, indicated by a line ending in an anchor symbol, which matches the \"GUY WIRE\" symbol in the LEGEND.\n\n**4. Are there any notations about electric easements or utility rights-of-way?**\nYes, there are specific notations regarding electric easements near the property boundaries:\n*   Along the eastern boundary (top edge of the image), there is a notation indicating a \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX**\".\n*   Along the southern boundary (right edge of the image), there is another notation for a \"**5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX**\".\n\n**5. How does the location of any overhead electric infrastructure relate to the existing structures and property boundaries?**\n*   The main distribution lines run along the perimeters of the property (the street frontage on the west and the rear property line on the east), largely staying within or near the designated easements/rights-of-way.\n*   There is a direct relationship between the eastern perimeter line and the existing main structure (labeled \"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"). An individual \"**O.H.E.**\" service drop line branches off off a power pole located on the eastern boundary and runs westward, crossing the property to physically connect to the eastern side of the existing main building.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1418,"outputTokens":637,"totalTokens":5133,"reasoningTokens":3078},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and identify:\n1. Are existing overhead electric poles or lines shown on this sheet?\n2. If so, where are they located on the property?\n3. Are any poles marked with specific symbols or labels?\n4. Are there any notations about electric easements or utility rights-of-way?\n5. How does the location of any overhead electric infrastructure relate to the existing structures and property boundaries?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the existing overhead electric facilities shown."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"790d4c46-cd86-49b4-a255-a4397ca7ac09","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_BASELINE_V3","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-5KuDd4mFNZlEMXw0ybGjGXpw","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-ga