{"level":30,"time":1778187723536,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":19,"prompt":"Examine the utility tap plan and identify the routing of all underground utilities: 1) Water line locations and routing from property boundary to each building, 2) Wastewater line locations and routing, 3) Storm drain routing, 4) Any utility crossings or close passes near transformer pad locations visible on Sheet 21. For each utility type, note if you can identify minimum horizontal or vertical clearances shown. List any separations or distances labeled between utilities and other site features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided image of the \"Utility Tap Plan\" (Sheet 19 of 39), here is a detailed analysis of the underground utility routing and requested information.\n\n### 1) Water Line Locations and Routing\n*   **Legend Identification:** The legend denotes `--- W ---` as \"Proposed Water Line\" (shown in blue on the plan).\n*   **Routing:** \n    *   The proposed water line taps into an \"Existing 8\" Water Line\" at the southwest corner of the property boundary. \n    *   A label at the tap points reads: \"Install 8\" Gate Valve on Existing 8\" Water Line\" and \"Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant\".\n    *   The 8\" main runs east across the southern drive aisle. It branches north to loop around Building 8 and runs north between Buildings 7 and 8. The main line continues east and then north to serve Buildings 5 and 6.\n    *   Individual domestic branches route to each building unit. A typical callout points to the service lines for Building 1 stating: `2\" HDPE Service Tubing Per Detail 520-AW-01B (Typ)`. The legend indicates these are marked with an `S` (Single Water Service) or `D` (Double Water Service).\n\n### 2) Wastewater Line Locations and Routing\n*   **Legend Identification:** The legend denotes `--- WW ---` as \"Proposed Wastewater Line\" (shown in magenta on the plan).\n*   **Routing:**\n    *   The proposed wastewater line connects to the \"Existing #13466 Wastewater MH\" at the northwest corner of the property boundary.\n    *   From the manhole, the line runs south along the western drive aisle, passing a \"Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station\" (labeled near Building 2).\n    *   It then turns east, running along the southern drive aisle roughly parallel to the proposed water line. It branches north into the driveways between the buildings to provide service.\n    *   Service lines routing to individual units feature typical callouts such as: `6\" PVC Wastewater Service Line Minimum 1% Slope Per Detail 520-AW-01C (Typ)`.\n\n### 3) Storm Drain Routing\n*   **Legend Identification:** The legend denotes `--- SD ---` as \"Proposed Storm Drain\" (shown in green on the plan).\n*   **Routing:** \n    *   The storm drain system routes primarily along the western and southern boundaries of the site, collecting runoff from various square inlet structures placed within the drive aisles.\n\n### 4) Transformer Pad Locations and Sheet 21\n*   **Note:** The provided document is specifically labeled \"Sheet 19 of 39\". Sheet 21 is not included in this view.\n*   While the legend includes a symbol for a \"Transformer Pad\", there are no transformer pads or proposed underground electric lines (`--- E ---`) explicitly labeled or visibly crossing the main utilities on this specific sheet. \n\n### 5) Minimum Horizontal or Vertical Clearances\n*   There are **no explicit dimension lines** on this plan view calling out a specific minimum horizontal or vertical clearance distance (e.g., \"9 ft separation\") between the water and wastewater lines.\n*   Clearance verification is addressed purely through textual instruction in the **Utility Notes**:\n    *   *\"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"*\n\n### 6) Separations or Distances Labeled Between Utilities and Site Features\n*   The plan provides extensive labeling for pipe lengths, sizes, and slopes (e.g., `128.1 lf 8\" SDR 26 @ 2.00%`, `92.37 lf 8\" C-900`), but does not label explicit separation distances between parallel utility lines.\n*   A single `10'` separation dimension is labeled between the eastern property line boundary and the side of Building 6.\n\n***\n\n### Exact Transcriptions of Relevant Tables and Notes\n\nAs requested, here is the character-by-character transcription of the visible table and critical utility notes on this sheet:\n\n**Drainage Fixture Unit Table**\n```text\nBuilding # | Building Type | DFU's\n1 | 4 Plex | 136\n2 | 6 Plex | 204\n3 | 5 Plex | 170\n4 | 5 Plex | 170\n5 | 4 Plex | 136\n6 | 4 Plex | 136\n7 | 5 Plex | 170\n8 | 6 Plex | 204\n```\n\n**Utility Notes**\n```text\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n```\n\n**Water Tap Note**\n```text\nThe existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\n```","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1407,"outputTokens":1195,"totalTokens":6896,"reasoningTokens":4294},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - leng