 this view.\n*   While the legend includes a symbol for a \"Transformer Pad\", there are no transformer pads or proposed underground electric lines (`--- E ---`) explicitly labeled or visibly crossing the main utilities on this specific sheet. \n\n### 5) Minimum Horizontal or Vertical Clearances\n*   There are **no explicit dimension lines** on this plan view calling out a specific minimum horizontal or vertical clearance distance (e.g., \"9 ft separation\") between the water and wastewater lines.\n*   Clearance verification is addressed purely through textual instruction in the **Utility Notes**:\n    *   *\"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"*\n\n### 6) Separations or Distances Labeled Between Utilities and Site Features\n*   The plan provides extensive labeling for pipe lengths, sizes, and slopes (e.g., `128.1 lf 8\" SDR 26 @ 2.00%`, `92.37 lf 8\" C-900`), but does not label explicit separation distances between parallel utility lines.\n*   A single `10'` separation dimension is labeled between the eastern property line boundary and the side of Building 6.\n\n***\n\n### Exact Transcriptions of Relevant Tables and Notes\n\nAs requested, here is the character-by-character transcription of the visible table and critical utility notes on this sheet:\n\n**Drainage Fixture Unit Table**\n```text\nBuilding # | Building Type | DFU's\n1 | 4 Plex | 136\n2 | 6 Plex | 204\n3 | 5 Plex | 170\n4 | 5 Plex | 170\n5 | 4 Plex | 136\n6 | 4 Plex | 136\n7 | 5 Plex | 170\n8 | 6 Plex | 204\n```\n\n**Utility Notes**\n```text\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n```\n\n**Water Tap Note**\n```text\nThe existing AC pipe must be replaced with DI pipe and a Tee cut into the DI pipe. The AC pipe must be worked on by a certified company that is licensed to handle AC pipes and the pipe disposed of in a pre-approved landfill for Asbestos pipe. Dispose of AC pipe per STATE regulations.\n```","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":223699.043799,"endTime":285929.977445,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"jf38aZ_dHIitsbwP3t6kmQw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.068907","marketCost":"0.068907","inferenceCost":"0.068682","inputInferenceCost":"0.002814","outputInferenceCost":"0.065868","reportingTagWriteCost":"0.000225","generationId":"gen_01KR23WVXNFDB0MN1PZ13S2ADA"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
