{"level":30,"time":1778187727595,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the southern edge of the landscape plan where the overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") is shown. Identify: 1) How many tree symbols are visible in the vicinity of the \"-OHE-\" line? 2) What are the approximate distances between the overhead electric line and the nearest tree symbols? Can you estimate if trees are within 15 feet, 25 feet, or 50 feet of the line? 3) Are there any dimension lines or measurements shown that quantify the distances? 4) What tree symbols/markers are used (M for mitigation, P for parking buffer, SY for street yard, etc.)? 5) Are there any notes or annotations near these trees referencing utilities or clearances? Please provide as much specific spatial information as possible.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the specific spatial information regarding the southern edge near the overhead electric line:\n\n**1) How many tree symbols are visible in the vicinity of the \"-OHE-\" line?**\nAlong the southern property boundary where the line explicitly labeled \"-OHE-\" is drawn horizontally, there is a cluster of **four (4)** distinct circular tree canopy symbols located towards the eastern (right) half of that southern edge.\n\n**2) What are the approximate distances between the overhead electric line and the nearest tree symbols? Can you estimate if trees are within 15 feet, 25 feet, or 50 feet of the line?**\nUtilizing the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the trees are extremely close to the line.\n*   The center points (indicated by small '+' or 'x' marks) of at least two of the tree symbols appear to be situated directly on or within 5 feet of the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   The drawn canopies of three of the four trees directly overlap and intersect the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   Based on the scale, it can be estimated with high confidence that the trunks/centers of these nearest trees are located **well within 15 feet** of the overhead electric line.\n\n**3) Are there any dimension lines or measurements shown that quantify the distances?**\n**No.** There are no dimension lines, leader lines, or numerical measurements provided on the plan that explicitly quantify the distance between the \"-OHE-\" line and the adjacent trees.\n\n**4) What tree symbols/markers are used?**\nWithin the cluster of four trees near the southern \"-OHE-\" line:\n*   Two of the tree symbols contain the letter **\"M\"** inside the circle. According to the legend on the right side of the page, \"M\" designates a **\"MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n*   The other two tree symbols in this specific cluster do not contain internal letter markers.\n\n**5) Are there any notes or annotations near these trees referencing utilities or clearances?**\n**No.** There are no notes, callouts, or annotations in the immediate vicinity of these trees that reference utility clearances, conflict resolution, or pruning requirements for overhead lines. Furthermore, a review of the \"NOTES:\" and \"IRRIGATION NOTES:\" blocks at the top of the page reveals no general instructions regarding planting clearances near overhead electric utilities.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":521,"totalTokens":3904,"reasoningTokens":1911},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, cha