{"level":30,"time":1778187732790,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D9jbbrv2k6JRwmEyRFMic7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55ff8a59-232f-4f64-9fd7-19e407044c7f","uuid":"e30207c0-f20a-48ba-bbac-917175c2fba9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
