{"level":30,"time":1778187738255,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23Z1VHBGJZ34ZGMGZTXVH6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This confirms that the Electric Review section specifically references UCM § 1.10.3 - \"Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\" which is the primary code section for this grouping.\n\nThe review comments are on a Bluebeam link, which I cannot access. However, this confirms that Austin Energy has reviewed the project and there are specific requirements mentioned about clearances from overhead lines.\n\nNow I need to systematically evaluate each checklist item. Based on my research so far:\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n1. **Applicability**: YES - The site has existing overhead electric utilities on and adjacent to it\n2. **Existing Overhead Utilities Location**: \n   - Along Valley View Road (western boundary)\n   - Along southern boundary\n   - Multiple utility poles documented\n   - Electric easements identified\n3. **Proposed Infrastructure**: All proposed electric is UNDERGROUND - no proposed overhead facilities\n4. **Planning Status**: Site plan is in comment response stage; Austin Energy has reviewed preliminary design requirements\n\nNow I need to evaluate each checklist item to determine if clearances are properly documented. The critical issue is: Are there building elevation sheets or profile views showing clearances from the existing overhead utilities to the proposed buildings and features?\n\nFrom my review of the sheet list, I don't see dedicated \"Building Elevation\" sheets. The site plan sheets show buildings in plan view, but I haven't found elevation views showing the vertical relationship between buildings and overhead utilities.\n\nThis is a significant finding. Let me now systematically go through each checklist item and evaluate them based on:\n1. Whether the triggering condition exists\n2. Whether the required documentation is present\n\nLet me start evaluating the checklist items now.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55ff8a59-232f-4f64-9fd7-19e407044c7f","uuid":"16667b5c-f4eb-4511-9e86-a87803b77710"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187738267,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23YWSJQQGF7P4ETASQRX0N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EXCELLENT! This is CRITICAL. The vision analysis reveals:\n\n1. **4 trees visible** in vicinity of \"-OHE-\" line\n2. **Trees are EXTREMELY CLOSE** to the overhead electric line:\n   - At least 2 tree symbols have centers within 5 feet of the \"-OHE-\" line\n   - Tree canopies directly overlap/intersect the \"-OHE-\" line\n   - Tree trunks/centers are definitely well within 15 feet\n3. **NO DIMENSION LINES** showing clearances\n4. **2 trees marked \"M\" (MITIGATION TREES)**\n5. **NO NOTES OR ANNOTATIONS** referencing utility clearances\n\nThis is a MAJOR VIOLATION of multiple checklist items:\n\n- EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor\n- EL-2.3: Large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor\n- EL-2.13: Tree clearances measured from tree canopy instead of from tree trunk (the plan shows trees but doesn't identify the clearance measurement methodology)\n- EL-2.14: Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities (actually they ARE shown, but no clearance verification)\n- EL-2.15: Plans propose trees within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval\n\nAlso:\n- EL-2.10: Plant legend may not identify species of these specific trees\n- EL-2.11: Large trees may not be differentiated (the 16' HT specification doesn't tell us the mature height per ECM Appendix F, which would determine if they're large/40+ feet)\n- EL-2.12: No dimension lines showing how clearances were measured\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Identify what specific trees are being planted near the OHE\n\n\n2. Look up their UC status and mature heights\n3. Confirm they don't have Austin Energy approval\n\nThe plant schedule shows 10 Cedar Elm and 2 Live Oak as shade trees—both are non-utility-compatible and exceed 40 feet at maturity. Additionally, 6 Mexican Redbud and 2 Texas Mountain Laurel are proposed; the Mexican Redbud typically reaches 20-30 feet, while Texas Mountain Laurel is smaller still, so these wouldn't trigger the 40-foot threshold but still need clearance verification.\n\nThe main issues I'm seeing: Cedar Elm and Live Oak fail utility compatibility requirements near overhead lines, there are no clearance dimensions documented, Austin Energy approval is missing, the plant legend may not adequately identify species near utilities, and large trees aren't differentiated by mature height categories. I should look more closely at what's actually being planted in the southern area adjacent to the OHE.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49385103-a1b8-4868-b0ea-01fec564ebbd","uuid":"93c3f1a4-cba5-4543-9b45-78eac5b27014"}
