rectly adjacent to the main incoming fire lane, but it is not immediately adjacent to any parking stalls.\n\n**5. Any measurements or clearance dimensions shown**\nSeveral dimensions regarding drive aisle widths, clearances, and turning radii are explicitly shown:\n*   **Drive Aisle/Fire Lane Widths:** \n    *   **\"24'\"** is marked across the main entrance driveway on the west side.\n    *   **\"26'\"** is marked in multiple locations across the internal drive aisles (e.g., north of Bldg. 2, between Bldg. 2 and 8, south of Bldg. 3, and south of Bldg. 8).\n*   **Clearances/Setbacks:**\n    *   **\"27.3'\"** is marked on the east side, indicating the distance from the eastern edge of Bldg. 4 to the property boundary/easement line.\n    *   **\"25'\"** is marked just below that, indicating the distance from the eastern edge of Bldg. 6 to the property boundary/easement line.\n    *   **\"25' Building Setback\"** is written in the western area of the site near Bldg. 2.\n*   **Turning Radii:** Various corners along the fire lane loop indicate turning radii, including **\"R25\"**, **\"R40\"**, **\"R10\"**, and **\"R15\"**.\n*   **Signage Dimensions:** The detail box in the bottom left provides precise dimensions for the fire zone signs (e.g., 12\" x 18\" overall, with specific text height clearances like \"76.2 mm (3\")\", \"50.8 mm (2\")\", etc.).\n\n**6. Whether transformer pads are located near parking areas, fire lanes, or other site features**\nAs stated in point 3, **no transformer pads are explicitly labeled** on this plan. Therefore, an analysis of their location relative to parking areas and fire lanes cannot be performed based solely on the visual evidence provided in this specific document. If the \"Vault Easement\" at the front entrance serves a similar function, it is located immediately adjacent to the fire lane entrance but isolated from parking areas.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":141