{"level":30,"time":1778187746233,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23Z9A3MCBWB2J8Z7SD7N1S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I found the Electric Notes on Sheet 3, Block 19. These notes specifically address:\n\n1. Austin Energy's right to prune/remove trees and obstructions\n2. Owner must provide easements/access for electric facilities\n3. Owner responsible for tree pruning within 10 feet of centerline of proposed overhead electric facilities\n4. Owner responsible for maintaining NESC/OSHA clearances from overhead power lines - \"Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained\"\n5. Relocation costs are owner's responsibility\n\nThis is significant. The notes acknowledge that there ARE overhead electric facilities being designed for the project. But critically, I haven't found any evidence that:\n1. Surveyed elevations of existing overhead conductors are shown on building elevation sheets\n2. Mid-span clearance verification has been done\n3. Clearance dimensions are labeled on plans\n4. The site plan shows existing overhead poles and their clearances from proposed buildings\n5. A 48-hour notification requirement note is included per Texas Health & Safety Code\n\nThe Electric Notes in Block 19 also indicate that the owner must ensure clearances are maintained per NESC and OSHA. However, the site plans submitted don't appear to include sufficient documentation to verify these clearances have been met.\n\nLet me check if there's anything in the master comment report about electric/overhead utility issues.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"75e3c407-28ce-4b4f-9c64-f8c5f950c86a"}
