{"level":30,"time":1778187749378,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6c7fCpyZbQfnT2LAr5eMP","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"f5fa3a35-97b1-4b30-9830-2b6ef167eaaf","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778187756066,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23ZCJGZV6T8HHT6AN41XBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is helpful. The fire protection plan shows:\n- Fire lanes\n- One existing fire hydrant (off-site on Valley View Road)\n- Two proposed fire hydrants (one near entrance, one south of Bldg. 7) - the notes mention \"includes 1 private hydrants\" which suggests only one is private\n- A \"Vault Easement\" near the entrance with an \"E\" symbol (likely electrical)\n- 5' electrical easements on the eastern property line\n- No explicit \"Transformer Pad\" labels on this sheet\n\nBut the electrical plan (Sheet 21) showed 4 transformer pads. The issue is that the fire protection plan doesn't show transformer pads labeled, and the site plan (Sheet 9) only showed one transformer pad labeled \"(Typ.)\".\n\nNow let me compile my research findings. Based on my investigation:\n\n## Research Summary:\n\n**Found Evidence:**\n1. **Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan)**: Shows 4 transformer pads with locations:\n   - Pad 1: West/Entrance (near property line, sidewalk easement)\n   - Pad 2: Mid-West (between Bldg. 2 and 8, with \"Vault Easement\" noted)\n   - Pad 3: Mid-East (bounded by Bldgs 4, 5, 6)\n   - Pad 4: South-Central (between Bldgs 7 and 8, **very close to southern property line with wood fence**)\n\n2. **Sheet 9 (Site Plan)**: Shows only one transformer pad labeled \"(Typ.)\" near western property line, west of Bldg. 1, south of main entrance drive\n\n3. **No specific transformer pad detail sheets** found in the construction details (Sheets 22-28 show curbs, sidewalks, water, fire, wastewater details, but no transformer pad details)\n\n4. **Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10)**: Shows \"Vault Easement\" near entrance but does not explicitly label transformer pads\n   \nThe plans are missing critical specifications—no dimensions, clearances, access door orientations, or drainage patterns are documented for any of the four pads. Pad 4's proximity to the property line and fence raises a potential clearance concern. Additionally, there's no documentation showing whether the pads fall within easements, no bollard details provided, and no transformer easement boundaries delineated. The architectural design doesn't include transformer pad details either.\n\nI can't verify pad dimensions, clearance distances to buildings or structures, access door orientations for maintenance, whether confined spaces exist near the pads, AE Design-approved details, equipment type (oil-filled or dry), easement locations, drainage slopes at pad locations, tree root barriers, service configurations, electrical routing to confirm private property use, or vertical clearances shown in cross-sections.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c61cd73-4ad7-4ea5-8322-a86050b264be","uuid":"02b0a3b3-ec8e-4940-afff-b82f3da7ae77"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187757220,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the southern boundary of the site (bottom edge of the landscape plan). Describe in detail: 1) The exact path/routing of the OHE (overhead electric) line as it runs along this boundary. 2) Each individual tree symbol shown on or near the OHE line - how many trees and what letters/symbols mark them? 3) The specific distances or gaps between trees and the OHE line. 4) Any dimensions or annotations showing clearances. 5) The relationship between the trees and Valley View Road at the southern boundary.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the detailed observations regarding the southern boundary (bottom edge) of the site:\n\n**1) The exact path/routing of the OHE (overhead electric) line:**\nA line designated with the text \"- OHE -\" runs horizontally along the southern boundary of the site plan. It begins near the southwest corner of the property (just east of the western boundary line bordering Valley View Road) and runs in a straight, continuous line eastward, parallel to the southern property line. It continues until it reaches the eastern boundary of the site at the southeast corner.\n\n**2) Individual tree symbols on or near the OHE line:**\nThere is a distinct row of six plotted tree canopy symbols positioned directly along the path of the \"- OHE -\" line on the southern boundary.\n*   Moving from West (left) to East (right) along this line, there are six individual tree symbols drawn as large circles with a \"+\" mark in the center indicating the trunk location.\n*   Five of these six trees clearly contain the letter \"M\" placed within the lower right quadrant of the circle. According to the \"KEY NOTES,\" \"M\" indicates a \"MITIGATION TREE\".\n*   The sixth tree, located at the far eastern end of this row (southeast corner), also contains the letter \"M\". Immediately adjacent and slightly north of this tree is another tree symbol containing the letter \"P\" (indicated in the key as \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\").\n*   Note: There is an additional tree symbol located at the far southwest corner, west of where the OHE line begins, which is a circle with a central dot and resides in a grey shaded area, but the OHE line does not pass through it.\n\n**3) Specific distances or gaps between trees and the OHE line:**\nThere are **no** specific distances or gaps indicated between the trees and the OHE line on this plan. The drafting of the plan shows the \"- OHE -\" line passing directly through the canopy circles of all six \"M\" designated trees. In several instances, the OHE line appears to pass directly over or within a very close margin of the center \"+\" mark (the trunk location) of the trees. The plan graphically depicts a direct conflict or intersection between the overhead line and the tree locations rather than a gap.\n\n**4) Dimensions or annotations showing clearances:**\nThere are **no** dimensions, annotations, callouts, or text notes anywhere along the southern boundary that indicate horizontal or vertical clearance requirements between the planted mitigation trees (\"M\") and the overhead electric line (\"- OHE -\").\n\n**5) Relationship between the trees and Valley View Road at the southern boundary:**\nThe text \"Valley View Road\" is located along the far left (western) edge of the site plan, indicating the road runs North-South. The southern boundary meets Valley View Road at the site's southwest corner. The row of \"M\" designated trees situated under the \"- OHE -\" line begins near this southwest corner and runs eastward along the southern property line, moving away from Valley View Road in a perpendicular orientation to the street.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"sto