t.\n\n**3) Specific distances or gaps between trees and the OHE line:**\nThere are **no** specific distances or gaps indicated between the trees and the OHE line on this plan. The drafting of the plan shows the \"- OHE -\" line passing directly through the canopy circles of all six \"M\" designated trees. In several instances, the OHE line appears to pass directly over or within a very close margin of the center \"+\" mark (the trunk location) of the trees. The plan graphically depicts a direct conflict or intersection between the overhead line and the tree locations rather than a gap.\n\n**4) Dimensions or annotations showing clearances:**\nThere are **no** dimensions, annotations, callouts, or text notes anywhere along the southern boundary that indicate horizontal or vertical clearance requirements between the planted mitigation trees (\"M\") and the overhead electric line (\"- OHE -\").\n\n**5) Relationship between the trees and Valley View Road at the southern boundary:**\nThe text \"Valley View Road\" is located along the far left (western) edge of the site plan, indicating the road runs North-South. The southern boundary meets Valley View Road at the site's southwest corner. The row of \"M\" designated trees situated under the \"- OHE -\" line begins near this southwest corner and runs eastward along the southern property line, moving away from Valley View Road in a perpendicular orientation to the street."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"7435780d-eacf-4f74-aa80-2c517825f44d","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the detailed observations regarding the southern boundary (bottom edge) of the site:\n\n**1) The exact path/routing of the OHE (overhead electric) line:**\nA line designated with the text \"- OHE -\" runs horizontally along the southern boundary of the site plan. It begins near the southwest corner of the property (just e