{"level":30,"time":1778187758439,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23Z76Q0PGZV3YYM80XR2G8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sheet 37 contains tree planting details but they appear to be standard City of Austin tree protection and planting details. There's no mention of utility clearances or overhead electric line coordination. This is another problem - there are no details specific to tree planting near overhead electric lines.\n\nNow let me compile my findings:\n\n**APPLICABILITY**: \nThe project has:\n1. EXISTING overhead electric lines on/near the property (shown on both electrical plan and landscape plan)\n2. PROPOSED new trees being planted near these overhead electric lines\n3. NO documentation of Austin Energy approval for trees in proximity to utilities\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM MY RESEARCH**:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present**: The electrical plan (Sheet 21) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) both show existing overhead electric lines (\"-OHE-\") along the western and southern boundaries of the property.\n\n2. **Trees Proposed Near OHE**: The landscape plan shows trees planted directly adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line on the southern boundary, with at least 4 trees within a few feet of the overhead line.\n\n3. **Species Identification Issues**: \n   - Proposed trees include Cedar Elm (non-UC, mature height 40+ ft) and Live Oak (non-UC, mature height 40+ ft)\n   - These are being planted near the OHE\n   - Plant schedule lists \"16' HT minimum\" which is planting height, NOT mature height per ECM Appendix F\n   - Trees are NOT differentiated on the landscape plan by mature height class\n\n4. **No Clearance Documentation**:\n   - NO dimension lines showing clearances from trees to overhead conductors\n   - NO reference to conductor locations (only pole locations implied)\n   - NO measurements from tree trunk centers to outer conductors\n   - NO measurements indicating measurement methodology\n\n5. **No Austin Energy Approval**:\n   - No evidence of written Austin Energy approval for trees within restricted zones\n   - Austin Energy review specifically flagged \"Landscaping & Trees\" (UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4) as a requirement\n   - The submitted documents lack any Bluebeam markups or coordination notes that would indicate utility review.\n\nNow evaluating the checklist items:\n\n**EL-2.1**: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 lateral feet of distribution conductor\n- APPLICABILITY: YES - overhead distribution lines are present\n- STATUS: FAIL - Cedar Elm and Live Oak (non-UC) are being planted within visible distance of OHE\n\n**EL-2.2**: Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductor  \n- APPLICABILITY: UNCLEAR - need to determine if lines are distribution or transmission\n- The grouping suggests typical overhead lines are distribution unless labeled transmission. These appear to be distribution (not labeled as transmission, typical residential area)\n- STATUS: LIKELY N/A (if distribution), but FAIL if transmission\n\n**EL-2.3**: Large trees (40+ ft per ECM App F) within 25 lateral feet of distribution conductor\n- APPLICABILITY: YES - Cedar Elm and Live Oak are both 40+ ft at mature height\n- STATUS: FAIL - these large trees are being planted within very close proximity (within 5 feet based on vision analysis) of OHE\n\n**EL-2.4**: Large trees (40+ ft per ECM App F) within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductor\n- APPLICABILITY: UNCERTAIN (depends on transmission vs distribution)\n- STATUS: FAIL if applicable (same trees violate this zone)\n\n**EL-2.5**: Trees in transmission easement\n- APPLICABILITY: UNKNOWN - not seeing transmission easement designation, only drainage/wastewater easements\n- STATUS: N/A (unless transmission easement is present)\n\n**EL-2.6**: Trees within 10 lateral feet of utility pole\n- APPLICABILITY: POSSIBLE - poles supporting OHE may be near trees\n- STATUS: Cannot verify exact pole locations and distances from available documentation\n\n**EL-2.7**: Trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment\n- APPLICABILITY: POSSIBLE - electrical transformers (pad-mounted) are shown on Sheet 21\n- STATUS: Cannot verify exact distances from trees to transformers\n\n**EL-2.8**: Trees within 5 lateral feet of underground equipment\n- APPLICABILITY: POSSIBLE - underground electrical conduits and pull boxes shown on Sheet 21\n- STATUS: Cannot verify exact distances from trees to underground equipment\n\n**EL-2.9**: Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground equipment lack root barriers\n- APPLICABILITY: POSSIBLE - trees might be within 20 ft of underground equipment\n- STATUS: Root barriers not shown on plans if applicable\n\n**EL-2.10**: Plant legend doesn't identify species near utilities\n- APPLICABILITY: YES - trees are proposed near utilities\n- STATUS: Depends on interpretation—plant schedule can be cross-referenced to identify species, but species aren't directly labeled at tree locations on the landscape plan\n\n**EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans\n- APPLICABILITY: YES - large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) are proposed\n- STATUS: Trees are shown on landscape plan but lack specific marking or differentiation to distinguish larger specimens from smaller ones. The plant schedule notes \"16' HT minimum\" for planting height, which doesn't convey mature height expectations per ECM Appendix F. This is a FAIL—large trees (40+ ft mature) aren't visually distinguished from smaller trees on the landscape plan.\n\n**EL-2.12**: Tree clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor\n- APPLICABILITY: YES - IF clearances are dimensioned on plans\n- STATUS: No clearance dimensions appear on the landscape plan, so measurement methodology cannot be verified.\n\n**EL-2.13**: Tree clearances measured from canopy edge instead of trunk\n- APPLICABILITY: YES -