n6. **No tree species documentation relative to overhead utilities:**\n   - Plant list on Sheet 35 includes Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel but does NOT indicate which are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n   - Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees near the southern boundary overhead electric line without species restrictions or clearance notations\n\n7. **No 48-hour notification requirement note** visible on cover sheet or general notes per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003\n\n8. **No Austin Energy coordination survey** or proximity analysis showing clearances from buildings/features to existing overhead poles/conductors\n\n9. **Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design) shows PROPOSED underground electrical infrastructure** but does NOT address existing overhead facilities or clearances from them\n\nThe Electric Notes on Sheet 3, Block 19 acknowledge that Austin Energy has requirements and that the owner must maintain clearances per UCM standards, yet the design documents lack the necessary clearance verification and coordination details to demonstrate compliance.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"e37e17ff-9ebf-4f59-9505-eb04e2cb6a1f"}
