ication at tree planting locations near utilities\n- Clearance measurements from trunk center to outer conductor (only tree canopy symbols visible)\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49385103-a1b8-4868-b0ea-01fec564ebbd","uuid":"d6121212-4a9e-4594-85b6-acdb6c4c27de"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187761506,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23ZJ25B33PN92HS436T9F0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the project and the available documentation. Let me systematically evaluate each checklist item based on my findings:\n\n## Research Summary - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n\n**Existing Overhead Infrastructure (from Sheet 4):**\n- Overhead utility poles and lines exist around property boundaries (shown on existing conditions survey)\n- OHE line visible on southern boundary per Sheet 9 vision analysis\n\n**Missing Documentation:**\n1. NO surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on any sheets (no building elevation sheets exist)\n2. NO profile/section exhibits showing vertical clearances from conductors to buildings, parking, or other site features\n3. NO dimension annotations on plans showing specific clearance measurements from conductors\n4. NO registered surveyor mid-span clearance data\n5. Incomplete/inconsistent depiction of existing overhead poles on proposed site plans compared to existing survey\n6. NO notes specifying tree species utility compatibility relative to overhead lines\n7. NO 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement note on plans\n8. NO Austin Energy coordination survey showing clearances\n\nThe Electric Notes on Sheet 3, Block 19 acknowledge Austin Energy clearance requirements but submitted plans lack adequate documentation.\n\n---\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"f0a8d30e-6be9-498d-b467-b8719d860ce6"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187765225,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Looking at Sheet 9 (Site Plan), I need to identify:\n1. Does the overhead electric line (if shown) cross over any driveways, parking areas, or access roads?\n2. Are there any driveway or parking clearances labeled regarding overhead lines?\n3. What is the relationship between the buildings and any shown utility lines?\n4. Are there any section/elevation callouts that reference detailed views showing clearances?\n5. Are there any notes about utility clearances or overhead line restrictions?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the relationship between the site features (buildings, driveways, parking) and any overhead electric infrastructure shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan), here are the findings regarding the overhead electric lines and their relationship to site features:\n\n**1. Does the overhead electric line (if shown) cross over any driveways, parking areas, or access roads?**\n*   **Yes.** There is a utility line explicitly labeled **\"--- OHE ---\"** (Overhead Electric) running horizontally along the southern property boundary (bottom edge of the drawing), connecting between utility poles labeled \"Pole\".\n*   This \"--- OHE ---\" line **crosses directly over the main driveway entrance** located near the bottom-left (southwest) portion of the site. This driveway is annotated with a callout that reads:\n    *   \"Construct Type II\"\n    *   \"Driveway\"\n    *   \"See Detail 133S-2\" *(Note: The first digit is slightly blurry, it could potentially be 433S-2, similar to the driveway callout on the west edge)*.\n*   The line does not appear to cross over the designated parking spaces themselves, running parallel and just south of the parking area located below Building 7 and Building 8.\n\n**2. Are there any driveway or parking clearances labeled regarding overhead lines?**\n*   **No.** There are no vertical clearance heights (e.g., \"18' min clearance\") or specific warning labels regarding overhead line clearances at the location where the OHE line crosses the driveway, nor anywhere else along the visible OHE route.\n\n**3. What is the relationship between the buildings and any shown utility lines?**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** The visible \"--- OHE ---\" line runs along the southern perimeter of the site and **does not cross over any of the buildings**. The closest buildings to this overhead line are Bldg. 7 and Bldg. 8, which are set back to the north, separated from the line by a driveway aisle and parking spaces.\n*   **Underground Utilities:** Various underground utility lines (labeled \"--- W ---\" for water, \"--- S ---\" for sewer, and \"--- SD ---\" for storm drain) route through the center drive aisles and between the buildings (e.g., between Buildings 1, 2, 8 on the west and Buildings 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 on the east), branching off into the individual structures. There are also utility easements noted on the eastern boundary (e.g., \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" and \"10' Electric Easement\"), but no overhead lines are drawn within them on this sheet.\n\n**4. Are there any section/elevation callouts that reference detailed views showing clearances?**\n*   **No specific clearance callouts.** While there are detail callouts for the driveway construction itself (e.g., \"See Detail 133S-2\" and \"See Detail 433S-2\") and sidewalks (e.g., \"See Dtl 432S-1\"), there are no visible callouts, section marks, or elevation references that specifically indicate they provide detailed views of utility clearances.\n\n**5. Are there any notes about utility clearances or overhead line restrictions?**\n*   **None found.** I have thoroughly reviewed the text blocks on the page, including:\n    *   **\"Site Plan Release Notes\"**\n    *   **\"Accessibility Notes\"**\n    *   **\"Lighting Note\"**\n    *   **\"Trash Collection Notes\"**\n*   None of these note sections contain text regarding overhead electric line restrictions or required minimum utility clearances. The only general utility note is located next to the **Texas 811** logo, which states: *\"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed...\"*, but it does not detail clearance requirements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1441,"outputTokens":820,"totalTokens":4765,"reasoningTokens":2504},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Looking at Sheet 9 (Site Plan), I need to identify:\n1. Does the overhead electric line (if shown) cross over any driveways, parking areas, or access roads?\n2. Are there any driveway or parking clearances labeled regarding overhead lines?\n3. What is the relationship between the buildings and any shown utility lines?\n4. Are there any section/elevation callouts that reference detailed views showing clearances?\n5. Are there any notes about utility clearances or overhead line restrictions?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the relationship between the site features (buildings, driveways, parking) and any overhead electric infrastructure shown."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"790d4c46-cd86-49b4-a255-a4397ca7ac09","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_BASELINE_V3","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-1pqsrfQV8EWjJ96TZydenN9r","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:02:45 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::8vn66-