{"level":30,"time":1778187772552,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23ZSQ4WFX862QGX11Q775C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have very clear evidence:\n\n**Critical findings from the detailed vision analysis:**\n1. Six mitigation trees (\"M\" designation) are shown directly on the OHE line along the southern boundary\n2. The OHE line appears to pass directly through the canopy circles and even over the trunk locations\n3. There are NO dimensions or clearance annotations shown\n4. This clearly violates clearance requirements - trees cannot be directly on the overhead electric line\n\nThis is a CLEAR FAIL for multiple checklist items.\n\nNow let me finalize my evaluation of each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution conductor**\n- The OHE line shown is an existing distribution line (based on standard Austin utility infrastructure and the voltage not being specified as transmission)\n- Trees are shown directly on the line (much closer than 15 ft)\n- However, the plant schedule does not document which species are utility-compatible and which are not\n- Live Oak and Cedar Elm are both known to be UC\n- Without documented UC status in the plans, and given the direct conflict shown, this is a FAIL\n- Status: FAIL (trees shown directly on OHE line, locations violate minimum clearances, no UC status documented in plant schedule)\n\n**EL-2.2: Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission conductor**\n- The OHE line shown appears to be distribution (typical Austin utility)\n- No transmission voltage is indicated\n- Even if it were transmission, the trees are within 50 ft\n- But since no voltage is specified, I cannot definitively determine if this is transmission or distribution\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE (voltage classification not shown)\n\n**EL-2.3: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution conductor**\n- Live Oak: Mature height 40-50 feet (LARGE TREE by ECM Appendix F standards)\n- Cedar Elm: Mature height 40-60 feet (LARGE TREE by ECM Appendix F standards)\n\n\n- Both species are positioned directly on the OHE line, with the plant schedule only noting \"16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\" at installation, not their mature dimensions. This is a FAIL since the trees will grow well beyond the 25 ft clearance requirement.\n\n**EL-2.4: Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission conductor**\n- The same species would violate this if the line were transmission, but without voltage classification shown on the plans, I cannot confirm applicability. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.5: Trees within transmission easement boundaries**\n- No transmission easement appears on the site or plans; the OHE line represents an existing utility easement. Status: N/A.\n\n**EL-2.6: Trees within 10 ft of utility pole**\n- Existing poles are marked on the western boundary with trees along all perimeter areas, but no dimensions are provided to verify clearances. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.7: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment**\n- The design calls for underground electrical service with no pad-mounted transformers proposed. Status: N/A.\n\n**EL-2.\n\n8: Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment**\n- Underground infrastructure is shown on Sheet 21, but the landscape plan lacks tree location data relative to these systems and provides no clearance dimensions. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.9: Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lack root barriers**\n- Root barrier specifications are not documented on the landscape plan for trees near underground electrical lines. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.10: Plant legend doesn't identify species**\n- The plant schedule provides both common and scientific names for all species, including Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud, and various shrubs and groundcovers.\n\n**EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated**\n- Live Oak and Cedar Elm are the large species with 40+ ft mature heights, but the schedule only lists \"16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\" as planting size without documenting mature heights. Status: FAIL.\n\n**EL-2.12: Clearances measured from pole instead of conductor**\n- No clearances are dimensioned on the landscape plan. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.13: Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk**\n- Clearances are not dimensioned on the plans. Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\n**EL-2.14: Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities**\n- The landscape plan shows trees positioned directly along the OHE line, creating a clear conflict. Status: FAIL.\n\n**EL-2.15: Trees within prohibited clearance zones without Austin Energy approval**\n- Trees are placed on the OHE line with no documented Austin Energy approval or exceptions. Status: FAIL.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"159d5199-1b19-4e60-b734-541962d15615"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187776540,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23ZSQ4WFX862QGX11Q775C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents and landscape plans, I now have sufficient evidence to evaluate all checklist items. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- Existing overhead electric line (OHE) runs along the southern property boundary (shown on Landscape Plan Sheet 31)\n- Existing OHE also shown along western boundary on Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)\n- All PROPOSED electrical infrastructure is underground (transformers, pull boxes, meters)\n- No transmission voltage designation found; existing OHE appears to be distribution-class\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\nFrom Plant Schedule (Sheet 35):\n- 2× Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) – 100 gal., 4\" caliper, \"16' HT. minimum\"\n- 10× Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) – 100 gal., 4\" caliper, \"16' HT. minimum\"\n- 2× Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) – 45 gal., 2.5\" caliper, \"8' HT. minimum\"\n- 6× Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) – 45 gal., 2.5\" caliper, \"10' HT. minimum\"\n- Additional shrubs and groundcovers\n\n**CRITICAL CONFLICT IDENTIFIED:**\nVision analysis of Landscape Plan (Sheet 31, southern boundary) reveals:\n- 6 mitigation trees (\"M\" designation) positioned directly ON the OHE line\n- OHE line passes through tree canopy circles and appears to pass directly over trunk locations\n- NO clearance dimensions or distance annotations shown\n- NO Austin Energy approval documentation provided\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Utility-compatible (UC) status of proposed trees NOT documented in plant schedule\n- Mature heights of Live Oak and Cedar Elm NOT specified (only planting sizes of \"16' minimum\" shown)\n- Voltage classification of OHE line NOT shown on plans\n- Distance measurements from any proposed tree to overhead conductors\n- Distance measurements from proposed trees to utility poles\n- Distance measurements from proposed trees to underground equipment\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment\n- Transmission easement boundaries (none appear to exist on site)\n- Austin Energy written approval for tree placement in conflict zones\n- Clarification whether OHE represents distribution or transmission facilities\n\n---"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"a5ca8f9f-735c-40c7-b3b9-937e74dd010b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187776767,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2401HBC2B4V3Z3X8K9B8CC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This is a critical finding:\n\n**Sheet 9 (Site Plan) - KEY FINDINGS:**\n1. **Overhead electric line (OHE) CROSSES DIRECTLY OVER THE MAIN DRIVEWAY** near the southwest portion of the site\n2. **NO vertical clearance heights are labeled** for this driveway where the OHE crosses\n3. Buildings are set back and don't appear to be directly under the OHE, but the driveway does\n4. **NO section/elevation callouts** for clearance verification\n5. **NO notes about utility clearances or restrictions**\n\nThis is a major deficiency for multiple checklist items:\n\n**Critical deficiencies identified:**\n1. **EL-1.18** - Driveways do not maintain minimum 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines - NO DOCUMENTATION OF CLEARANCE\n2. **EL-1.19** - If there's a parking pad under the line, clearances not verified\n3. **EL-1.46** - NO 48-hour notification note found\n4. **EL-1.37** - Trees not utility-compatible, placed near OHE line\n5. **EL-1.1** - NO clearance dimensions from buildings to overhead lines\n6. **EL-1.8** - NO section/plan exhibits showing clearances from outer conductor\n\nNow I have enough information to begin the formal evaluation. Let me organize my findings and assess each checklist item systematically.\n\nBased on all my research, here are the key findings:\n\n**APPLICABILITY:**\nThis grouping IS APPLICABLE. The project:\n- Has existing overhead electric distribution lines (confirmed on Sheets 4, 31)\n- Has electric easements (5' electric easements per Mecey plat)\n- Proposes new buildings, driveways, parking, walkways, and landscaping\n- Has an OHE driveway crossing requiring vertical clearance verification\n\n\n- The driveway crossing lacks clearance dimensions, profile sections showing vertical clearances, and surveyed conductor elevation data. Trees near the OHE line haven't been verified as utility-compatible species, and the cover sheet is missing the required 48-hour notification note. Building elevation sheets with conductor elevations are also absent from the submittal.\n\nNow I'll document each checklist deficiency formally, working through the major issues first before addressing the remaining items.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","uuid":"20997d81-1a7d-4164-9d1a-6237bf628d06"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187779109,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2401HBC2B4V3Z3X8K9B8CC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents, I now have sufficient evidence to evaluate all checklist items. Let me proceed with the formal assessment.\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**APPLICABILITY: YES - This grouping applies to this project**\n\n**Key Evidence Found:**\n1. **Existing overhead electric infrastructure confirmed** on Sheets 4 (survey) and 31 (landscape plan)\n   - OHE line runs along southern property boundary\n   - Poles marked with specific symbols\n   - 5' electric easements dedicated per Mecey Subdivision plat\n\n2. **Proposed site features requiring clearance verification:**\n   - 8 buildings with driveways, parking, and landscaping\n   - **OHE line crosses directly over main driveway** (southwest entrance)\n   - Trees proposed near OHE line boundary on Sheet 31\n   - Retaining walls up to 14 feet high\n\n3. **CRITICAL GAPS - Missing Documentation:**\n   - **NO vertical clearance dimensions** labeled where OHE crosses driveway\n   - **NO building elevation sheets** with surveyed conductor elevations\n   - **NO profile/section views** showing clearances from outer conductor to buildings/structures\n   - **NO utilities-compatible species verification** for trees near OHE line\n   - **NO 48-hour notification note** on cover sheet or general notes\n   - **NO mid-span clearance survey data** provided by registered surveyor\n\n**Trees near OHE (Sheet 31):**\n- Proposed species include: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud\n- None marked as utility-compatible (UC) per ECM Appendix F\n- Cedar Elm and Live Oak can exceed 20 feet mature height and are NOT utility-compatible\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","s