{"level":30,"time":1778187809667,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2416X18ERPBNVADPT3P13J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've successfully completed the site plan review for grouping 2, \"Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines.\" \n\nMy analysis found:\n\n**Key Findings**:\n1. **EL-2.1 (FAIL)**: Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) within 15 ft of distribution conductor\n2. **EL-2.2 (N/A)**: No transmission facilities present\n3. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)**: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution conductor\n4. **EL-2.4 (N/A)**: No transmission facilities present\n5. **EL-2.5 (N/A)**: No transmission easement shown\n6. **EL-2.6 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Pole positions not dimensioned on landscape plan\n7. **EL-2.7 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Pad-mounted equipment distances not documented\n8. **EL-2.8 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Underground equipment distances not documented\n9. **EL-2.9 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Trees near underground equipment and root barriers not documented\n10. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)**: Plant legend doesn't identify species near utilities\n11. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)**: Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan\n12. **EL-2.12 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: No dimension lines showing measurement methodology\n13. **EL-2.13 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: No dimensions showing measurement point (trunk vs. canopy)\n14. **EL-2.14 (PASS)**: Trees and overhead facilities shown together on landscape plan\n15. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)**: No Austin Energy written approval for trees in prohibited zones\n\nTotal: 5 FAIL, 4 NOT-VERIFIABLE, 3 N/A, 1 PASS (with caveats on the PASS items explaining that clearance documentation and approval are missing)\n\n\nThe evaluation systematically addresses all 15 requirements, identifying specific violations like incompatible species placement and missing clearance documentation, along with documentation gaps that prevent verification of compliance with utility safety standards.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49385103-a1b8-4868-b0ea-01fec564ebbd","uuid":"be5cdd21-e0c6-47c4-8130-c7fb1485e067"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187813763,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2416X18ERPBNVADPT3P13J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping **2 — Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nThe site plan for Valley View Townhomes proposes new trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel) that will be planted adjacent to existing overhead electric lines on the property's southern boundary. The review identified **critical compliance gaps** in tree clearance documentation and species selection:\n\n### Critical Violations (5 failures):\n\n1. **EL-2.1 (FAIL)**: Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) are being planted within 15 lateral feet of the overhead distribution conductor without clearance documentation or Austin Energy approval.\n\n2. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)**: Large trees with 40+ foot mature heights (Cedar Elm, Live Oak per ECM Appendix F) are proposed within 25 lateral feet of the distribution conductor in direct violation of clearance requirements.\n\n3. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)**: Trees shown on the landscape plan adjacent to overhead lines are not identified by species using a legend keyed to the plan; species identification requires cross-referencing a separate plant list.\n\n4. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)**: Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are not visually differentiated on the landscape plan; the plant schedule lists only installation heights (16'), not mature heights per ECM Appendix F.\n\n5. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)**: Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. The Master Comment Report indicates Austin Energy flagged \"Landscaping & Trees\" as a required review item, but no approval letter was submitted.\n\n### Unverifiable Items (4):\n\nItems EL-2.6, 2.7, 2.8, and 2.9 cannot be verified because utility pole locations, pad-mounted equipment positions, underground equipment locations, and root barrier specifications are not dimensioned on the landscape plan in relation to proposed tree placements.\n\n### Not Applicable (3):\n\nItems EL-2.2, 2.4, and 2.5 do not apply because the site has only distribution-class (not transmission) overhead facilities, and no transmission easement is depicted.\n\n### Passing (1):\n\nItem EL-2.14 passes because trees and overhead electric facilities are both shown together on the landscape plan, though critical clearance and approval documentation is absent.\n\n**Applicant must obtain explicit Austin Energy written approval and revise tree species and/or locations to comply with utility clearance requirements before plan approval.**"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49385103-a1b8-4868-b0ea-01fec564ebbd","uuid":"0fe68cf7-c8ef-4dca-ae38-9669522d22b7"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187813797,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":241655,"duration_api_ms":149959,"num_turns":22,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping **2 — Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nThe site plan for Valley View Townhomes proposes new trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel) that will be planted adjacent to existing overhead electric lines on the property's southern boundary. The review identified **critical compliance gaps** in tree clearance documentation and species selection:\n\n### Critical Violations (5 failures):\n\n1. **EL-2.1 (FAIL)**: Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) are being planted within 15 lateral feet of the overhead distribution conductor without clearance documentation or Austin Energy approval.\n\n2. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)**: Large trees with 40+ foot mature heights (Cedar Elm, Live Oak per ECM Appendix F) are proposed within 25 lateral feet of the distribution conductor in direct violation of clearance requirements.\n\n3. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)**: Trees shown on the landscape plan adjacent to overhead lines are not identified by species using a legend keyed to the plan; species identification requires cross-referencing a separate plant list.\n\n4. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)**: Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are not visually differentiated on the landscape plan; the plant schedule lists only installation heights (16'), not mature heights per ECM Appendix F.\n\n5. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)**: Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. The Master Comment Report indicates Austin Energy flagged \"Landscaping & Trees\" as a required review item, but no approval letter was submitted.\n\n### Unverifiable Items (4):\n\nItems EL-2.6, 2.7, 2.8, and 2.9 cannot be verified because utility pole locations, pad-mounted equipment positions, underground equipment locations, and root barrier specifications are not dimensioned on the landscape plan in relation to proposed tree placements.\n\n### Not Applicable (3):\n\nItems EL-2.2, 2.4, and 2.5 do not apply because the site has only distribution-class (not transmission) overhead facilities, and no transmission easement is depicted.\n\n### Passing (1):\n\nItem EL-2.14 passes because trees and overhead electric facilities are both shown together on the landscape plan, though critical clearance and approval documentation is absent.\n\n**Applicant must obtain explicit Austin Energy written approval and revise tree species and/or locations to comply with utility clearance requirements before plan approval.**","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"49385103-a1b8-4868-b0ea-01fec564ebbd","total_cost_usd":0.22594460000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":3090,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67846,"cache_read_input_tokens":605471,"output_tokens":15500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":67846},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3090,"outputTokens":15500,"cacheReadInputTokens":605471,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67846,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22594460000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols being planted directly adjacent to the overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") along the southern property boundary. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) proposes 10 Cedar Elm and 2 Live Oak trees. Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) and Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) are non-utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F. Vision analysis confirms at least 4 tree symbols are positioned within approximately 5 feet of the overhead electric line.","reasoning":"Non-utility-compatible trees are being planted well within 15 lateral feet of the overhead electric distribution conductor. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are specifically non-UC species that require greater clearance or are prohibited in restricted zones. The plan provides no evidence of Austin Energy written approval for this variation from standard requirements. This violates UCM § 1.10.10.4 clearance requirements for distribution conductors.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) are being planted within the 15-foot restricted zone adjacent to overhead electric distribution lines. No Austin Energy approval is documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The overhead electric lines shown on the site plan (labeled \"-OHE-\") appear to be distribution-class infrastructure. The plan does not indicate transmission voltage classification (60kV or higher). The site lacks the typical transmission infrastructure characteristics (dedicated easements, transmission plat notes, larger poles and structures). Facts.md confirms only distribution class electric easements (5-foot electric easements per Mecey Subdivision plat).","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are typically explicitly labeled as transmission, carry 60kV or higher, and are located in dedicated transmission easements with special plat designation. The existing overhead lines appear to be standard distribution infrastructure without transmission designation. Therefore, the 50-foot transmission conductor clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission facilities do not appear to be present on this site; requirement is not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols planted directly adjacent to the overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") on the southern boundary. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) proposes 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) and 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana). Both species are listed in ECM Appendix F with mature heights of 40+ feet. Vision analysis confirms tree symbols are positioned within approximately 5 feet of the overhead line, well within the 25-foot prohibited zone for large trees near distribution conductors.","reasoning":"Large trees with mature heights of 40+ feet are being planted within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductors. The plan provides no Austin Energy written approval authorizing this variation. This violates the large tree clearance requirement of UCM § 1.10.10.4, which prohibits trees exceeding 40-foot mature height within 25 feet of distribution conductors.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are proposed within 25 feet of overhead electric distribution lines without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy approval."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The overhead electric lines on the site appear to be distribution-class (not transmission 60kV+). Transmission facilities are not identified on the site plan with dedicated easements or transmission voltage labeling.","reasoning":"This item applies only to transmission facilities (60kV or higher). The site has only distribution-class overhead lines. Large tree prohibition within 50 feet of transmission does not apply when transmission facilities are absent.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities are present on site; requirement is not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan and facts.md document show multiple drainage and wastewater easements but no transmission easement is depicted or referenced. The plat (Sheet 2) shows drainage and utility easements but no transmission easement boundary is marked.","reasoning":"The categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement boundaries applies only when a transmission easement is present on the property. No transmission easement is depicted on the submitted site plans, and facts.md lists only drainage and wastewater easements on the NE portion of the lot.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is depicted on the site plan; requirement is not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows overhead electric lines (\"-OHE-\") but does not depict the specific locations of utility poles supporting these lines. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows that the proposed electrical infrastructure is underground with transformers and pull boxes, but does not clearly correlate pole locations with the existing overhead lines.","reasoning":"While trees are shown adjacent to overhead lines, the specific locations of utility poles supporting those lines are not clearly marked on the landscape plan with sufficient detail to measure 10-foot clearances. Without pole positions dimensioned on the landscape plan, it cannot be verified whether trees violate or comply with the 10-foot pole clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Area near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility pole locations are not clearly dimensioned on the landscape plan relative to proposed tree locations. Clearance verification cannot be completed from available documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows four pad-mounted electrical transformers located near the perimeter of the site. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees but does not include dimension lines or distance measurements from trees to the transformer pad locations. The specific coordinates of transformer pads are not clearly cross-referenced with tree placement on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"While pad-mounted equipment exists on the site and trees are shown on the landscape plan, the distance between specific tree symbols and transformer pad locations cannot be precisely determined from the submitted plans. No dimension lines or notes specify clearances from trees to pads, making verification impossible.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Area around transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted equipment locations are not dimensioned relative to proposed tree placements on the landscape plan. Clearance verification cannot be completed from available documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical conduit routing with pull boxes throughout the site. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols but does not overlay or dimension the underground utility paths relative to tree locations. No distance measurements from trees to underground equipment are provided.","reasoning":"The 5-foot clearance requirement for underground electric equipment applies only to specific equipment types (not duct banks/conduits). While underground infrastructure is shown, the landscape plan does not clearly identify which trees, if any, are within 5 feet of underground equipment pull boxes or vaults. Verification of compliance requires overlay analysis not visible on submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas with underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Specific locations of underground electrical equipment are not dimensioned relative to tree placements. Clearance verification cannot be determined from available documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical conduit and pull boxes. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees but no dimension lines quantifying distance from trees to underground equipment. Landscape details (Sheet 37) show standard tree planting and protection details but do not include specifications for root barriers when trees are within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment.","reasoning":"While underground equipment exists on site and trees are proposed, the plan does not clearly identify which trees, if any, are within 20 feet of underground equipment. Additionally, the landscape details do not specify root barrier installation for trees in proximity to underground utilities. Without distance verification and explicit root barrier notes, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment are not identified on the landscape plan, and root barrier specifications for such locations are not shown on landscape details."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols at various locations on the site, including the cluster of trees adjacent to the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. These tree symbols are not directly labeled with species names on the landscape plan itself. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists species separately: Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel. To identify which specific species are planted near the overhead lines, the viewer must cross-reference the landscape plan symbols with the separate plant schedule.","reasoning":"While the plant schedule documents all proposed species, the landscape plan itself does not identify the species of trees shown in proximity to electric facilities. Direct species identification on or immediately adjacent to the landscape plan drawing near utility lines is required to allow quick verification of utility compatibility. The current plan requires manual cross-referencing to identify species, which is not a complete plant legend that keys species to symbols shown on the landscape plan for areas near utilities.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown near overhead electric line on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near electric facilities on the landscape plan are not identified by species using a keyed legend. Species identification requires manual cross-reference to a separate plant list rather than direct labeling on the plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols without differentiation by size class or mature height. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists planting specifications including 'minimum heights' of 16' (for Cedar Elm and Live Oak, which are actually 40+ feet at mature height per ECM Appendix F) and 8'-10' for ornamental trees. The landscape plan provides no visual distinction (color, hatching, note callout) to identify which trees are large (40+ feet mature height) versus small or medium trees.","reasoning":"Trees with mature heights of 40+ feet (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) require special clearance distances from electric infrastructure and are subject to different restrictions than smaller trees. The landscape plan does not differentiate large trees on the drawing itself. The plant schedule lists only planting height specifications (16'), not mature heights per ECM Appendix F. This makes it impossible for reviewers to quickly identify which proposed trees have the large-tree restrictions without external research.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Cedar Elm and Live Oak tree locations on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not visually differentiated on the landscape plan. Plant schedule lists installation heights (16'), not mature heights, making it difficult to identify trees subject to large-tree clearance restrictions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and the overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") on the same drawing. However, no dimension lines, measurements, or leader lines are provided to quantify the distance between tree symbols and the conductor line. No notes explain the measurement methodology or point of reference for clearance calculations.","reasoning":"When tree clearances are dimensioned on plans, they must be measured from the outside (outer) conductor, not from the pole centerline, per the grouping's measurement methodology requirements. Since no dimensions are shown on this plan, the measurement reference point (conductor vs. pole) cannot be assessed. However, the absence of dimensions means that the requirement to measure from the correct reference point is inherently not met—the applicant has not demonstrated clearance verification using proper measurement methodology.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimension lines are provided on the landscape plan showing tree clearances from overhead electric conductors. Measurement methodology cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols as circles, which represent the tree canopy or general location. No dimension lines originate from specific tree trunk locations to the overhead electric line. Without dimensions on the plan, the point of measurement (trunk center vs. canopy edge) cannot be evaluated.","reasoning":"The requirement to measure from tree trunk center (planting location) rather than from canopy edge is a measurement methodology standard. Since no clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan, the applicant has not provided evidence of their measurement methodology. This means the specific requirement cannot be verified as compliant, though it also cannot be proven non-compliant from the plan set alone.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimension lines on the landscape plan show whether tree clearances were measured from tree trunk centers or canopy edges. Measurement methodology cannot be verified from available documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) clearly shows both tree symbols (representing proposed trees) and the overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") on the same drawing. The overhead line is labeled and runs along the southern property boundary. Trees are shown with their symbols positioned relative to the line, making the spatial relationship between trees and overhead facilities visible on a single drawing.","reasoning":"While clearance verification documentation is lacking, the fundamental requirement that trees be shown on the landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities is met. The applicant has depicted both elements on the same plan view, allowing the spatial relationship to be observed. The requirement is to show the relationship; detailed clearance analysis and approval are separate requirements covered by other checklist items.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing overhead electric infrastructure and trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and overhead electric facilities are shown together on the landscape plan, satisfying the basic requirement to depict them in relationship."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Trees are clearly proposed within prohibited clearance zones: Cedar Elm and Live Oak (both 40+ feet mature height, non-UC) are planted within approximately 5 feet of the overhead electric line according to landscape plan analysis. The master comment report indicates Austin Energy flagged 'Landscaping & Trees' (UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4) as a requirement requiring review. No written Austin Energy approval letter is visible in the submitted plan set or supplementary documents. The Bluebeam review link referenced in the master comments was not accessible in the document set provided.","reasoning":"The grouping's regulatory overview explicitly states that variations to planting distances and species identified as utility-compatible require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The plans propose non-UC trees and large trees within restricted zones without documented Austin Energy approval. Austin Energy's review flagged this requirement, but no approval letter was submitted with the plans. This is a direct violation of UCM § 1.10.10.4 exception provisions.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within 15 feet of overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report - Electric Review"}],"comment":"Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones (non-UC Cedar Elm and Live Oak within 15 feet of overhead distribution line). No documented Austin Energy written approval is provided. Applicant must obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy or modify tree species/locations to comply with clearance requirements."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e7959e38-cf89-49cb-bf78-eb5d90bf98a9"}
