mer pads:**\nThere are no clearly labeled transformer pads or equipment pads designated for transformers on this sheet. The legend does not include a symbol for a transformer. The only electrical-specific areas designated on the plan are easements on the eastern (right) side of the site:\n*   \"Greenbelt Access & Elec Easement Doc. 2010049121 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located near Building 5)\n*   \"3' Elec. Easement Vol. 66, Pg. 14...\" (Located near the eastern boundary)\n*   \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located near the southeastern boundary)\n\n**3) Drainage flow direction near any transformer pad areas:**\nBecause no transformer pads are identified on this plan, specific drainage flow directions immediately adjacent to them cannot be determined. \n\n**4) Finish grade elevations around transformer pads if labeled:**\nNo transformer pads are identified, so no corresponding finish grade elevations can be provided.\n\n**5) Any spot elevations or contour information that would show drainage slope direction:**\nThe plan is populated with specific proposed spot elevations that confirm the drainage slopes indicated by the arrows:\n*   **Confirming Western Slope:** The main driveway slopes down toward the entrance on the left. A spot elevation between Building 3 and 4 is **\"684.90\"**. Moving left (west) down the drive, a spot elevation between Building 2 and 7 is **\"683.48\"**. Further west, near the site entrance at Valley View Road, a spot elevation reads **\"681.36\"**, confirming a downward slope toward the street.\n*   **Confirming Eastern Slope:** Moving right (east) from the central high point, a spot elevation between Building 4 and 5 is **\"684.34\"**. At the eastern end of the paved driveway near Building 5, the spot elevation drops to **\"681.00\"**, confirming a downward slope toward the rear of the site.\n*   **Site Perimeter (Bottom Left):** Spot elevations in the bottom left corner near the road drop to **\"679.46\"** and **\"679.25\"**, indicating the lowest point on the western edge.\n\n**6) Any notes about oil-filled or other equipment on this sheet:**\nThere are no notes regarding oil-filled equipment, transformers, or associated containment requirements on this sheet. The only notes present are a \"Legend,\" \"Curb Note,\" \"Tree List\" reference, \"Benchmarks,\" and a utility location note for \"Texas 811.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1407,"outputTokens":849,"totalTokens":5545,"reasoningTokens":3289},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the grading plan and identify: 1) Surfa