{"level":30,"time":1778187829004,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR241QS9XCH5FG9ZE8AZ83T0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete: EL-MD-EXP Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)\n\nI have completed the site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n**Overall Status: MULTIPLE CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED**\n\nThe site plan shows a **critical conflict** between proposed landscape mitigation trees and existing overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure:\n\n- **6 mitigation trees are shown directly on the overhead electric line** running along the southern property boundary\n- **No clearance distances are documented** between trees and conductors\n- **No Austin Energy written approval** is provided for trees in restricted zones\n- **Large tree species (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with 40+ ft mature heights) lack proper differentiation** on the plant schedule\n\n### Deficiency Summary by Status:\n\n**FAIL (4 items):**\n- **EL-2.1**: Trees positioned within prohibited 15-foot distribution clearance zone\n- **EL-2.3**: Large trees (40+ ft mature height) positioned within prohibited 25-foot distribution clearance zone\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans (mature heights not documented in plant schedule)\n- **EL-2.14**: Trees shown directly on OHE line creating apparent zero-clearance condition\n- **EL-2.15**: Trees within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy approval\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (5 items):**\n- **EL-2.2**: Voltage classification of OHE not specified (cannot determine if transmission standard applies)\n- **EL-2.4**: Cannot verify transmission clearance without voltage classification\n- **EL-2.6**: No lateral distance dimensions provided between trees and utility poles\n- **EL-2.8**: Distances between proposed trees and underground electrical equipment not documented\n- **EL-2.9**: Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment not documented\n- **EL-2.12**: No clearance dimensions shown; measurement methodology cannot be verified\n- **EL-2.13**: No clearance dimensions shown; measurement reference point cannot be verified\n\n**PASS (1 item):**\n- **EL-2.10**: All plant species properly identified in plant schedule with common and scientific names\n\n**N/A (3 items):**\n- **EL-2.5**: No transmission easement on property\n- **EL-2.7**: No pad-mounted equipment (all electrical infrastructure is underground)\n\n### Primary Recommendation\n\nThe applicant must resolve the fundamental conflict of six mitigation trees shown directly on the overhead electric line. Options include: (1) relocating trees away from the OHE line to maintain minimum clearances (15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for large trees from distribution conductors); (2) obtaining and documenting written approval from Austin Energy for the non-standard placement; or (3) selecting alternative tree species with documented utility-compatible designation and appropriate mature heights."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","uuid":"f6187664-802d-44a3-87a7-50a79508159e"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187829033,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":256978,"duration_api_ms":145443,"num_turns":21,"result":"## Review Complete: EL-MD-EXP Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)\n\nI have completed the site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n**Overall Status: MULTIPLE CRITICAL DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED**\n\nThe site plan shows a **critical conflict** between proposed landscape mitigation trees and existing overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure:\n\n- **6 mitigation trees are shown directly on the overhead electric line** running along the southern property boundary\n- **No clearance distances are documented** between trees and conductors\n- **No Austin Energy written approval** is provided for trees in restricted zones\n- **Large tree species (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with 40+ ft mature heights) lack proper differentiation** on the plant schedule\n\n### Deficiency Summary by Status:\n\n**FAIL (4 items):**\n- **EL-2.1**: Trees positioned within prohibited 15-foot distribution clearance zone\n- **EL-2.3**: Large trees (40+ ft mature height) positioned within prohibited 25-foot distribution clearance zone\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans (mature heights not documented in plant schedule)\n- **EL-2.14**: Trees shown directly on OHE line creating apparent zero-clearance condition\n- **EL-2.15**: Trees within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy approval\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (5 items):**\n- **EL-2.2**: Voltage classification of OHE not specified (cannot determine if transmission standard applies)\n- **EL-2.4**: Cannot verify transmission clearance without voltage classification\n- **EL-2.6**: No lateral distance dimensions provided between trees and utility poles\n- **EL-2.8**: Distances between proposed trees and underground electrical equipment not documented\n- **EL-2.9**: Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment not documented\n- **EL-2.12**: No clearance dimensions shown; measurement methodology cannot be verified\n- **EL-2.13**: No clearance dimensions shown; measurement reference point cannot be verified\n\n**PASS (1 item):**\n- **EL-2.10**: All plant species properly identified in plant schedule with common and scientific names\n\n**N/A (3 items):**\n- **EL-2.5**: No transmission easement on property\n- **EL-2.7**: No pad-mounted equipment (all electrical infrastructure is underground)\n\n### Primary Recommendation\n\nThe applicant must resolve the fundamental conflict of six mitigation trees shown directly on the overhead electric line. Options include: (1) relocating trees away from the OHE line to maintain minimum clearances (15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for large trees from distribution conductors); (2) obtaining and documenting written approval from Austin Energy for the non-standard placement; or (3) selecting alternative tree species with documented utility-compatible designation and appropriate mature heights.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0f3dc44-9163-45e1-9f6b-3d0c261bf982","total_cost_usd":0.24315304999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":11677,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73963,"cache_read_input_tokens":602573,"output_tokens":15753,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":73963},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11677,"outputTokens":15753,"cacheReadInputTokens":602573,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73963,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24315304999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows six mitigation trees (marked 'M') positioned directly along the marked OHE (overhead electric) line running the full length of the southern property boundary. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists proposed trees including Live Oak and Cedar Elm but does not document their utility-compatible (UC) designation status, and the trees are shown directly on the conductor path rather than maintaining the required 15-foot lateral clearance from distribution conductors.","reasoning":"Under UCM § 1.10.10.4, non-utility-compatible trees must be kept at least 15 lateral feet from distribution conductors. The landscape plan graphically depicts trees placed directly on the OHE line, indicating clearances of near-zero feet. The plant schedule's failure to document which species are UC-designated prevents confirmation that all proposed species meet the utility-compatible requirement for proximity to distribution lines. The visible conflict on the landscape plan itself (trees on the OHE line) constitutes a deficiency regardless of species UC status.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary along Valley View Road where OHE runs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Six mitigation trees shown directly on overhead electric line on landscape plan, with no clearance maintained from distribution conductor and no UC status documented for proposed species in plant schedule."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows an OHE line on the southern boundary and the electrical plan shows existing overhead lines. However, the voltage classification of the existing overhead electric lines is not specified on either the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) or the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Without voltage designation (distribution <60kV vs. transmission ≥60kV), the applicability of the 50-foot transmission clearance requirement cannot be determined.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 distinguishes clearance requirements based on voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission). To determine if the 50-foot transmission clearance applies, the voltage of the overhead lines must be identified. The plans do not provide this critical information, making it impossible to verify whether the requirement applies or whether proposed trees comply with transmission clearances.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern and western property boundaries where OHE shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Voltage classification of existing overhead electric lines not specified on plans. Cannot determine if transmission (≥60kV) or distribution (<60kV) classification applies, and therefore cannot verify compliance with 50-foot transmission clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule (Sheet 35) proposes 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) trees. According to ECM Appendix F, Live Oak has a mature height of 40-50 feet and Cedar Elm has a mature height of 40-60 feet, both qualifying as 'large trees' (≥40 feet). The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols for these species positioned directly on the marked OHE line running along the southern boundary, indicating clearances of near-zero lateral feet from the distribution conductor.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 prohibits large trees (mature height ≥40 feet) within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductors. Both Live Oak and Cedar Elm are confirmed as large trees per ECM Appendix F standards. The landscape plan graphically depicts these trees directly on the OHE line, indicating a clearance violation. The plant schedule's notation of '16' HT. Minimum Container Grown' documents planting size only, not mature height; mature heights must be derived from ECM Appendix F standards.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary OHE line where large tree mitigation trees are planted"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with mature heights 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) shown directly on distribution OHE line on landscape plan, violating 25-foot minimum clearance from distribution conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, both ≥40 feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are shown on the landscape plan positioned near overhead electric lines. However, the voltage classification of the overhead electric lines is not specified on the plans, making it impossible to determine whether the 50-foot transmission clearance requirement applies or whether the trees' proximity violates the transmission standard.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 establishes different clearance requirements for distribution (25 feet from large trees) vs. transmission (50 feet from large trees) facilities. Without the voltage classification of the OHE shown on the plans, this requirement's applicability cannot be verified. If the line is transmission, a 50-foot clearance is required; if distribution, 25 feet applies (which is already failed under EL-2.3). The deficiency cannot be independently verified from transmission-specific evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern and western property boundaries where OHE shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Voltage classification not specified. Cannot independently verify transmission clearance compliance without confirmation that OHE is transmission-class (≥60kV)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The facts.md document lists multiple easements on the property (greenbelt, drainage, wastewater, and electric easements), but no transmission easement is identified as existing on the site. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows an existing OHE line running along the southern boundary, but this is labeled as a utility line (OHE) rather than a transmission easement. No plat notes or easement designations on the site plan identify a transmission easement corridor.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 and § 1.14.6 categorically prohibit trees within transmission easement boundaries. Applicability requires the presence of a transmission easement on the property. The facts and plans provided do not identify a transmission easement on this site; the existing overhead line shown (OHE) is a distribution utility line with its own easement, not a transmission easement. In the absence of documented transmission easement boundaries, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement identified on property. Requirement applies only when transmission easement is present."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows utility pole symbols marked with 'E' along the western property boundary as part of the existing OHE infrastructure. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows multiple trees positioned around all four property boundaries. However, no specific lateral distance dimensions are provided between any proposed tree and the nearest utility pole.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires trees to be maintained at minimum 10 lateral feet from any electric utility pole. While infrastructure exists (poles are shown) and trees are shown on plans (making them visible), the specific clearance distances between individual tree symbols and pole locations are not dimensioned or calculated. Without documented distances, compliance cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["western boundary where utility poles are located; all property perimeters where trees are shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles exist on site but clearance distances from proposed trees to poles are not dimensioned or documented on landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows that all proposed electrical infrastructure for this development is underground, including underground electric lines, electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. No pad-mounted transformers are shown anywhere on the site. The plan explicitly notes 'Underground Electric Line' as the routing type, not overhead or pad-mounted equipment.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 restricts tree planting within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted electric equipment. This requirement applies only when pad-mounted equipment is proposed or present on the site. Since the project design utilizes exclusively underground electrical distribution with underground transformer pads (not pad-mounted surface units), this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All proposed electrical infrastructure is underground; no pad-mounted equipment proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines routing throughout the site with pull boxes and underground transformer locations marked. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed tree locations. However, the landscape plan does not provide lateral distance dimensions between any proposed tree symbol and any underground electrical equipment (pull boxes, underground transformers, or duct banks).","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires trees to be kept minimum 5 lateral feet from underground electric equipment (other than duct banks). To verify compliance, the lateral distances between trees and underground equipment must be documented or measurable from dimensioned plans. The submitted landscape plan does not provide these distances, making it impossible to confirm whether specific trees maintain the 5-foot clearance from underground facilities.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["throughout site where underground electrical infrastructure and planted trees intersect"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distances between proposed trees and underground electrical equipment not documented on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Underground electrical equipment is shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21), and trees are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). However, neither the landscape plan nor any detail sheets provide documentation of root barrier specifications, dimensions, depths, or locations for any proposed trees located within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) for trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment. To verify compliance, the plans must document root barrier specifications. The submitted plans contain no such detail or notes, making it impossible to confirm whether required root barriers are specified and compliant.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["areas within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier specifications, depths, and positions not documented for trees within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule on Sheet 35 comprehensively identifies all proposed tree and shrub species by both common and scientific names: Live Oak (Quercus virginiana), Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia), Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora), Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana), and all shrubs and groundcovers (Dwarf Palmetto, Big Muhly, Gulf Muhly, Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle, Obedient Plant, Frogfruit). Each entry includes both the common name and the scientific binomial nomenclature.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires plant legend or schedule to identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities. The submitted plant schedule clearly identifies all species with both common and scientific names, satisfying this documentation requirement.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["throughout site landscape plan where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists Live Oak and Cedar Elm as proposed species but documents only their planting specifications ('100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN'). The 16' height notation refers to the minimum container-grown plant height at installation, not the mature height. According to ECM Appendix F, Live Oak has a mature height of 40-50 feet and Cedar Elm has a mature height of 40-60 feet, both qualifying as large trees (≥40 feet). The plant schedule does not differentiate or indicate which species are large trees by mature height standard.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires large trees (mature height ≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F) to be differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities. The submitted plant schedule lists planting sizes only and does not identify which species achieve large tree status (40+ feet mature height). This omission prevents a reviewer from readily identifying which trees must maintain the more restrictive 25-foot distribution or 50-foot transmission clearance requirements.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plan and plant schedule for Live Oak and Cedar Elm"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Live Oak and Cedar Elm are large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) but plant schedule does not differentiate or identify them as large trees; only planting size (16' minimum) is documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) both show trees and overhead/underground electrical infrastructure, but neither plan provides any dimensions or distance callouts measuring clearance between trees and conductors or poles.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 specifies that clearances must be measured as lateral (horizontal) distance from tree trunk center to the outer electric conductor (not pole centerline). Correct measurement methodology can only be verified when clearances are explicitly dimensioned on plans with clear notation of measurement origin and terminus. Without any dimensions shown, the measurement methodology cannot be evaluated for correctness.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["any area where tree-to-conductor distances are dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions provided on plans; measurement methodology cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols as circles representing tree canopy, with a '+' or dot mark in the center indicating trunk location. However, no clearance dimensions are provided anywhere on the landscape plan that would indicate whether any measured distances originate from the trunk location (proper method) or from the canopy edge.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires clearances to be measured from tree trunk center (planting location), not from canopy edge. This measurement methodology can only be verified when clearances are explicitly dimensioned with callouts clearly indicating the measurement reference point. Without any dimensions shown, the measurement origin cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["any area where tree clearances are dimensioned on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions provided on landscape plan; measurement reference point (trunk vs. canopy) cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) clearly shows both overhead electric line (OHE) running along the southern boundary and tree symbols positioned along all four property perimeters. Vision analysis confirms that six mitigation trees are shown directly on the OHE line path along the southern boundary, with the OHE line appearing to pass through the tree canopy circles and potentially over trunk locations. The trees ARE shown relative to the overhead facilities, and the relationship shows a direct conflict.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires trees to be shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities to allow clearance verification. Trees ARE shown, and overhead facilities ARE shown. However, the graphical relationship depicted indicates trees positioned directly on the conductor path with apparent zero clearance maintained. This violates clearance requirements (EL-2.1 and EL-2.3). The failure is not that trees are absent from the plan in relation to electrical facilities, but rather that trees are shown in positions that violate clearance standards without documented justification or approval.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary along OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown directly on overhead electric line, indicating zero clearance maintained from distribution conductor. No clearance distances documented or dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows six mitigation trees positioned directly on the overhead electric (OHE) line running along the southern property boundary. This placement violates the minimum clearance distances required by UCM § 1.10.10.4 (15 feet for non-utility-compatible trees from distribution conductors, 25 feet for large trees from distribution conductors). No documentation of written approval from Austin Energy is provided anywhere in the site plan set, supplementary documents, or plan notes that would authorize an exception to these clearance requirements.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 specifies that trees proposed within prohibited clearance zones require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The landscape plan shows trees in clear violation of standard clearance distances (trees directly on the OHE line). Without documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing the variation, the trees within the prohibited zones represent a deficiency. Plans must include approval correspondence or notes documenting the authorization; its absence constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary where mitigation trees are positioned on OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Six trees positioned directly on overhead electric line without documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing the clearance variance."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"38595bf9-776e-4849-9c16-67de6ab428ca"}
