{"level":30,"time":1778187832419,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23YDNJM2Z6F1G82Q68YH89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BPK14Gj6czL1QNJhrmmFqk","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations on the site, and Sheet 9 (Site Plan) labels one as 'Transformer Pad (Typ.)' near Bldg 2. However, no specific clearance dimensions or measurements are provided from any transformer pad to adjacent buildings, foundations, or structures on any submitted sheet.","reasoning":"While transformer pads are clearly present and located on the plans, the specific horizontal clearance distances required by UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 (minimum 5 feet from buildings/structures for brick/masonry and 12 feet for non-brick/masonry oil-filled equipment) cannot be verified from the submitted documents. The plans lack dimensioned clearance callouts, measurement lines, or distance annotations.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations - Sheet 21 (four pads) and Sheet 9 (one pad labeled)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown but clearance dimensions to buildings are not documented. Submit detailed plan sheets showing measured clearances from each transformer pad to all adjacent buildings and structures."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows retaining walls located on the site perimeter (north, east, and south). Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations, but no explicit dimensions or clearance measurements are shown between transformer pads and the retaining walls.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are present on the site, so this item is applicable. However, the specific 5-foot clearance distance from transformer pads to retaining walls (per Reviewer Convention) cannot be verified from the submitted documents. No dimension lines, callouts, or distance annotations showing the clearance are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to retaining walls shown on Sheet 11"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are present on site. Submit clearance dimensions from transformer pads to all adjacent retaining walls, demonstrating minimum 5-foot clearance where applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows wooden privacy fences (marked with 'H.6' key notes) along property boundaries. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations, including some with bollards marked. However, no dimensions show the distance from transformer pads to adjacent fences, and no callout indicates which sides of transformer pads are operators/controls sides versus non-operators/controls sides.","reasoning":"Fences are present on the site, triggering applicability of this item. However, the specific clearance distances required (5 feet for sides with operators/controls, 3 feet for sides without) and the transformer access door orientation cannot be verified from the submitted documents. No dimension annotations or access door orientation callouts are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to fences on property boundaries, especially western and southern perimeter"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on site. Submit clearance dimensions from transformer pads to fences, and identify transformer access door orientation to verify compliance with differential clearance requirements (5 feet vs. 3 feet per UCM § 1.10.4)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No clearance dimensions from any transformer pad to buildings are shown on the submitted plans. No note on any sheet indicates the presence, absence, or applicability of a 3-foot clearance reduction exception. No Austin Energy Design written approval documents are included in the submittal. No architectural specifications are provided documenting fire ratings in any clearance area.","reasoning":"This item addresses the case where clearances less than 5 feet are shown. Since no specific clearance dimensions are documented at all, it cannot be determined whether reduced clearances (3 feet) have been proposed. Without seeing reduced clearances proposed, this particular exception documentation cannot be evaluated. However, the absence of AE Design approval documents is notable given that the grouping explicitly requires them for any clearance reduction.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if clearances less than 5 feet to buildings are proposed (not shown on submitted plans)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances (less than 5 feet) are documented on the submitted plans. If the applicant intends to use reduced 3-foot clearances to brick/masonry buildings, submit Austin Energy Design written approval and architectural specifications documenting 3-hour fire rating in the clearance area."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations but provides no information about building balconies, overhangs, or structures directly above the pads. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) does not show overhead building elements or clearance dimensions. No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances or overhead obstructions above transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"While the site plan shows buildings with various heights and FFEs (shown on Sheets 9 and 11), no specific documentation indicates whether balconies or overhangs are present above or adjacent to transformer pads, and no vertical clearance measurements are provided. Without these dimensions, compliance with the 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies/overhangs cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to building balconies and overhangs (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balcony or overhang clearance documentation is provided. If balconies or overhangs exist above or adjacent to transformer pads, submit building elevations or cross-sections demonstrating minimum 5-foot lateral clearance and confirming no structures directly above pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevations with windows, doors, and ventilating duct locations are not provided in the submitted plan set. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer locations but does not indicate proximity to windows or doors. No transformer equipment specification sheet is provided identifying whether equipment is oil-filled (triggering the 12-foot clearance requirement).","reasoning":"This item requires verification of three conditions: (1) proximity of windows/doors/ducts on adjacent buildings, (2) grade elevation at those windows/doors, and (3) transformer equipment type (oil-filled). None of this information is documented in the submitted plans. Building elevation sheets are not included in the site plan set, and transformer type is not specified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to adjacent buildings' windows, doors, and ventilation (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevations or transformer type specifications are provided. Submit building elevation sheets showing window, door, and ventilation locations, transformer equipment specifications identifying whether oil-filled, and measured clearance distances demonstrating compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 (12 feet minimum for oil-filled equipment when clearance conditions are met)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows sidewalk locations, including a '5' Concrete Sidewalk' note near the western transformer pad. However, no dimension lines or distance measurements show the clearance from transformer pad edges to the back of sidewalk.","reasoning":"While sidewalks are present on the site and the western transformer pad is adjacent to a proposed sidewalk per the vision analysis, the specific 2-foot minimum clearance from the back of sidewalk cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or measurement annotations.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to proposed sidewalks, particularly the western pad near Bldg 2"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown on site plan. Submit clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 2-foot separation from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalk per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows the site's fire access routing and one private fire hydrant location. No stairwell serving as a fire exit is identified adjacent to transformer pad locations on any submitted sheet.","reasoning":"This item applies only when stairwells serving as fire exits are present adjacent to transformer pads. While the site has fire access and hydrants, the building floor plans and architectural drawings showing internal stairwells are not included in the site plan set. There is no evidence on the available sheets that a stairwell fire exit is adjacent to any transformer pad.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if fire exit stairwell is adjacent to transformer pad (not shown)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows one private fire hydrant location on the site and general fire lane routing. No fire escape structures are depicted on any site plan sheet. No transformer equipment specification sheet is provided identifying whether equipment is oil-filled (triggering the 20-foot fire escape clearance requirement).","reasoning":"Fire escapes are not shown on the submitted site plan sheets. However, building elevation sheets and detailed architectural plans (which would show fire escape locations) are not included in the site plan set. Additionally, transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified, which determines whether the 20-foot clearance requirement applies.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes (if present on buildings)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escape locations are shown on site plan sheets. If fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are present on the buildings, submit building elevations showing their locations and clearance dimensions from transformer pads (minimum 20 feet for oil-filled equipment per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations on the site with no specific dimensions, measurements, or callouts indicating access door orientation or the clearance distances from the access door side to open area or adjacent buildings.","reasoning":"The hot-stick use area clearance requirement (10 feet minimum from access door side to open area or adjacent building) cannot be verified without explicit documentation of: (1) which side of each transformer pad is the access door side, and (2) what features exist 10 feet from that side in all directions. No measurement callouts or access door orientation indicators are provided on any sheet.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown but access door orientation is not identified. Submit detailed site plan sheets showing transformer access door orientation and dimensions demonstrating minimum 10-foot clearance from hot-stick use area (access door side) to open area or adjacent building per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations without indicating whether any face enclosed areas, niches, vaults, or areas on 3+ sides. No detail drawings or cross-section views show niche configurations. No access path or entrance clearance heights are documented.","reasoning":"This item applies only when transformer locations face confined spaces (enclosed on 3+ sides). The submitted plans do not provide cross-section drawings or niche details that would indicate whether any transformer pads are in such a configuration. The 15-foot hot-stick clearance (versus standard 10-foot) cannot be evaluated without this configuration information.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if transformer faces confined space such as niche or enclosed area (not shown as proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche or enclosed area transformer configurations are indicated on submitted plans. If any transformer is located in a confined space (enclosed on 3+ sides), submit cross-section drawings demonstrating 15-foot vertical clearance per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows one private fire hydrant location on the site. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations. However, no distance dimensions or callouts show the clearance between transformer pads and the fire hydrant.","reasoning":"A fire hydrant is present on the site, making this item applicable. The specific 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to the fire hydrant (per Reviewer Convention) cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or distance measurements on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to the private fire hydrant location shown on Sheet 10"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant is shown on site. Submit clearance dimension from nearest transformer pad to fire hydrant, demonstrating minimum 5-foot separation per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows tree locations and plant symbols but does not provide a species list cross-referenced with ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) designation. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer locations but provides no dimension lines showing distances to trees. Trees are referenced in Sheets 33 and 34 (Canopy Impact and Root Zone exhibits) relative to one transformer.","reasoning":"Trees are present on the site and some are near transformer locations (evidenced by tree impact sheets 33 & 34 showing a transformer relative to Tree 4034). However, the submitted landscape plan does not include a species list with ECM Appendix F utility compatibility ratings. Without this species identification and utility compatibility confirmation, compliance cannot be verified. The lateral distances from trees to transformer pads are also not dimensioned.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (tree locations shown on Sheets 31, 33, 34)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":33},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":34}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree locations are shown on landscape plan but species are not identified with ECM Appendix F utility compatibility ratings. Submit tree species list with ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) designations for all trees within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads or 15 lateral feet of overhead electric conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows landscape plantings with keynote symbols (H.4 for parking lot landscaping, H.5 for common open space, etc.) and general planting locations. However, no dimension lines or distance callouts show the clearance from shrubs or vegetation to transformer pad access doors or sides. No callout identifies which transformer pad sides are access door sides versus non-access sides.","reasoning":"Landscaping is present on the site, making this item applicable. The specific clearance distances required (10 lateral feet from access door side, 5 lateral feet from other sides) cannot be verified without: (1) clear identification of transformer access door orientation on each pad, and (2) dimensioned separations from plantings to each pad side.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscaping locations relative to all four transformer pads shown on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscaping is shown on site but clearance dimensions from plantings to transformer pads are not provided. Submit detailed planting plan with dimensions showing: (1) minimum 10 lateral feet clearance from shrubs/vegetation to transformer access door side, and (2) minimum 5 lateral feet clearance from other sides, per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 33 and 34 (tree impact exhibits) show trees near proposed construction including reference to a transformer relative to Tree 4034. However, no root barrier specifications or detail drawings are provided on the landscape plan sheets or detail sheets. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) does not show root barrier callouts or dimensions near transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Trees are present within 20 lateral feet of transformer equipment (evidenced by tree impact sheets showing Tree 4034 relative to a transformer). The requirement for 4-foot deep root barriers installed 5 feet from equipment cannot be verified because no root barrier details, specifications, or construction drawings are provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, particularly Tree 4034 relative to transformer on Sheets 33-34"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":33},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":34},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformers are not documented with root barrier details. Submit landscape detail sheets showing root barrier specifications (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment) for all trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows building and parking area layouts. No dumpsters or waste enclosures are shown or labeled on any site plan sheet. No dimension lines or distance callouts from transformer pads to potential dumpster locations are provided.","reasoning":"Dumpster locations are not shown on the submitted site plan. Without documentation of whether dumpsters are present or their locations, the 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if dumpsters are present (not shown on submitted plans)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dumpster or waste enclosure locations are not shown on submitted site plan. If dumpsters are proposed, submit site plan showing dumpster locations with dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows parking area layouts and notes that 41 bicycle parking spaces are provided (39 long-term, 2 short-term) per the parking data table. However, specific locations of bike racks are not clearly marked or dimensioned on the sheet. No distance callouts show clearance from transformer pads to bike rack locations.","reasoning":"Bicycle parking is provided on the site, and one detail (Sheet 22) references bicycle rack specifications. However, the specific locations of bike racks relative to transformer pads are not documented with dimension callouts or distance measurements on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bicycle parking locations relative to transformer pads (if adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bicycle parking is noted on site plan but specific rack locations relative to transformer pads are not dimensioned. Submit clarification of bike rack locations with dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows site layout but does not identify light pole locations. Sheet 2 (Plat) and other sheets do not show detailed lighting or photometric plans. No dimension lines or distance callouts show clearance from transformer pads to any light poles.","reasoning":"Light pole locations adjacent to transformer pads are not shown or dimensioned on the submitted site plan sheets. A photometric or lighting plan sheet is not included in the site plan set. Without this documentation, the 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if light poles are located adjacent to transformer pads (not shown)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations are not shown on site plan. If light poles are proposed adjacent to transformer pads, submit photometric plan with dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot clearance per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows fire lanes and fire zone designations with notes and a standard detail for fire zone signage. However, specific fire lane locations are not dimensioned or clearly marked relative to transformer pad locations on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan). No distance callouts show clearance between transformer pads and fire lane boundaries.","reasoning":"Fire lanes are designated on the site per Sheet 10. However, the specific 15-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to fire lane boundaries (per Reviewer Convention) cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or distance measurements showing the clearance from each transformer pad to the nearest fire lane.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to designated fire lanes shown on Sheet 10"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes are shown on site plan. Submit clearance dimensions from transformer pads to fire lane boundaries, demonstrating minimum 15-foot separation per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' with no specific dimensions or markings. The vision analysis identified four separate pads but provided no distance callouts between them. No dimension lines show clearance from one pad to another.","reasoning":"Multiple transformer pads are present (four shown on Sheet 21), making this item applicable. However, the specific 5-foot minimum clearance from one transformer pad to another (per Reviewer Convention) cannot be verified without distance measurements between all pads.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations on Sheet 21 relative to each other"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple transformer pads are shown on site. Submit dimensions showing minimum 5-foot clearance between all transformer pads per Reviewer Convention."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water line routing and connections. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations. However, no distance dimensions or callouts show the clearance between transformer pads and water lines. The utility plan shows water routing but does not provide measured separation distances to electrical equipment.","reasoning":"Water lines are present on the site (shown on Sheet 19). The specific 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance from transformer pads to water lines (per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2) cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or distance measurements showing the separation between water lines and each transformer pad location.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to water service lines shown on Sheet 19"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plan. Submit clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot horizontal separation from transformer pads to water lines per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows wastewater service connections and routing. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations. However, no distance dimensions or callouts show the clearance between transformer pads and wastewater lines. The utility plan does not provide measured separation distances from electrical equipment to wastewater infrastructure.","reasoning":"Wastewater lines are present on the site (shown on Sheet 19). The specific 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance from transformer pads to wastewater lines (per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2) cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or distance measurements.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to wastewater service lines shown on Sheet 19"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on utility plan. Submit clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot horizontal separation from transformer pads to wastewater lines per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 12 (Storm Sewer Plan) and Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) show storm drain routing and infrastructure. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations. However, no distance dimensions or callouts show the clearance between transformer pads and storm drain lines. The utility plans do not provide measured separation distances to electrical equipment.","reasoning":"Storm drain lines are present on the site (shown on Sheets 12 and 19). The specific 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines (per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2) cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts or distance measurements.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to storm drain infrastructure shown on Sheets 12 and 19"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain infrastructure is shown on utility plans. Submit clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot horizontal separation from transformer pads to storm drain lines per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The facts.md and project documents indicate that this site is served by City of Austin water and wastewater utilities. No gas service is indicated as proposed for the project on any sheet. Gas meters or gas line routing are not shown on the site plan sheets.","reasoning":"This item applies only when gas service is present on the site. The project specifications (Sheet 3 - General Notes) reference water and wastewater service by City of Austin but do not mention gas service. No gas infrastructure is shown on any submitted sheet.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if gas service is present (not shown as proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 (Utility Tap Plan) and other utility sheets show water, wastewater, and storm drain infrastructure. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations. However, no distance dimensions or callouts show the specific 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities (conduits, communications, etc.). The utility plans do not provide measured separations from electrical equipment to these facilities.","reasoning":"Multiple underground utilities are present on the site. The specific 12-inch horizontal and vertical minimum clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, steam) per UCM § 1.10.5.A cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts showing these close-proximity separations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to all underground utilities shown on Sheets 19 and other utility plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utility routing is shown on utility plans but clearance dimensions from transformer pads are not provided. Submit clearance dimensions demonstrating minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical separation from transformer pads to other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, steam) per UCM § 1.10.5.A."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 (Utility Tap Plan) and 21 (Electrical Plan) are provided. Sheet 19 shows water and wastewater service routing; Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. However, no cross-section drawings or profile views show the relative vertical position of transformer pads and underground utilities. No documentation indicates whether transformers or AE underground facilities pass over/under other utility lines, or whether customer buildings/foundations/structures are installed over AE underground facilities.","reasoning":"The requirement to verify that transformer pads or AE underground facilities are not located over/under other utility lines, and that customer structures are not placed over AE facilities, requires cross-section or profile documentation showing vertical relationships. The submitted plans provide plan views only, lacking the three-dimensional clarity needed to confirm these conditions.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and AE underground facility routing relative to all other utilities shown on Sheets 19, 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical relationships between transformer pads, AE facilities, and other utilities are not provided. Submit utility cross-sections demonstrating that transformer pads and AE underground facilities do not cross over/under other utility lines, and that buildings/foundations are not constructed over AE facilities, per UCM § 1.10.5.B."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of the facts.md, sheet index (README.md), and site plan sheets (9, 21) shows no overhead distribution lines proposed or existing on the site. Sheet 3 references electric transmission line clearances (for lines running through or near the site), but no actual overhead electric distribution infrastructure is depicted adjacent to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This item applies only when overhead distribution lines are present. The project appears to utilize underground electric service (evidenced by the underground transformer pads and lack of any pole-mounted equipment shown). No overhead distribution conductors are depicted on the site plan sheets.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if overhead distribution lines are present (not shown on site)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets shows no overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors depicted adjacent to transformer locations. The site plan shows underground electric service with pad-mounted transformers. No aerial electric lines are shown on any site plan sheet.","reasoning":"This item applies only when overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are present. The submitted site plan does not show overhead distribution conductors on the property.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if overhead distribution primary/neutral conductors are present (not shown)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows one transformer location labeled with a 'Vault Easement' (southwest pad near Bldg 8), which may indicate a specialized configuration. However, no detail drawings, cross-section views, or niche specifications are provided. No documentation of 35-foot vertical clearance inside the niche or entrance is provided.","reasoning":"One transformer pad is marked as a 'Vault Easement,' which may suggest a vault or enclosed configuration. However, without cross-section drawings, niche detail sheets, or explicit clearance documentation, the 35-foot minimum vertical clearance requirement (UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3) cannot be verified. A 'Vault Easement' label alone does not provide sufficient detail to confirm compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Vault transformer near Bldg 8 (southwest pad with 'Vault Easement' label on Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One transformer is labeled as a vault configuration ('Vault Easement'). If this is a niche service installation, submit cross-section drawings demonstrating minimum 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche and niche entrance per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows one transformer labeled 'Vault Easement' (near Bldg 8) which may indicate a specialized configuration. However, no architectural specifications documenting 3-hour fire wall ratings are provided. No notes or documentation indicate consultation with Austin Energy Design business unit for niche service. No ventilation specifications are included.","reasoning":"If the 'Vault Easement' transformer is indeed a niche service installation (equipment within building footprint, accessible from outside), then architectural specifications for 3-hour fire walls, ventilation documentation, and Austin Energy Design coordination are required per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3. These documents are not provided in the submittal.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Vault transformer near Bldg 8 if configured as niche service (not fully documented as such)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If the vault transformer is a niche service installation, submit: (1) architectural specifications documenting 3-hour fire wall ratings, (2) ventilation specifications, and (3) evidence of consultation with Austin Energy Design business unit per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations at ground level. Sheets 9 and 11 (Site Plan and Grading Plan) show site topography and building footprints. However, no cross-section or profile drawings are provided showing vertical clearances at transformer locations relative to overhead structures, parking garage roofs, or enclosed areas. No vertical clearance documentation exists.","reasoning":"While buildings with various FFEs are shown on the site, cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearances in access paths above transformer locations are not provided. Without these drawings, the specific vertical clearance requirements (whether for overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas) cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["Vertical clearance paths above all transformer locations shown on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances at transformer locations are not provided. If overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas exist above transformer access paths, submit cross-section drawings demonstrating adequate vertical clearance per UCM § 1.10.3 as required by Austin Energy Design."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows site topography and grading with contour lines and spot elevations. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pad locations. However, no specific notation indicates whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type. The grading plan does not include a note or arrow showing drainage direction away from transformer pad locations. No callouts document that liquid flow is directed away from buildings.","reasoning":"The requirement to ensure drainage flows away from buildings for oil-filled transformer equipment (UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1) cannot be verified because: (1) transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified, and (2) no explicit notation on the grading plan shows drainage direction around transformer locations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Grading around all transformer pad locations on Sheet 11"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. If oil-filled transformers are proposed, submit grading plan notes and arrow callouts demonstrating that surface drainage flows away from transformer pads and building structures per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 (Plat) shows property boundaries. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations within the site boundary. Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows the site layout relative to property lines. However, no dimension callouts or property boundary overlay on the electrical plan verify that all transformer pads are 100% on private property and not straddling property lines.","reasoning":"While the transformer pads appear to be located within the site boundary based on visual inspection of Sheet 21 relative to Sheet 2, no explicit dimensioning or callouts verify that transformer pads are 100% on private property and not in the public right-of-way. The requirement (UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4) requires explicit confirmation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations on Sheet 21 relative to property boundaries shown on Sheet 2"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad property location is not explicitly documented. Submit plan sheets with dimension callouts confirming all transformer pads are located 100% on private property and do not straddle property lines per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 2, 9, and 11 show various easements including drainage, wastewater, and electric easements. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. One transformer (near Bldg 8) is labeled with 'Vault Easement.' However, no explicit note or callout states whether transformer pads are located within drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements, or whether Austin Energy Design written approval has been obtained if they are.","reasoning":"The requirement that transformer pads cannot be located in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, electrical) without AE Design written approval (UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4) cannot be verified without: (1) explicit identification of which easements, if any, underlie each transformer pad location, and (2) documentation of any required AE Design approvals.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to easements shown on Sheets 2, 9, 11"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations relative to easements are not explicitly documented. Submit plan sheets with notes identifying whether any transformer pads are located in drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements, and provide Austin Energy Design written approval if required per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"One transformer pad (near Bldg 8) is labeled as being within a 'Vault Easement' on Sheet 21. However, no transformer easement is explicitly drawn around the other three transformer pads shown on Sheet 21. No easement dimensions, boundaries, or access specifications are provided for any of the transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement for transformer easements around pads with adequate width for Austin Energy accessibility (UCM § 1.10.3) cannot be verified because: (1) only one easement ('Vault Easement') is labeled for one pad, and (2) no easement boundaries, dimensions, or accessibility requirements are documented for any of the four pads.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not documented for most pads (only one 'Vault Easement' is labeled). Submit plat or easement exhibit showing transformer easement boundaries around all four pads with dimensions sufficient for Austin Energy accessibility per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer locations and electrical routing to meters and buildings. However, no explicit note or dimension callout indicates that all electrical routing from transformers to meters is 100% on private property. No property boundary overlay or dimension verification is provided showing the routing remains outside public right-of-way.","reasoning":"The requirement that electrical routing from transformer to meter must be 100% on private property (UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4) cannot be verified without explicit documentation identifying the routing path and confirming it does not cross public right-of-way or easements not controlled by the applicant.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from all transformer locations to respective meter locations on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing property boundaries are not documented. Submit plan sheets with notes and dimension callouts confirming all electrical routing from transformers to meters is 100% on private property per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations on the site. No dimensions (width x depth) are labeled for any of the pads. No reference to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets is provided. No service type specification (single-phase vs. three-phase) is documented. The submission does not include AE Design pad detail drawings matching the proposed equipment.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require that transformer pad dimensions match Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets specific to the service type. The submitted electrical plan shows transformer pad locations only, with no detailed dimensions or reference to AE Design detail sheets. This is a required submission element that is missing from the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations shown on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad detail sheets matching Austin Energy Design specifications are not provided. Submit AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets for each pad showing: (1) service type (single-phase or three-phase), (2) pad dimensions (width x depth), (3) equipment specifications, and (4) any special installation requirements per UCM § 1.5.2.6."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows parking layout with driveways and parking areas. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows four transformer pad locations. Vision analysis identified that two pads (between Bldgs 5 & 6 and near Bldg 7) have four small circles marked, suggesting bollards. However, no dimension callouts show whether these pads are within 4 feet of parking areas, and no bollard specifications (4-inch diameter, galvanized, rigid metal, spacing for door opening) are provided.","reasoning":"While bollards appear to be shown on two pads, verification that they meet the 4-inch minimum diameter specification per AE Design equipment pad details cannot be made without explicit specifications. Additionally, whether the other two pads are within 4 feet of parking/vehicle circulation areas cannot be determined without dimension callouts. The grouping notes that bollards must be spaced to allow equipment door opening, which is not documented.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations relative to parking areas, drive aisles, and vehicle circulation on Sheets 9 and 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bollard specifications and clearance determinations are not provided. For all transformer pads within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle circulation routes, submit: (1) dimension callouts confirming distances to parking/circulation areas, and (2) bollard detail sheets showing 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts with spacing that allows equipment access door opening per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheets 9, 21) shows underground electrical service with pad-mounted transformers. No overhead distribution facilities are depicted on any site plan sheet. No poles or aerial conductors are shown.","reasoning":"This item applies only when overhead distribution facilities exist on the property. The submitted site plan shows underground electrical service exclusively. No customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, tanks) are proposed to be installed under or over non-existent overhead distribution facilities.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Only applicable if overhead distribution facilities are present (not shown on site)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a136e13c-2680-4375-811f-a5416413e77d","uuid":"e14261f5-b946-4d98-8a59-7dc9f7350942"}
