{"level":30,"time":1778187890433,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2401HBC2B4V3Z3X8K9B8CC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0123eAekuiRUUL6p82m8GYpn","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings (Bldg 1-8) and existing overhead electric line along southern boundary (Sheet 4, Sheet 31). Building locations are set back from the OHE line approximately 100+ feet to the north.","reasoning":"While buildings are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist on the site, no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions are provided. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified from plan view alone without elevation data showing the conductor location and building face clearance. The spatial separation visible on the plan view is sufficient distance, but the requirement is specific about demonstrating clearances from the 'outside conductor' and requires professional verification.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations 1-8 relative to OHE line at southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and labeled clearance dimensions are required to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead distribution lines are confirmed on site plan (Sheets 4, 31). The OHE line is shown with dashes and 'OHE' notation. Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service with transformers and pull boxes, indicating underground distribution to buildings.","reasoning":"The site appears to have existing overhead distribution primary lines (not transmission lines, as voltage not specified but typical for urban Austin is 12.47kV or 34.5kV distribution). Customer facilities (buildings) are proposed but no dimensional clearance verification from outside conductor is shown. The code requires 15-foot radial clearance measured in all directions from the outside conductor, which requires explicit dimensional documentation in plan and section views. Spatial separation visible on plan view is insufficient without precise dimensional verification from the outer conductor location.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations 1-8 relative to existing overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimension lines showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to all customer facilities must be provided on site plan and section views."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevation sheets are not included in the submitted site plan set (39 sheets reviewed; no building elevation documents found). Sheet 9 shows buildings in plan view only without elevation or projection details.","reasoning":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks) are standard features of residential buildings but cannot be assessed without building elevation sheets. The overhead electric facilities exist (confirmed on Sheets 4, 31), but without elevation documentation showing the three-dimensional relationships between conductor location and building projections, compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections on all 8 proposed buildings relative to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets showing all building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) with dimensions and clearance verification from overhead electric conductors are required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review of all sheets (1-39) and supplementary documents found no gas pump canopies proposed or shown on the site plan.","reasoning":"No gas pump canopies are included in the proposed site development. This is a residential multi-family townhomes project with no fuel service facilities proposed. The triggering condition (gas pump canopies) does not exist.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan sheets reviewed (9, 11, 15-17, 31, 38-39) show buildings, driveways, sidewalks, parking areas, and retaining walls. No elevated walkways, elevated platforms, or elevated structures (beyond standard building structures addressed separately) are proposed.","reasoning":"The proposed site improvements consist of ground-level or building-level features. While concrete sidewalks and pedestrian walkways are proposed, these are ground-level, not elevated structures requiring radial clearance from overhead distribution facilities. No elevated walkways or platforms separate from the buildings are shown on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document indicates Valley View Road is a Local Street (ASMP Level 1), ROW classification 2U-OP. The site is adjacent to ROW. Sheet 4 and facts document show 5' electric easements dedicated in the Mecey Subdivision plat. Electric facilities exist in or near ROW adjacent to site.","reasoning":"Building setback from ROW and electric facility locations/relocation notes are not clearly documented with clearance dimensions. The code requires buildings to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance and 15-foot radial clearance from any overhead electric facilities in ROW adjacent to the site. Without elevation views showing the relationship between building faces and overhead facilities in the ROW, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to Valley View Road ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations with labeled clearance dimensions from overhead electric facilities in adjacent ROW must be provided, demonstrating both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet site plan package. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows buildings in plan view only. Overhead electric facilities are confirmed to exist on property (Sheets 4, 31) with poles and conductors shown.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires building elevation sheets to include surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimension annotations. This is a fundamental documentation requirement when buildings or elevated structures are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. The absence of elevation sheets means the surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance verification do not exist in the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings 1-8 relative to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets must be submitted, including registered surveyor data showing surveyed conductor elevation and clearance dimension annotations for all buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review reveals no section or plan view exhibits with dimension lines from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings or building projections. Sheet 9 shows plan view only; no section callouts reference building clearance details.","reasoning":"The code requires explicit dimensional documentation from the outside conductor (not pole center) to the outermost building edge. This is the primary method for verifying compliance. The absence of these dimensions across all submitted sheets (verified through review of Sheets 1-39) means the clearance verification requirement is not satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings 1-8 and any building projections"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits must be added showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of each building and building projection for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3. Dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor location, not pole center."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows property fencing and enclosure systems. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) shows retaining walls; Sheet 9 shows wooden privacy fences per legend key note H.6. However, no traditional fences (temporary or permanent barriers separate from retaining walls) are explicitly proposed in relation to overhead electric conductor locations visible on the plan.","reasoning":"While fencing exists on the site (privacy fences, retaining walls), they do not appear to be positioned directly under or in the immediate proximity of the OHE line shown on Sheet 31. The OHE line runs along the southern boundary where the driveway and parking area are located. No fences appear to be proposed directly beneath this line based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing power poles are shown on Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) at the southern and eastern boundaries. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed fence locations (wooden privacy fences, per legend). Horizontal distances between proposed fence posts and existing electric poles are not dimensionally labeled.","reasoning":"The reviewer convention requires 10-foot horizontal clearance from fence posts to overhead electric poles. Plan view provides general layout but lacks specific dimensional callouts for fence post locations relative to pole centers. Without explicit dimension annotations, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed fence locations relative to existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dimension annotations must be provided showing fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document identifies electric easements but no Austin Energy substation is noted on the property or in the immediate adjacency description. Site plan review (Sheets 1-39) finds no substation enclosures or transformer vaults identified as substations.","reasoning":"This item applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation infrastructure is documented on the site plan or in the project facts.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) shown or referenced on property. Existing overhead electric facilities are distribution lines (typical Austin distribution 12.47kV or 34.5kV). No transmission easements or transmission structures are documented.","reasoning":"This item applies only to fencing beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV). No transmission facilities are present on the property based on available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed fencing (wooden privacy fences per Sheet 9 legend, retaining walls per Sheet 38). The vehicle barrier/fence locations visible on Sheet 9 do not appear to be positioned directly beneath the OHE line visible on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The item applies when vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines with clearance verification needed. While the site has both fencing and overhead lines, the fencing does not appear to be positioned directly beneath the OHE line based on plan view analysis.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 shows retaining walls up to 14 feet in height planned for the site. Overhead electric line is shown on Sheets 4 and 31 running along southern boundary. Retaining walls shown on Sheet 38 plan view are in the northeast and central areas, but horizontal relationship to OHE line not explicitly dimensioned.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement applies to retaining walls near overhead facilities. Without section views showing wall face elevations and dimension lines to the outer electric conductor, compliance cannot be verified. Plan view alone does not provide sufficient evidence of either compliance or non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls in relation to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views showing retaining wall elevations with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall must be provided to demonstrate compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no Austin Energy substation on the property or identified in adjacency materials. Retaining walls are proposed but not near any substation property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property (within 10 feet of substation boundary) requiring 5-foot separation. No substation is identified in project documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review of all sheets finds no emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms proposed for the project. The site consists of buildings, driveways, parking, sidewalks, and landscaping only.","reasoning":"The item applies only when emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed near overhead facilities. No such structures are included in the proposed development.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are shown on Sheet 38. Overhead electric facilities are shown on Sheets 4 and 31. No section views with clearance dimensions from outer conductor to wall face are provided anywhere in the 39-sheet plan set.","reasoning":"Section exhibits showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining walls are required for clearance verification. The absence of these sections means compliance cannot be determined from available documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views for retaining walls must be provided showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to wall face for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) clearly shows overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' running horizontally along the southern boundary, and vision analysis confirms it crosses directly over the main driveway entrance (southwest portion of site). No vertical clearance height is labeled at this crossing point. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) provides finished elevations for buildings but no overhead line elevations or mid-span clearance data are shown.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 16-foot vertical clearance for driveways without truck traffic, 18-foot for areas with truck traffic. The site plan clearly shows the OHE crossing the driveway without any clearance dimension labeled. This is a critical documentation gap: without surveyed conductor elevation and finished driveway grade elevations showing the clearance distance, the requirement cannot be verified. The absence of these essential dimensions constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Main driveway entrance at southwest portion of site where OHE line crosses"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions must be provided for the driveway where the OHE line crosses, showing minimum 16-foot or 18-foot clearance from the lowest point of the overhead electric line (including any attachments) to the finished driveway grade. Registered surveyor data for mid-span clearance verification is required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows parking areas on the site, primarily in the central and southern portions. The OHE line runs along the southern boundary. Vertical relationship between parking surface elevation and overhead line is not documented with dimension annotations.","reasoning":"The item applies when vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. While parking exists and overhead lines are present on the site, the vertical clearance requirement cannot be determined without elevation documentation showing the finished pad grade and overhead line height with dimension callouts.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Parking areas in proximity to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If parking or vehicle display areas are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, section views with labeled vertical clearance dimensions must be provided to demonstrate the required clearance (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet for parking without trucks, 18 feet with truck traffic)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) on the property. Existing overhead facilities are distribution-level (typical 12.47kV or 34.5kV for Austin urban areas). No transmission easements or transmission structures identified.","reasoning":"This item applies only when roads or driveways are regraded beneath electric transmission lines (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV). No transmission facilities are documented as existing on the property.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No highway or freeway construction is proposed on this multi-family residential site. The project is limited to local streets and driveways for a 39-unit townhomes development on Valley View Road (a local street, ASMP Level 1).","reasoning":"This item applies only to highway/freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures. The project scope does not include highway or freeway work.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and existing conditions (Sheet 4) show existing electric poles at the property boundary, not within the proposed driveway footprints shown on Sheet 9.","reasoning":"This item applies when proposed driveways are shown in conflict with or immediately adjacent (within 30 feet) to existing electric pole locations. The existing poles appear to be located along the property boundary, not in direct conflict with the proposed internal driveway system based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Extensive review of all 39 site plan sheets and supporting documents reveals that where clearance dimensions are shown anywhere on the plans (limited clearance callouts exist for other utilities like water, sewer), they do not demonstrate measurement from the 'outside conductor' or 'outermost electric line' as required by code. More critically, no clearance dimensions FROM overhead electric conductors TO buildings or site features are shown at all.","reasoning":"The grouping guidance specifically warns that 'Clearances measured from utility pole or centerline instead of from outside conductor' is a common violation pattern. A review of all dimension annotations on Sheets 1-39 shows no instances of dimensions explicitly originating from a conductor location. The required methodology—measuring from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from pole centerline or centerline of three-phase lines—is not documented anywhere on the plans. This is a systematic deficiency in all clearance documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All clearance dimensions on site plan where overhead electric facilities exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All clearance dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from pole center or centerline of multi-conductor installations. On three-phase installations, the conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension line endpoints must clearly show measurement origin at the conductor location."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed site lighting fixtures. Sheet 9 includes lighting note requiring full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5. No streetlight poles are shown as proposed on the site plan.","reasoning":"The item applies when new streetlight poles are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. The site has lighting fixtures on buildings and in landscaping areas, but no proposed streetlight poles (separate free-standing light poles in the public right-of-way) are documented on the site plan.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows sidewalks and pedestrian pathways throughout the site. Existing power poles are shown on Sheets 4 and 31 at property boundaries. The site plan does not explicitly show sidewalk alignment clearance from existing power poles at the property line/ROW frontage on Valley View Road.","reasoning":"The item applies when new or modified sidewalks are proposed and existing power poles are located within or immediately adjacent to the sidewalk alignment at property ends along ROW. While sidewalks are proposed and poles exist at the boundary, the specific alignment clearance from poles at the property limits is not dimensionally documented.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk alignment along Valley View Road ROW frontage near existing power poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If sidewalks are positioned at or near existing power pole locations at the property boundary along ROW, clearance dimensions must be provided showing sidewalk alignment and pole location."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows trash collection notes and site plan includes trash enclosure areas. The trash enclosure locations are shown in the building areas, not beneath the OHE line visible on Sheet 31 running along the southern boundary.","reasoning":"The item applies when trash enclosures or receptacle locations are shown beneath overhead electric facilities. While the site has trash management areas, they do not appear to be positioned directly beneath the overhead electric line based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead distribution electric line is confirmed on Sheets 4, 31 running along southern boundary of site. Trees are shown on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) positioned at and overlapping the OHE line marking on the southern property boundary. Electric easement exhibit and site plan show the OHE facility location.","reasoning":"The code absolutely prohibits customer facilities (including landscaping features) from being installed under or over overhead distribution facilities, separate from and distinct from the clearance distance requirements. The vision analysis of Sheet 31 explicitly noted trees 'directly adjacent to, and in some cases overlapping, the OHE line.' This positioning violates the prohibition regardless of whether clearances otherwise might be maintained. The deficiency is the placement of landscape features at or overlapping the overhead line location itself, not merely insufficient clearance distance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Trees on Landscape Plan Sheet 31 at southern property boundary where OHE line exists"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and other landscape features are shown positioned at or overlapping the overhead electric line on Sheet 31, violating the prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. All landscape features within the electric easement must maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from the outside conductor. Trees positioned directly beneath the line must be relocated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21) shows domestic water branches connecting to buildings via 2\" HDPE service tubing. No water meter locations are explicitly dimensioned on the utility plan in relation to the OHE service drop line that may exist on the property.","reasoning":"The item applies when water meter locations are shown and overhead electric service-drop conductors (secondary voltage service lines from utility infrastructure to customer service point) exist on site. While water service is proposed, specific water meter locations relative to any overhead service drop are not clearly documented on the plans reviewed, and the OHE line shown on Sheets 4 and 31 appears to be distribution-level, not a service drop.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows new water line routing through the site. Overhead electric facilities (distribution lines) are shown on Sheets 4 and 31. The spatial relationship between underground water line routing and overhead electric pole/conductor locations is not explicitly dimensioned.","reasoning":"The item applies when new water lines are shown beneath or adjacent to overhead electrical distribution facilities. While both water lines and overhead lines exist on the site, the clearance dimensions or separation distances between them are not documented with explicit callouts on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing relative to overhead distribution poles and conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions must be provided showing water line routing maintains adequate separation from overhead distribution poles and conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows building foundations and setbacks. Facts document indicates Valley View Road frontage with proposed buildings. Electric facilities are documented as existing in ROW via dedicated easements noted in facts document and on Sheet 4.","reasoning":"The item applies when permanent structure foundations are within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities exist or are planned in adjacent ROW. While the spatial relationships are shown in plan view, specific dimension verification of foundation clearance from property line is not explicitly documented, making definitive assessment difficult from plan view alone.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations near property line adjacent to Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If any building foundations are located within 5 feet of the property line, detailed dimensions showing clearance space for electric facility access and maintenance must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line is confirmed crossing the main driveway (Sheet 9, vision analysis). The driveway finished grade elevation is shown on Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) at approximately 680-682 feet. No registered surveyor data for overhead conductor elevations or mid-span clearance measurements are provided anywhere in the 39-sheet plan set or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"The code requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance data when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements. The driveway clearance is marginal based on available information (no conductor height documented), making this a condition where surveyor verification would be required. The complete absence of surveyor clearance data constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway where OHE line crosses"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor data must be provided showing pole locations, overhead conductor elevations, and mid-span clearance measurements for the driveway crossing. This data is essential to verify the minimum 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.6.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No new overhead electric lines are being constructed by the applicant on this project. The site plan shows existing overhead lines to be maintained in place.","reasoning":"This item applies only when new overhead electric lines are being constructed and cross roadways. The project involves repositioning and managing existing facilities, not constructing new overhead lines.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows underground electrical service for the proposed buildings with transformers and pull boxes. No overhead secondary or primary lines are being installed by the applicant.","reasoning":"This item applies only when secondary overhead lines are constructed crossing over primary overhead lines. The project does not propose new overhead electrical infrastructure.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheets 9, 31, 35) shows landscape features and building signage plans. No marquee signs are identified or proposed on the project site plan.","reasoning":"Marquee signs are large illuminated sign structures typically associated with commercial entertainment or hospitality uses. This is a multi-family residential project with no marquee sign features proposed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical service with pull boxes and transformers. No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed on the site plan.","reasoning":"The item applies when new poles are proposed for underground service conversion (typically replacing existing poles with new ones during conversion work). This project is transitioning to underground service but the site plan does not show new pole installations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows site lighting requirements for full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5. Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows various landscape and lighting features. Overhead electric line is shown on Sheet 31 running along the southern boundary. No specific decorative light fixture locations or clearance dimensions from the OHE line are documented.","reasoning":"The item applies when decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. While site lighting is planned and overhead lines exist, the specific positioning of decorative light fixtures in relation to the OHE line is not explicitly documented with clearance verification.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixture locations near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If decorative lighting fixtures are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, clearance dimensions must be provided showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from the outside conductor, or alternative relocation notes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31, vision analysis) shows trees 'directly adjacent to, and in some cases overlapping, the OHE line' along the southern property boundary. Plant lists (Sheet 35, vision analysis) specify proposed tree species: Live Oak (2), Cedar Elm (10), Texas Mountain Laurel (2), Mexican Redbud (6). None of these species are marked or identified as 'utility-compatible' (UC) per ECM Appendix F. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are large trees with mature heights exceeding 20 feet, making them non-utility-compatible. No notation or schedule marking indicates UC designation for any proposed species.","reasoning":"The code (ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4) requires trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors and 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors to be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC', generally mature height ≤20 feet). The trees shown on Sheet 31 in or near the OHE line location are not documented as utility-compatible. Cedar Elm and Live Oak specifically are NOT utility-compatible due to large mature size. This is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees planted at southern property boundary near OHE line (Landscape Plan Sheet 31)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC'). The currently proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are not utility-compatible. Trees must either be relocated to positions more than 10 feet from conductors, or replaced with utility-compatible species verified in ECM Appendix F 'UC' column."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows electrical meters and transformers placed at specific locations on the site plan. No enlarged detail sheets showing meter area layouts with access clearances are provided.","reasoning":"The item applies when electric meter locations are shown on plans. The code requires 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom for meter access and installation (UCM § 1.10.9). Without detailed enlarged drawings of meter installation areas, it cannot be determined whether site features (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, building projections) obstruct these required clearances.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical meter locations shown on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Enlarged detail drawings of proposed meter locations must be provided showing no obstructions to meter access and working clearances: minimum 30 inches wide, 36 inches deep front access space, and 6.5 feet headroom per UCM § 1.10.9."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings and existing streetlight poles may be present along Valley View Road (adjacent public ROW). The clearance relationship between proposed buildings and existing streetlight poles is not explicitly documented with dimensions.","reasoning":"The item applies when new buildings or structures are proposed adjacent to existing streetlight poles. While the site abuts Valley View Road where streetlights may exist, the specific clearance relationship is not dimensionally documented on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near Valley View Road ROW where existing streetlights may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If existing streetlight poles are located near proposed buildings, clearance dimensions must be provided showing building location and pole proximity."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4, vision analysis) confirms existing power poles with at least one guy wire visible on the plan. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed driveways, sidewalks, and accessible routes. However, guy wire locations and accessible path alignments are not explicitly cross-referenced or dimensioned to show conflicts or clearances.","reasoning":"The item applies when down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible paths or driveways. The grouping guidance notes that 'electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.' While the survey shows at least one guy wire, the detailed conflict analysis between guy wire locations and proposed accessible routes/driveways is not documented. Without explicit dimension annotations or conflict resolution notes, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wire locations relative to proposed driveways and accessible paths"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wire locations and anchors must be clearly identified on the site plan relative to all proposed accessible paths and driveways. Any conflicts must be resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting steel poles, with details and relocation notes provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Easement exhibits (facts document, Sheet 4) reference plat-dedicated easements but no angled guy anchors or transmission structures with guy easement requirements are identified on the property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist or will exist on site. The property has distribution-level electric facilities, not transmission structures.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4, vision analysis) shows at least one existing power pole with a guy wire, indicating potential down guy anchors. Easement exhibit (facts document, Sheet 4) shows utility easements. However, dedicated easement boundaries for down guy anchors are not clearly identified with specific dimensions showing 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past ground entry.","reasoning":"The item applies when down guy anchors from distribution poles exist or will exist on site. While guy wires are shown on the survey, the specific easement documentation for these anchors (showing 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry per Austin Energy standards) is not visible in the submitted easement exhibits.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations identified on existing survey"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dedicated easements for down guy anchors must be clearly shown on the easement exhibit, displaying 10-foot width and minimum 5-foot extension past where the guy wire enters the ground, per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows pole-mounted and pad-mounted transformers. No overhead electric lines above these transformer locations are documented. The OHE line shown on Sheets 4 and 31 runs along the southern boundary, separate from transformer equipment locations.","reasoning":"This item applies when transformers are shown and overhead lines exist above or adjacent to them. The transformers on this site appear to be underground or pad-mounted in areas not directly beneath overhead distribution lines.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and electrical infrastructure. No niche service configurations (covered, recessed installations with overhead structures above equipment) are identified on the site plan.","reasoning":"This item applies only to transformers and switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). Standard pad-mounted or pole-mounted transformer installations do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Construction staging and sequence is referenced in general notes (Sheet 3, referenced in guide). Overhead electric line is confirmed on property (Sheets 4, 31). However, no site logistics plan, construction phasing plan, or staging area exhibit showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines is provided in the submitted 39 sheets or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"The code requires construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms to maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines during construction. This is separate from permanent clearance requirements and is a critical safety requirement for construction operations. The absence of a construction phasing/logistics plan with staging area boundaries documented against overhead line locations constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging and equipment operation zones relative to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A site logistics plan or construction phasing plan must be submitted showing staging areas, equipment laydown zones, crane swing radius, material storage, and scaffold locations, with explicit notation that all construction activities maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of cover sheet (Sheet 1), general notes (Sheet 3), and site plan release notes (Sheets 1, 9) finds no note stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. The required notation per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is absent.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires a plan note regarding the 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. This is a mandatory disclosure on construction documents when overhead electric facilities exist and construction activities are proposed. The complete absence of this note from all sheets is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A plan note must be added to the cover sheet or general notes stating: 'The owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevation sheets are not included in the submitted site plan set. Without elevation documentation, service-mast through-roof installations cannot be assessed. Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service distribution.","reasoning":"This item applies only when service-mast through-roof installations are shown on building elevations. No building elevation sheets are provided, and the electrical design appears to be underground distribution to the buildings, not overhead service masts.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","uuid":"ff7fd3ea-5fa5-4820-9566-d0002747f424"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187890472,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0123eAekuiRUUL6p82m8GYpn","type":"tool_result","content":"Structured output provided successfully"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","uuid":"5f3d4590-05d3-4fc0-832f-cf465aaef021","tool_use_result":"Structured output provided successfully"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187894411,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR23ZJ25B33PN92HS436T9F0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CF1RGtBjg6fjyhe4tGpi36","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing overhead utility poles with conductors are depicted on Sheet 4 (existing conditions survey) running around property boundaries, with OHE line marked on Sheet 9 southern boundary. Proposed Buildings 1-8 are shown on site plan with finished floor elevations ranging from 683.0 to 687.50 feet. However, no surveyed elevations or heights of existing overhead conductors are provided, no building elevation sheets exist showing conductor heights relative to building structures, and no dimension annotations on plans show clearance distances from conductors to any building faces or projections.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.3, buildings must maintain 7'6\" horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead conductors. The requirement is applicable because overhead conductors exist and buildings are proposed. However, the plans do not include surveyed conductor elevation data, building elevations, or clearance dimensions necessary to verify compliance. Without conductor elevations and building heights documented relative to the conductors, compliance cannot be assessed from the available documents.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed elevations of existing overhead conductors and building elevation drawings showing clearance dimensions are required to verify 7'6\" sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from conductors to building faces and projections."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE (overhead electric) line is labeled on Sheet 9 (site plan) along the southern boundary of the property. The legend on Sheet 4 indicates that utility poles and overhead lines are depicted. However, no documentation specifies whether the existing overhead infrastructure is distribution (voltage <60kV) or transmission (voltage ≥60kV), no conductor types are labeled as primary or neutral, and no plan or section views show dimensions from the outside conductor to any customer facilities or buildings indicating radial clearance distances.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors. The applicability depends on confirmation that the overhead facilities are distribution-voltage facilities and that customer facilities (buildings, etc.) are proposed. While customer facilities (buildings) are clearly proposed, the voltage classification of the existing overhead lines is not documented on the plans. Without specification of conductor type, voltage, and documented radial clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All customer facilities (buildings 1-8, parking, infrastructure) relative to OHE line on southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans must specify whether existing overhead lines are distribution primary/neutral conductors, and provide 15-foot radial clearance dimensions from outside conductor to all customer facilities in plan and section views."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevation sheets for the eight proposed buildings do not appear in the 39-sheet site plan set. Sheet 21 shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, meters) and building FFE data but not overhead conductor elevations or clearances. No section or elevation views are provided showing building projections (roofs, parapets, overhangs, canopies) relative to overhead conductor elevations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires building projections to maintain both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from conductors. While buildings are proposed and overhead lines exist on the property, building elevation or section drawings with surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance dimensions are required but not provided. The absence of these elevation sheets prevents verification of compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building roofs, parapets, overhangs, and projections on Buildings 1-8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and dimension annotations showing clearances from conductors to all building projections (roofs, parapets, overhangs, decks, patios) must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets (Sheet 9 site plan, Sheet 19 utility tap plan, Sheet 21 electrical design) shows no gas pump canopy or gas service infrastructure proposed on the site.","reasoning":"EL-1.4 applies only when gas pump canopies are proposed and overhead electric lines exist. No gas pumps or canopies are shown in the proposed site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply to this project.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows concrete sidewalks and decomposed granite walkways connecting buildings and the detention pond. Sheet 22 (Construction Details) shows standard sidewalk and pathway details. However, no section views or elevation drawings are provided showing whether any walkways or pathways include elevated platforms, elevated decks, or stairs that would be located near the overhead electric line running along the southern boundary, and no clearance dimensions from conductors to such features are documented.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires 15-foot radial clearance from distribution conductors for elevated walkways, stairs, and platforms. The applicability depends on whether any elevated features are actually proposed. While pathways are shown on the site plan, it is unclear whether any are elevated or whether they are near the overhead line. Without section views and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Elevated walkways, stairs, platforms near OHE line if any are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If any elevated walkways, stairs, or platforms are proposed, provide section views with dimension annotations showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) shows overhead utility poles and lines existing around the property perimeter, including near property boundaries and adjacent to Valley View Road (ROW). Proposed buildings are shown on Sheet 9, with setbacks from property lines. However, no Austin Energy utility plan or easement exhibit specifically identifying the location of electric facilities in the right-of-way is included in the site plan documentation. No elevation drawings show clearances from buildings to overhead facilities in the ROW.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires buildings to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from overhead facilities in adjacent ROW. While buildings are proposed and overhead poles exist near the ROW, the specific location of AE overhead facilities in the right-of-way and clearance documentation from buildings to those facilities are not provided on the submitted plans. A utility plan from Austin Energy showing the exact location of overhead infrastructure in the ROW would be needed to verify compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1, 2, and other structures near Valley View Road ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Austin Energy utility plan showing exact location of overhead facilities in adjacent ROW with clearance dimensions from buildings must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet site plan set. Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design) shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure and building FFE data but does not include surveyed overhead conductor elevations. No registered surveyor data showing mid-span clearances or overhead conductor elevation measurements are provided anywhere in the site plan or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors to be included on building elevation sheets when buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities. The requirement is applicable because buildings are proposed and overhead lines exist. However, building elevation sheets are not present in the submittal, making it impossible to verify whether this requirement is met.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets prepared by registered surveyor must include surveyed elevations and locations of existing overhead conductors with dimension annotations showing clearances to building components."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (site plan) shows OHE line on southern boundary and buildings in plan view, but contains no dimension annotations showing distances from conductors to building edges. No enlarged plan details or section view exhibits are provided on any construction detail sheets (22-28) showing dimensions from outer conductor to outermost edges of buildings or building projections. Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure only.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires section and plan view exhibits with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost building edges when buildings and projections are proposed within potential clearance distance. The requirement is applicable because buildings are proposed near overhead lines. However, the necessary dimension annotations and exhibits are not provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings and projections relative to OHE line on southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Provide enlarged plan details and section views with dimension lines extending from outside conductor to outermost edges of all buildings and building projections, demonstrating required clearance envelopes are maintained."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (site plan) shows wooden privacy fences along property boundaries (marked with 'X' symbols per key notes). Overhead electric line (OHE) is depicted on the southern boundary. However, no dimension annotations are provided on Sheet 9 or on any other sheets showing the horizontal distance from the fence to the overhead conductor. The vision analysis of Sheet 4 confirmed overhead poles at property corners, but the proposed site plan (Sheet 9) does not show these pole locations or clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires fences to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor. While fences are proposed and overhead facilities exist, the specific location of fence alignment relative to the conductor and documented clearance dimensions are not provided. Without dimension annotations measuring clearance from the conductor (not pole center) to the fence, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Privacy fences along southern property boundary near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plan must include dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from outside conductor to fence face, measured from conductor location not from pole centerline."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows proposed wooden privacy fences marked with 'X' symbols. Sheet 4 (existing conditions survey) shows utility poles at or near property corners (southwest, southeast, northwest, northeast). However, the proposed site plan (Sheet 9) does not clearly identify the locations of existing utility poles or show them with dimension annotations. No measurements are provided showing the distance from fence posts to the nearest utility pole locations.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires fence posts to maintain 10-foot horizontal clearance from overhead electric poles. While fences are proposed and poles exist on the property, the specific pole locations and fence post locations are not adequately documented on the proposed plans with dimension callouts. Without clear identification of pole locations and distance annotations, compliance cannot be verified from the available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence posts relative to utility poles at property corners"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan must clearly identify existing utility pole locations and provide dimension annotations showing minimum 10-foot clearance from fence posts to pole centerlines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), easement exhibits (Sheet 2), and utility plans shows no Austin Energy substation shown or noted on the property. Facts.md identifies only the biofiltration/detention pond, buildings, parking, and utilities but no substation facility.","reasoning":"EL-1.11 applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation is depicted on the site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply to this project.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and the site plan review show no transmission-voltage electric lines on or adjacent to the property. The existing overhead utilities are labeled as OHE (overhead electric) on the site plan but are not specified as transmission voltage (≥60kV) facilities. No 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV facilities are noted on any plans. The utility poles shown on Sheet 4 appear to be distribution-scale infrastructure typical of lower-voltage distribution lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 requirements for transmission line fencing apply only when fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV). No transmission facilities are identified on this site plan, therefore the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 9 (site plan) shows no vehicle barrier posts, vehicle barrier fencing, or protective bollards depicted beneath or immediately adjacent to the OHE line on the southern boundary. Parking areas are shown but with standard curb-mounted parking space markings, not vehicle barriers.","reasoning":"EL-1.13 applies only when vehicle barrier posts or fencing are proposed beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines. No such barriers are shown in the proposed site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) and Sheet 39 (Wall Plan Details and Notes) detail retaining walls for the biofiltration detention pond located in the northeast portion of the site. These walls are not located near the OHE line on the southern boundary. The vision analysis of Sheet 4 (existing survey) showed overhead utilities on the property perimeter but the precise location of the OHE line relative to the retaining wall locations on the northeast is not clearly specified. No section views showing vertical clearances from the outer electric line to the retaining wall faces are provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires retaining walls to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric facilities. While retaining walls are proposed, their proximity to overhead lines must be determined from plan geometry. The OHE line shown on Sheet 9 appears to run along the southern boundary, distant from the northeast retaining walls. However, without explicit dimension annotations or section views showing the clearance from the conductor to the wall, compliance cannot definitively be verified from the available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls around biofiltration pond if located near overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If retaining walls are located near overhead electric lines, provide section views with dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to wall face."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and the site plan review indicate no Austin Energy substation exists on or immediately adjacent to the property. The site shows proposed improvements but no substation facility structures are depicted on Sheet 9 or any utility sheets.","reasoning":"EL-1.15 applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No substation is shown on the site plans, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), drainage plans (Sheets 15-17), and construction details (Sheets 22-28) shows no emergency access bridges, elevated emergency platforms, or emergency escape structures proposed on the site. The site shows standard pedestrian walkways and driveways but no specialized emergency access structures.","reasoning":"EL-1.16 applies only when emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist. No such emergency access structures are shown in the proposed site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38-39 show retaining wall details and cross-sections for the biofiltration pond. However, these sections do not include dimensions from any overhead electric conductor to the outermost edge of the retaining wall faces. The existing overhead line (OHE) shown on the southern boundary is geographically distant from the northeast pond retaining walls, but explicit section exhibits with clearance dimensions are not provided to confirm separation.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires section exhibits showing dimensions from outer conductor to outermost wall edge when retaining walls are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead lines. While the pond walls appear to be distant from the OHE line based on plan view, documented section exhibits with conductor elevations and clearance dimensions would be needed to definitively verify compliance for any walls that might be affected.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls around biofiltration detention pond"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views for retaining walls near any overhead electric lines must include dimension annotations showing clearance from outside conductor to wall face."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows finished driveway grades across the site, ranging from approximately 678 to 688 feet. Sheet 9 shows the general driveway layout. OHE line exists on the southern boundary per Sheet 9 vision analysis. However, no surveyed mid-span clearance data is provided for the overhead line, and no section views or dimension annotations on Sheets 9, 11, or 22 show the vertical distance from the lowest point of the overhead electric facilities (including any attachments) to the finished driveway grades.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires 16-foot vertical clearance for parking without truck traffic, or 18-foot for areas with truck traffic, from lowest point of overhead facilities including telecommunications attachments. The requirement applies because driveways are proposed and overhead lines may cross or be adjacent to them. However, without registered surveyor mid-span clearance data and dimension callouts on grading or section views, compliance cannot be verified. Whether truck traffic is expected on the site access driveways also affects the applicable clearance height requirement.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and parking areas if located beneath or adjacent to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data must be provided showing vertical clearance from lowest point of overhead facilities (including all conductors and attachments) to finished driveway grades. Section views must show 16-foot clearance for parking without truck traffic or 18-foot for areas with truck traffic."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) shows 10 surface parking spaces and 78 garage parking spaces. The surface parking area does not appear to be located directly beneath the overhead electric line on the southern boundary based on the plan layout. Additionally, no separate vehicle display or vehicle storage area on concrete pads beneath overhead lines is shown on the site plan.","reasoning":"EL-1.19 applies only when vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. While parking exists on the site, the surface parking appears to be located away from the OHE line based on plan view, and no dedicated vehicle display area is shown. Without explicit indication that parking pads are located beneath overhead conductors, this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and site plan review show no transmission-voltage electric lines (≥60kV) on or crossing the property. The overhead utilities depicted are labeled OHE (overhead electric) at distribution voltage. No 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV transmission line is identified on any plans.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 requires 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to ground surface only when roads or driveways are proposed or regraded beneath electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV). No transmission facilities are shown on this project, therefore the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No highway or freeway is proposed or shown on the site plan. The site fronts Valley View Road which is classified as a Local Street (ASMP Street Level 1) per facts.md. No transmission structures with underbuilt distribution are depicted on the site.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 applies only to highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures. The project is a local residential development with no highway or freeway improvements proposed, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) shows utility poles at or near property corners. The proposed site plan (Sheet 9) shows internal driveway layout but does not clearly indicate whether any existing utility poles directly conflict with or are immediately adjacent to proposed driveway locations. Vision analysis confirmed poles are depicted on the existing survey but their final disposition (remain vs. relocate) relative to proposed driveways is not explicitly documented on the proposed site plans with dimension callouts or relocation notes.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires electric poles in conflict with proposed driveways to be relocated minimum 30 feet from driveway edge. While utility poles exist and driveways are proposed, the specific relationship between pole locations and driveway alignments, and whether relocation is needed, cannot be definitively determined from the available plan documentation without explicit distance annotations or notes addressing pole relocation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Utility poles at property boundaries relative to proposed driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan must clearly show the location of all existing utility poles and provide dimension annotations indicating clearance from driveway edges. If any poles are within 30 feet of driveway edge, relocation plans must be noted."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows an OHE (overhead electric) line on the southern boundary with three small circular symbols that typically represent utility poles. However, no dimension annotations on Sheet 9 or any other sheet explicitly show or specify whether clearance dimensions are being measured from the outside conductor location or from the pole centerline. Sheet 4 legend indicates utility pole symbols, but proposed site plan Sheet 9 lacks dimension callouts that would clarify the measurement origin point (conductor vs. pole center).","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires all clearances be measured from the outside conductor, not from pole centerline or pole structure. On multi-conductor installations, the outside conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. The absence of dimension annotations on the plans prevents verification that dimensions are correctly measured from conductor location. This is a deficiency pattern noted in the grouping documentation as 'Common Violation Patterns': 'Clearances measured from pole instead of conductor: Dimension annotations read \"10'-0\" from pole\" instead of \"15'-0\" from outside conductor\".'","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All clearance dimensions relative to overhead electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All clearance dimension annotations must explicitly originate at the outside conductor location, not at the utility pole centerline or pole face. Dimension lines and callouts must clearly show measurement origin point (e.g., '15'-0\" from outside conductor')."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) show landscape and site lighting features, but no new streetlight poles are shown on the site plan as proposed site infrastructure. The site appears to rely on building-mounted lighting per Sheet 9 notes regarding full cut-off fully shielded fixtures. No streetlight pole locations are depicted on the photometric plan or other sheets.","reasoning":"EL-1.24 applies only when new streetlight poles are proposed. No proposed streetlight poles are shown on the site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply. Building-mounted lighting per Subchapter E 2.5 appears to be the design approach.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) shows utility poles at property corners near Valley View Road right-of-way frontage. Sheet 9 (site plan) shows sidewalk alignment along Valley View Road frontage in the general area of these poles. However, no detail views or dimension annotations are provided showing the exact relationship between the proposed sidewalk alignment and the existing pole locations at property corners. Whether the poles fall within or immediately adjacent to the sidewalk area is not clearly documented.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires sidewalks to be cleared from existing power poles at each end of property along ROW frontage. While poles exist at property corners and sidewalks are proposed, the specific clearance or conflict relationship is not adequately documented on the plans. Enlarged details or dimension callouts showing pole locations relative to sidewalk edges would be needed to verify compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks along Valley View Road frontage at property ends"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Enlarged plan details must show existing power pole locations at property ends and document that proposed sidewalk alignments maintain adequate clearance from pole structures, or note if poles are to be relocated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows trash collection notes indicating that commercial dumpsters and containers are not permitted to be left at curbside. Refuse areas appear to be managed at individual building locations. No dedicated trash enclosure or receptacle location is explicitly shown on the site plan as positioned beneath overhead electric facilities.","reasoning":"EL-1.26 applies only when trash enclosures or receptacle locations are shown beneath overhead electric facilities. While waste management is addressed on the site, no dedicated trash enclosure is depicted as being located beneath the OHE line, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (site plan) shows OHE line on southern boundary. Buildings and site features are shown in plan view. Sheet 4 (existing survey) depicts overhead utility poles and lines around property boundaries, including along the southern boundary where the OHE line is marked. However, no section views or cross-sections showing the vertical positioning of buildings and site features relative to the overhead line are provided. The plans do not explicitly indicate whether any buildings, structures, or site features are proposed to be positioned directly beneath, over, or within the electric easement boundary.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 contains an absolute prohibition: customer facilities cannot be installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities, regardless of clearance distances. Additionally, items within electric easements must maintain 7.5-foot clearance from the conductor. While the OHE line is shown on the site plan and buildings are proposed, the three-dimensional relationship (under/over/within) cannot be definitively determined from plan view alone without explicit cross-sectional analysis or notes addressing easement boundaries and facility positioning.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings (1-8) and site features relative to OHE line and electric easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans must include Austin Energy easement exhibit showing electric easement boundaries with notes confirming no buildings or permanent structures are proposed under or over overhead distribution facilities, and that items within easement boundaries maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water meter locations at each building, but the specific elevation or location coordinates relative to any overhead service drop lines are not documented. The vision analysis of Sheet 9 noted an 'AT&T Pole' near the top-left but did not identify electric service drop locations. No sheet explicitly shows overhead electric service drop conductor elevations or the locations of water meters relative to service drops.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 and § 1.10.6.2 require water meters to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric service-drop conductors. While water meter locations are shown on the utility plan, the specific location of electric service drops and clearance dimensions from the meters to these service drops are not documented on any sheet. Without this information, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations relative to overhead electric service drops"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plan must show locations of overhead electric service-drop lines with dimension annotations verifying 7.5-foot clearance from service drop conductors to water meter locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water line routing throughout the site serving all eight buildings from the connection point on Valley View Road. Overhead electric infrastructure (OHE line) is depicted on Sheet 9. However, no dimension annotations or clearance callouts on Sheet 19 or the utility routing details specify the horizontal or vertical clearance distance from the water line routing to the overhead electric poles or conductors.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires water lines to maintain clearance from overhead electrical distribution facilities. While water lines are clearly shown on the utility plan and overhead distribution infrastructure exists, documented clearance dimensions from water lines to the overhead poles and conductors are not provided. This clearance information is necessary to verify compliance.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing relative to overhead distribution infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plan must include dimension annotations showing clearance distances from water line routing to all overhead electric poles and conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of the site plan layout (Sheet 9) shows all proposed building structures (Buildings 1-8) are positioned well away from the property lines. Building setbacks from property lines appear to exceed 5 feet based on the depicted distances and the scale of the drawing. The buildings are concentrated in the interior of the site, with the detention pond on the northeast, parking and driveways in the central area, and landscaping between buildings and property boundaries.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires structures with permanent foundations within 5 feet of property line to allow clearance space for electric facilities. The site layout clearly shows all proposed buildings are set back significantly from property lines (more than 5 feet). Therefore, this requirement does not create an issue - there is adequate space for electric facilities in the area near property lines where overhead poles and lines are located.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All building locations relative to property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The proposed site plan shows buildings with FFE (finished floor elevation) values on Sheet 21 ranging from 683.0 to 687.50 feet. The existing overhead utility poles are depicted on Sheet 4 around property boundaries. However, no surveyed data from a registered surveyor showing pole locations, conductor heights, or mid-span clearance measurements is provided anywhere in the site plan or supplementary documents. The vertical clearance from overhead conductors to buildings, parking, and other site features is not documented on any sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires a registered surveyor to provide mid-span clearance data when vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient. While the plans do not contain explicit elevation callouts for overhead conductors that would allow visual comparison to building heights, the complete absence of surveyor mid-span clearance data is a deficiency. Professional engineering judgment indicates that overhead distribution lines at typical utility pole heights (30-40+ feet) would likely provide adequate vertical clearance to residential building roofs (approximately 35-40 feet MSL). However, without documented surveyor data, compliance cannot be formally verified and certified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features with vertical extent (buildings, parking structures, etc.)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor must provide documented mid-span clearance measurements for existing overhead facilities showing vertical distance from lowest point of conductors and attachments to highest proposed site features (building roofs, HVAC equipment, etc.) to demonstrate code-required clearances are maintained."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows only existing overhead electric lines that are already in place - no new overhead electric lines are proposed to be constructed as part of this development. Sheet 21 shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure only. The project is developing with underground service per the preliminary electrical design.","reasoning":"EL-1.32 applies only when new overhead electric lines cross proposed or existing roadways. No new overhead electric lines are proposed on this project, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure only - transformers, pull boxes, electrical meters, and underground lines. No secondary or primary overhead electric lines are proposed to cross each other on this project. The existing overhead utilities are on the property perimeter, not crossing through the site.","reasoning":"EL-1.33 applies only when both secondary and primary overhead electric lines are shown on utility plans with one crossing over the other. The proposed design uses underground electric service exclusively; no secondary or primary overhead line crossings are proposed, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets shows no marquee signs proposed on the site. Building signage is not depicted on Sheet 9 or any architectural/signage sheets. The project is a multi-family residential townhome development without commercial signage.","reasoning":"EL-1.34 applies only when marquee signs are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist. No marquee signs are shown in the proposed site plan, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure with transformers and service points, but no new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed to be constructed. The design appears to utilize existing overhead infrastructure with underground service extensions to the buildings.","reasoning":"EL-1.35 applies only when new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion and existing poles will remain. No new power poles are proposed in the preliminary electrical design, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and Sheet 9 (Site Plan) show landscape elements and site lighting features. The landscape plan indicates outdoor lighting will be provided, and Sheet 9 notes specify that 'All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5.' However, no explicit photometric plan or enlarged fixture location details are provided showing the specific location of individual decorative light fixtures relative to the overhead electric line on the southern boundary, nor are clearance dimensions documented.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires decorative lighting fixtures beneath overhead lines to meet clearance requirements or be relocated. While site lighting is proposed and overhead lines exist, the specific locations of decorative fixtures relative to the OHE line and documented clearance verification are not provided. Without a photometric plan showing fixture locations and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixtures if located near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Photometric plan or enlarged lighting detail must show locations of all decorative light fixtures near overhead electric lines with dimension annotations verifying clearance requirements are met (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial), or notes indicating fixtures are relocated away from lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows OHE (overhead electric) line on the southern boundary with trees indicated by canopy symbols positioned near and beneath this line. Vision analysis confirmed trees are placed in close proximity to the OHE line. However, the specific tree species for proposed plantings are not identified on Sheet 31 itself. Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations) provides a plant list showing Cedar Elm (10 trees), Live Oak (2), Mexican Redbud (6), Texas Mountain Laurel (2), and groundcovers, but this list does NOT indicate which species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. No notes on Sheets 31 or 35 address or reference the requirement that trees within 10 feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible trees list (ECM Appendix F, species marked 'UC').","reasoning":"ECM § 2.4.1.D, § 2.4.2.C, and UCM § 1.10.10.4 require trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (or 50 feet of transmission per UCM 1.10.10.4) to be utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F (generally mature height ≤20 feet marked 'UC'). The requirement is applicable because trees are proposed near the OHE line on the southern boundary. However, the plans do not verify that the proposed tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F, nor do they document lateral distances from tree locations to the conductor.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 10 lateral feet of OHE line on southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule must specify which tree species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F for planting within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Tree species must be marked or noted as 'UC' (Utility Compatible, generally ≤20' mature height). Plan must include dimension annotations showing lateral distance (horizontal) from each tree location to the overhead conductor and note species compliance with utility compatibility requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed electrical meter locations at various points on the site serving each building. However, no enlarged detail views or landscape plan annotations are provided showing whether any meters are obstructed by proposed structures, fences, equipment, vegetation, or building projections. The specific clearances around meter locations (30-inch front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) are not documented on any plan detail.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.9.3.1 requires proposed meter locations to be accessible without obstruction. Specific working clearances are required: 30-inch width, 36-inch depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9. While meter locations are identified on the electrical plan, the accessibility and clearance verification around meter areas are not documented on the plans with detail views or notes confirming no obstructions.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical meter locations throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Enlarged meter detail views must show 30-inch front width, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances around each meter location, confirming no site features, fences, walls, vegetation, or building projections obstruct access."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) shows existing utility poles at property corners and boundaries. Sheet 9 (site plan) shows all proposed buildings positioned in the interior of the site with significant setbacks from property lines where utility poles exist. No building is depicted in direct adjacency to pole locations based on the plan geometry and scale.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires new buildings to maintain clearance from existing streetlight poles. Review of the site layout confirms all proposed buildings are set back substantially from property boundaries where poles are located, creating adequate separation distance. The buildings appear to be far enough from the existing poles that no clearance violation is present.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings relative to existing utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) legend indicates that down guy wires from utility poles are depicted with 'GUY' notation. Vision analysis of Sheet 4 confirmed that guy wires are marked on poles at property corners. Sheet 9 (site plan) shows driveways, accessible pathways, and parking areas, but does not include dimension annotations showing the location of guy anchor points or guy wire alignments relative to proposed accessible routes and driveways. The Electric Notes on Sheet 3, Block 19 require the owner to include tree pruning and removal work within construction limits, but do not specifically address guy wire relocation or conflicts.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.17.0 (Glossary) and practical utility design distinguish down guy wires (distribution support cables) from angled guy wires (transmission tower guys). Down guy anchors from existing poles can conflict with proposed accessible paths and driveways. While guy wires are shown on the existing survey, their specific locations and potential conflicts with proposed site features are not documented on the proposed site plan with dimension callouts or relocation/resolution notes.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations relative to proposed accessible routes and driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan must clearly identify existing down guy wire anchor locations and document resolution of any conflicts with proposed accessible routes and driveways through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles, or provide plan notes confirming no conflicts exist."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of sheet index and facts.md shows no transmission facilities on this site. No transmission structures or transmission towers with angled guy wire systems are depicted on any plans. The utility poles on the property appear to be distribution-scale poles based on the existing survey depiction.","reasoning":"EL-1.41 applies only to angled guy easements from transmission structures (high-voltage facilities). No transmission facilities or transmission towers are shown on this project, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (existing survey) depicts utility poles at property corners with guy notations indicating down guy support cables. However, no easement exhibit or legal description of down guy anchor easements is provided on the site plan sheets. Sheets 2 (Plat) and the easement exhibits focus on drainage, wastewater, public utility, and electric easements, but down guy anchor easements are not separately depicted or dimensioned.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires down guy anchor points to have dedicated 10-foot-wide easements extending minimum 5 feet past where the guy enters ground. While down guys exist on the property (shown on existing survey), the specific easement boundaries for these down guys are not depicted on the plat or easement exhibit. Without documented easement areas on the plat, compliance with the easement dedication requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor points at property corners"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Easement exhibit and plat must identify and show 10-foot-wide down guy anchor easements extending minimum 5 feet past ground entry point for each down guy support cable on property."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed pole-mounted transformers at multiple locations on the site serving the electrical distribution to buildings. However, no surveyed elevation or height data is provided for these transformers, and no section views showing vertical clearance from existing overhead electric lines to the tops of the transformer equipment are documented on any sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires transformers to maintain 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric lines when lines are above or adjacent to transformer locations. While transformers are shown on the plan, the specific type (pole-mounted vs. pad-mounted) and vertical clearance dimensions are not documented. Without surveyed transformer elevation data and clearance dimensions on section views, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed transformer locations if located beneath overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan must specify transformer types (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) and provide section views with dimension annotations showing vertical clearance from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment, verifying 7.5-foot minimum clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows proposed electrical infrastructure with transformers and service points. No niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations with structures, canopies, or covered areas above equipment) are depicted on the site plan or electrical design sheets. All proposed electrical equipment appears to be exposed/open installation types.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 applies only to transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). No niche-configured electrical equipment is shown in the proposed design, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 5 (Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan) and 8 (Tree Removal & Demolition Plan) show construction staging and phasing. However, no explicit construction logistics plan, site logistics diagram, or notes on Sheets 5, 8, or 6 (Erosion Control Notes) document the location of construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, crane swing radius zones, or work platforms relative to the existing overhead electric lines. The distance between construction activity areas and overhead lines is not dimensioned or noted.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms to maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA. This is a temporary requirement distinct from permanent clearances. While construction is planned on the site with overhead utilities present, the specific construction staging layout and documented 10-foot clearances from overhead lines are not provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, work platforms"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":8}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction logistics plan or site phasing plan must document staging area boundaries, crane swing radius zones, equipment laydown areas, and work platforms with dimension annotations verifying 10-foot radial clearance from all overhead electric lines. Construction management notes must address overhead line safety during all phases."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheet 3 (General Notes) - all block content; Sheet 6 (Erosion Control Notes); cover sheet notes; and the Electric Notes on Sheet 3, Block 19 reveals that the site plan includes Electric Notes acknowledging Austin Energy requirements and stating 'The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations...' However, there is NO note on the cover sheet or general notes stating: 'Owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' or any reference to Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires a note stating owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. The Electric Notes reference OSHA and NESC clearance requirements but do not include the specific 48-hour notification requirement for high-voltage work. This is a documentation deficiency - the required note is missing from the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Add note to cover sheet or general notes: 'Owner/contractor shall notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before beginning any construction activities or operations near overhead electric lines. Contact Austin Energy at [number] per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.'"},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows proposed electrical service infrastructure, but no service-mast through-roof installations are depicted on the site plan or on any building elevation sheets. The design appears to utilize underground service distribution from transformers on pad/pole to individual building service points.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 applies only to service-mast through-roof installations where the mast penetrates the roof to connect service lines. No service masts are shown on the submitted plans; the design uses underground service routing, therefore this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"616e92cf-d57d-4404-a5fc-6cc71991193e","uuid":"75159b1b-d71b-4183-aa1b-a475b14ff460"}
