{"level":30,"time":1778187898350,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR243VVGRCDE3YK74EBN3CA2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've completed my comprehensive evaluation of all 47 checklist items in the EL-1 (Overhead Electric Clearances) grouping. Let me summarize the key findings:\n\n**SUMMARY OF FINDINGS:**\n\n**Applicability: YES** - This grouping applies to the Valley View Townhomes project because:\n- Existing overhead distribution electric lines are present on the property\n- Multiple proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, and landscaping features\n- Electric easements documented on property\n- OHE line crosses main driveway entrance\n\n**FAIL FINDINGS (5 items):**\n1. **EL-1.7** - Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations not provided\n2. **EL-1.8** - Section/plan view exhibits with clearance dimensions not provided\n3. **EL-1.18** - Driveway vertical clearance dimensions not documented where OHE crosses\n4. **EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions measured from wrong reference point (not from outside conductor)\n5. **EL-1.27** - Trees positioned at/overlapping OHE line violating prohibition\n6. **EL-1.31** - Surveyor mid-span clearance data not provided\n7. **EL-1.37** - Trees near overhead line not utility-compatible species\n8. **EL-1.45** - Construction staging plan with 10-foot clearance not provided\n9. **EL-1.46** - 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy not included\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE FINDINGS (14 items):**\n- EL-1.1, EL-1.2, EL-1.3, EL-1.6, EL-1.14, EL-1.17, EL-1.19, EL-1.25, EL-1.29, EL-1.30, EL-1.36, EL-1.38, EL-1.39, EL-1.40, EL-1.42\n\n\n- The remaining 28 items are marked N/A because their triggering conditions don't apply—no gas pumps, elevated walkways, transmission lines, substations, marquee signs, or emergency access structures exist on the site. The findings have been documented in StructuredOutput format with complete status designations, reasoning, code references, and applicable sheet locations.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","uuid":"f4d65636-0b23-4c70-b7fd-f5f428eafab5"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187900622,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR243VVGRCDE3YK74EBN3CA2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed a comprehensive site plan review for the **EL-1 grouping (Overhead Electric Feature Clearances)** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Review Completion Summary\n\n**Grouping Status: APPLICABLE** — The project has existing overhead electric distribution facilities on-site with proposed buildings and site features requiring clearance verification.\n\n### Key Findings Overview:\n\n**Critical Deficiencies (9 FAIL items):**\n- **EL-1.7** - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n- **EL-1.8** - No section/plan view exhibits showing clearance dimensions\n- **EL-1.18** - **Driveway clearance undocumented** where OHE line crosses main entrance\n- **EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions not properly originating from outside conductor\n- **EL-1.27** - **Trees positioned at/overlapping OHE line**, violating prohibition\n- **EL-1.31** - No surveyor mid-span clearance data provided\n- **EL-1.37** - **Proposed trees NOT utility-compatible species** (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, etc. near OHE line)\n- **EL-1.45** - Construction staging plan missing with 10-foot clearance requirements\n- **EL-1.46** - **48-hour Austin Energy notification note missing** from plans\n\n**Unverifiable Items (14):** Require additional documentation to confirm compliance (conductor elevations, dimension callouts, detail sheets not provided)\n\n**Non-Applicable Items (28):** Triggering conditions not present (no transmission lines, substations, gas pumps, emergency structures, etc.)\n\nAll 47 checklist items have been formally evaluated and documented with specific code citations, observations, reasoning, and applicable areas. The findings are ready for applicant response and remediation planning."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","uuid":"ab08a1fa-b580-4756-8973-a7c2bde3ea74"}
{"level":30,"time":1778187900649,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":328689,"duration_api_ms":214487,"num_turns":28,"result":"I have completed a comprehensive site plan review for the **EL-1 grouping (Overhead Electric Feature Clearances)** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Review Completion Summary\n\n**Grouping Status: APPLICABLE** — The project has existing overhead electric distribution facilities on-site with proposed buildings and site features requiring clearance verification.\n\n### Key Findings Overview:\n\n**Critical Deficiencies (9 FAIL items):**\n- **EL-1.7** - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n- **EL-1.8** - No section/plan view exhibits showing clearance dimensions\n- **EL-1.18** - **Driveway clearance undocumented** where OHE line crosses main entrance\n- **EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions not properly originating from outside conductor\n- **EL-1.27** - **Trees positioned at/overlapping OHE line**, violating prohibition\n- **EL-1.31** - No surveyor mid-span clearance data provided\n- **EL-1.37** - **Proposed trees NOT utility-compatible species** (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, etc. near OHE line)\n- **EL-1.45** - Construction staging plan missing with 10-foot clearance requirements\n- **EL-1.46** - **48-hour Austin Energy notification note missing** from plans\n\n**Unverifiable Items (14):** Require additional documentation to confirm compliance (conductor elevations, dimension callouts, detail sheets not provided)\n\n**Non-Applicable Items (28):** Triggering conditions not present (no transmission lines, substations, gas pumps, emergency structures, etc.)\n\nAll 47 checklist items have been formally evaluated and documented with specific code citations, observations, reasoning, and applicable areas. The findings are ready for applicant response and remediation planning.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f0048680-e5a3-4ca8-8dfa-cc37e7cbf9e3","total_cost_usd":0.3207225,"usage":{"input_tokens":8109,"cache_creation_input_tokens":94270,"cache_read_input_tokens":794010,"output_tokens":23075,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":94270},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8109,"outputTokens":23075,"cacheReadInputTokens":794010,"cacheCreationInputTokens":94270,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3207225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings (Bldg 1-8) and existing overhead electric line along southern boundary (Sheet 4, Sheet 31). Building locations are set back from the OHE line approximately 100+ feet to the north.","reasoning":"While buildings are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist on the site, no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions are provided. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified from plan view alone without elevation data showing the conductor location and building face clearance. The spatial separation visible on the plan view is sufficient distance, but the requirement is specific about demonstrating clearances from the 'outside conductor' and requires professional verification.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations 1-8 relative to OHE line at southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and labeled clearance dimensions are required to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead distribution lines are confirmed on site plan (Sheets 4, 31). The OHE line is shown with dashes and 'OHE' notation. Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service with transformers and pull boxes, indicating underground distribution to buildings.","reasoning":"The site appears to have existing overhead distribution primary lines (not transmission lines, as voltage not specified but typical for urban Austin is 12.47kV or 34.5kV distribution). Customer facilities (buildings) are proposed but no dimensional clearance verification from outside conductor is shown. The code requires 15-foot radial clearance measured in all directions from the outside conductor, which requires explicit dimensional documentation in plan and section views. Spatial separation visible on plan view is insufficient without precise dimensional verification from the outer conductor location.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building locations 1-8 relative to existing overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimension lines showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to all customer facilities must be provided on site plan and section views."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevation sheets are not included in the submitted site plan set (39 sheets reviewed; no building elevation documents found). Sheet 9 shows buildings in plan view only without elevation or projection details.","reasoning":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks) are standard features of residential buildings but cannot be assessed without building elevation sheets. The overhead electric facilities exist (confirmed on Sheets 4, 31), but without elevation documentation showing the three-dimensional relationships between conductor location and building projections, compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections on all 8 proposed buildings relative to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets showing all building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) with dimensions and clearance verification from overhead electric conductors are required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review of all sheets (1-39) and supplementary documents found no gas pump canopies proposed or shown on the site plan.","reasoning":"No gas pump canopies are included in the proposed site development. This is a residential multi-family townhomes project with no fuel service facilities proposed. The triggering condition (gas pump canopies) does not exist.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan sheets reviewed (9, 11, 15-17, 31, 38-39) show buildings, driveways, sidewalks, parking areas, and retaining walls. No elevated walkways, elevated platforms, or elevated structures (beyond standard building structures addressed separately) are proposed.","reasoning":"The proposed site improvements consist of ground-level or building-level features. While concrete sidewalks and pedestrian walkways are proposed, these are ground-level, not elevated structures requiring radial clearance from overhead distribution facilities. No elevated walkways or platforms separate from the buildings are shown on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document indicates Valley View Road is a Local Street (ASMP Level 1), ROW classification 2U-OP. The site is adjacent to ROW. Sheet 4 and facts document show 5' electric easements dedicated in the Mecey Subdivision plat. Electric facilities exist in or near ROW adjacent to site.","reasoning":"Building setback from ROW and electric facility locations/relocation notes are not clearly documented with clearance dimensions. The code requires buildings to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance and 15-foot radial clearance from any overhead electric facilities in ROW adjacent to the site. Without elevation views showing the relationship between building faces and overhead facilities in the ROW, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to Valley View Road ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations with labeled clearance dimensions from overhead electric facilities in adjacent ROW must be provided, demonstrating both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet site plan package. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows buildings in plan view only. Overhead electric facilities are confirmed to exist on property (Sheets 4, 31) with poles and conductors shown.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires building elevation sheets to include surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimension annotations. This is a fundamental documentation requirement when buildings or elevated structures are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. The absence of elevation sheets means the surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance verification do not exist in the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings 1-8 relative to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets must be submitted, including registered surveyor data showing surveyed conductor elevation and clearance dimension annotations for all buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review reveals no section or plan view exhibits with dimension lines from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings or building projections. Sheet 9 shows plan view only; no section callouts reference building clearance details.","reasoning":"The code requires explicit dimensional documentation from the outside conductor (not pole center) to the outermost building edge. This is the primary method for verifying compliance. The absence of these dimensions across all submitted sheets (verified through review of Sheets 1-39) means the clearance verification requirement is not satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings 1-8 and any building projections"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits must be added showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of each building and building projection for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3. Dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor location, not pole center."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows property fencing and enclosure systems. Sheet 38 (Wall Plan) shows retaining walls; Sheet 9 shows wooden privacy fences per legend key note H.6. However, no traditional fences (temporary or permanent barriers separate from retaining walls) are explicitly proposed in relation to overhead electric conductor locations visible on the plan.","reasoning":"While fencing exists on the site (privacy fences, retaining walls), they do not appear to be positioned directly under or in the immediate proximity of the OHE line shown on Sheet 31. The OHE line runs along the southern boundary where the driveway and parking area are located. No fences appear to be proposed directly beneath this line based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing power poles are shown on Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) at the southern and eastern boundaries. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed fence locations (wooden privacy fences, per legend). Horizontal distances between proposed fence posts and existing electric poles are not dimensionally labeled.","reasoning":"The reviewer convention requires 10-foot horizontal clearance from fence posts to overhead electric poles. Plan view provides general layout but lacks specific dimensional callouts for fence post locations relative to pole centers. Without explicit dimension annotations, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed fence locations relative to existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dimension annotations must be provided showing fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document identifies electric easements but no Austin Energy substation is noted on the property or in the immediate adjacency description. Site plan review (Sheets 1-39) finds no substation enclosures or transformer vaults identified as substations.","reasoning":"This item applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation infrastructure is documented on the site plan or in the project facts.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) shown or referenced on property. Existing overhead electric facilities are distribution lines (typical Austin distribution 12.47kV or 34.5kV). No transmission easements or transmission structures are documented.","reasoning":"This item applies only to fencing beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV). No transmission facilities are present on the property based on available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed fencing (wooden privacy fences per Sheet 9 legend, retaining walls per Sheet 38). The vehicle barrier/fence locations visible on Sheet 9 do not appear to be positioned directly beneath the OHE line visible on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The item applies when vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines with clearance verification needed. While the site has both fencing and overhead lines, the fencing does not appear to be positioned directly beneath the OHE line based on plan view analysis.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 shows retaining walls up to 14 feet in height planned for the site. Overhead electric line is shown on Sheets 4 and 31 running along southern boundary. Retaining walls shown on Sheet 38 plan view are in the northeast and central areas, but horizontal relationship to OHE line not explicitly dimensioned.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement applies to retaining walls near overhead facilities. Without section views showing wall face elevations and dimension lines to the outer electric conductor, compliance cannot be verified. Plan view alone does not provide sufficient evidence of either compliance or non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls in relation to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views showing retaining wall elevations with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall must be provided to demonstrate compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no Austin Energy substation on the property or identified in adjacency materials. Retaining walls are proposed but not near any substation property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property (within 10 feet of substation boundary) requiring 5-foot separation. No substation is identified in project documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review of all sheets finds no emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms proposed for the project. The site consists of buildings, driveways, parking, sidewalks, and landscaping only.","reasoning":"The item applies only when emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed near overhead facilities. No such structures are included in the proposed development.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are shown on Sheet 38. Overhead electric facilities are shown on Sheets 4 and 31. No section views with clearance dimensions from outer conductor to wall face are provided anywhere in the 39-sheet plan set.","reasoning":"Section exhibits showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining walls are required for clearance verification. The absence of these sections means compliance cannot be determined from available documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views for retaining walls must be provided showing dimensions from outer electric conductor to wall face for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) clearly shows overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' running horizontally along the southern boundary, and vision analysis confirms it crosses directly over the main driveway entrance (southwest portion of site). No vertical clearance height is labeled at this crossing point. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) provides finished elevations for buildings but no overhead line elevations or mid-span clearance data are shown.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 16-foot vertical clearance for driveways without truck traffic, 18-foot for areas with truck traffic. The site plan clearly shows the OHE crossing the driveway without any clearance dimension labeled. This is a critical documentation gap: without surveyed conductor elevation and finished driveway grade elevations showing the clearance distance, the requirement cannot be verified. The absence of these essential dimensions constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Main driveway entrance at southwest portion of site where OHE line crosses"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions must be provided for the driveway where the OHE line crosses, showing minimum 16-foot or 18-foot clearance from the lowest point of the overhead electric line (including any attachments) to the finished driveway grade. Registered surveyor data for mid-span clearance verification is required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows parking areas on the site, primarily in the central and southern portions. The OHE line runs along the southern boundary. Vertical relationship between parking surface elevation and overhead line is not documented with dimension annotations.","reasoning":"The item applies when vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. While parking exists and overhead lines are present on the site, the vertical clearance requirement cannot be determined without elevation documentation showing the finished pad grade and overhead line height with dimension callouts.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Parking areas in proximity to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If parking or vehicle display areas are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, section views with labeled vertical clearance dimensions must be provided to demonstrate the required clearance (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet for parking without trucks, 18 feet with truck traffic)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts document and site plan review find no electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) on the property. Existing overhead facilities are distribution-level (typical 12.47kV or 34.5kV for Austin urban areas). No transmission easements or transmission structures identified.","reasoning":"This item applies only when roads or driveways are regraded beneath electric transmission lines (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV). No transmission facilities are documented as existing on the property.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No highway or freeway construction is proposed on this multi-family residential site. The project is limited to local streets and driveways for a 39-unit townhomes development on Valley View Road (a local street, ASMP Level 1).","reasoning":"This item applies only to highway/freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures. The project scope does not include highway or freeway work.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and existing conditions (Sheet 4) show existing electric poles at the property boundary, not within the proposed driveway footprints shown on Sheet 9.","reasoning":"This item applies when proposed driveways are shown in conflict with or immediately adjacent (within 30 feet) to existing electric pole locations. The existing poles appear to be located along the property boundary, not in direct conflict with the proposed internal driveway system based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Extensive review of all 39 site plan sheets and supporting documents reveals that where clearance dimensions are shown anywhere on the plans (limited clearance callouts exist for other utilities like water, sewer), they do not demonstrate measurement from the 'outside conductor' or 'outermost electric line' as required by code. More critically, no clearance dimensions FROM overhead electric conductors TO buildings or site features are shown at all.","reasoning":"The grouping guidance specifically warns that 'Clearances measured from utility pole or centerline instead of from outside conductor' is a common violation pattern. A review of all dimension annotations on Sheets 1-39 shows no instances of dimensions explicitly originating from a conductor location. The required methodology—measuring from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from pole centerline or centerline of three-phase lines—is not documented anywhere on the plans. This is a systematic deficiency in all clearance documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All clearance dimensions on site plan where overhead electric facilities exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All clearance dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from pole center or centerline of multi-conductor installations. On three-phase installations, the conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension line endpoints must clearly show measurement origin at the conductor location."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed site lighting fixtures. Sheet 9 includes lighting note requiring full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5. No streetlight poles are shown as proposed on the site plan.","reasoning":"The item applies when new streetlight poles are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. The site has lighting fixtures on buildings and in landscaping areas, but no proposed streetlight poles (separate free-standing light poles in the public right-of-way) are documented on the site plan.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows sidewalks and pedestrian pathways throughout the site. Existing power poles are shown on Sheets 4 and 31 at property boundaries. The site plan does not explicitly show sidewalk alignment clearance from existing power poles at the property line/ROW frontage on Valley View Road.","reasoning":"The item applies when new or modified sidewalks are proposed and existing power poles are located within or immediately adjacent to the sidewalk alignment at property ends along ROW. While sidewalks are proposed and poles exist at the boundary, the specific alignment clearance from poles at the property limits is not dimensionally documented.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk alignment along Valley View Road ROW frontage near existing power poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If sidewalks are positioned at or near existing power pole locations at the property boundary along ROW, clearance dimensions must be provided showing sidewalk alignment and pole location."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows trash collection notes and site plan includes trash enclosure areas. The trash enclosure locations are shown in the building areas, not beneath the OHE line visible on Sheet 31 running along the southern boundary.","reasoning":"The item applies when trash enclosures or receptacle locations are shown beneath overhead electric facilities. While the site has trash management areas, they do not appear to be positioned directly beneath the overhead electric line based on plan view inspection.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead distribution electric line is confirmed on Sheets 4, 31 running along southern boundary of site. Trees are shown on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) positioned at and overlapping the OHE line marking on the southern property boundary. Electric easement exhibit and site plan show the OHE facility location.","reasoning":"The code absolutely prohibits customer facilities (including landscaping features) from being installed under or over overhead distribution facilities, separate from and distinct from the clearance distance requirements. The vision analysis of Sheet 31 explicitly noted trees 'directly adjacent to, and in some cases overlapping, the OHE line.' This positioning violates the prohibition regardless of whether clearances otherwise might be maintained. The deficiency is the placement of landscape features at or overlapping the overhead line location itself, not merely insufficient clearance distance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Trees on Landscape Plan Sheet 31 at southern property boundary where OHE line exists"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and other landscape features are shown positioned at or overlapping the overhead electric line on Sheet 31, violating the prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. All landscape features within the electric easement must maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from the outside conductor. Trees positioned directly beneath the line must be relocated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21) shows domestic water branches connecting to buildings via 2\" HDPE service tubing. No water meter locations are explicitly dimensioned on the utility plan in relation to the OHE service drop line that may exist on the property.","reasoning":"The item applies when water meter locations are shown and overhead electric service-drop conductors (secondary voltage service lines from utility infrastructure to customer service point) exist on site. While water service is proposed, specific water meter locations relative to any overhead service drop are not clearly documented on the plans reviewed, and the OHE line shown on Sheets 4 and 31 appears to be distribution-level, not a service drop.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows new water line routing through the site. Overhead electric facilities (distribution lines) are shown on Sheets 4 and 31. The spatial relationship between underground water line routing and overhead electric pole/conductor locations is not explicitly dimensioned.","reasoning":"The item applies when new water lines are shown beneath or adjacent to overhead electrical distribution facilities. While both water lines and overhead lines exist on the site, the clearance dimensions or separation distances between them are not documented with explicit callouts on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing relative to overhead distribution poles and conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions must be provided showing water line routing maintains adequate separation from overhead distribution poles and conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows building foundations and setbacks. Facts document indicates Valley View Road frontage with proposed buildings. Electric facilities are documented as existing in ROW via dedicated easements noted in facts document and on Sheet 4.","reasoning":"The item applies when permanent structure foundations are within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities exist or are planned in adjacent ROW. While the spatial relationships are shown in plan view, specific dimension verification of foundation clearance from property line is not explicitly documented, making definitive assessment difficult from plan view alone.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations near property line adjacent to Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If any building foundations are located within 5 feet of the property line, detailed dimensions showing clearance space for electric facility access and maintenance must be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line is confirmed crossing the main driveway (Sheet 9, vision analysis). The driveway finished grade elevation is shown on Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) at approximately 680-682 feet. No registered surveyor data for overhead conductor elevations or mid-span clearance measurements are provided anywhere in the 39-sheet plan set or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"The code requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance data when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements. The driveway clearance is marginal based on available information (no conductor height documented), making this a condition where surveyor verification would be required. The complete absence of surveyor clearance data constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway where OHE line crosses"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor data must be provided showing pole locations, overhead conductor elevations, and mid-span clearance measurements for the driveway crossing. This data is essential to verify the minimum 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.6.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No new overhead electric lines are being constructed by the applicant on this project. The site plan shows existing overhead lines to be maintained in place.","reasoning":"This item applies only when new overhead electric lines are being constructed and cross roadways. The project involves repositioning and managing existing facilities, not constructing new overhead lines.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows underground electrical service for the proposed buildings with transformers and pull boxes. No overhead secondary or primary lines are being installed by the applicant.","reasoning":"This item applies only when secondary overhead lines are constructed crossing over primary overhead lines. The project does not propose new overhead electrical infrastructure.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheets 9, 31, 35) shows landscape features and building signage plans. No marquee signs are identified or proposed on the project site plan.","reasoning":"Marquee signs are large illuminated sign structures typically associated with commercial entertainment or hospitality uses. This is a multi-family residential project with no marquee sign features proposed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical service with pull boxes and transformers. No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed on the site plan.","reasoning":"The item applies when new poles are proposed for underground service conversion (typically replacing existing poles with new ones during conversion work). This project is transitioning to underground service but the site plan does not show new pole installations.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows site lighting requirements for full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5. Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows various landscape and lighting features. Overhead electric line is shown on Sheet 31 running along the southern boundary. No specific decorative light fixture locations or clearance dimensions from the OHE line are documented.","reasoning":"The item applies when decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath overhead electric lines. While site lighting is planned and overhead lines exist, the specific positioning of decorative light fixtures in relation to the OHE line is not explicitly documented with clearance verification.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixture locations near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If decorative lighting fixtures are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, clearance dimensions must be provided showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from the outside conductor, or alternative relocation notes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31, vision analysis) shows trees 'directly adjacent to, and in some cases overlapping, the OHE line' along the southern property boundary. Plant lists (Sheet 35, vision analysis) specify proposed tree species: Live Oak (2), Cedar Elm (10), Texas Mountain Laurel (2), Mexican Redbud (6). None of these species are marked or identified as 'utility-compatible' (UC) per ECM Appendix F. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are large trees with mature heights exceeding 20 feet, making them non-utility-compatible. No notation or schedule marking indicates UC designation for any proposed species.","reasoning":"The code (ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4) requires trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors and 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors to be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC', generally mature height ≤20 feet). The trees shown on Sheet 31 in or near the OHE line location are not documented as utility-compatible. Cedar Elm and Live Oak specifically are NOT utility-compatible due to large mature size. This is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees planted at southern property boundary near OHE line (Landscape Plan Sheet 31)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC'). The currently proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are not utility-compatible. Trees must either be relocated to positions more than 10 feet from conductors, or replaced with utility-compatible species verified in ECM Appendix F 'UC' column."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows electrical meters and transformers placed at specific locations on the site plan. No enlarged detail sheets showing meter area layouts with access clearances are provided.","reasoning":"The item applies when electric meter locations are shown on plans. The code requires 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom for meter access and installation (UCM § 1.10.9). Without detailed enlarged drawings of meter installation areas, it cannot be determined whether site features (fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, building projections) obstruct these required clearances.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical meter locations shown on Sheet 21"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Enlarged detail drawings of proposed meter locations must be provided showing no obstructions to meter access and working clearances: minimum 30 inches wide, 36 inches deep front access space, and 6.5 feet headroom per UCM § 1.10.9."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows proposed buildings and existing streetlight poles may be present along Valley View Road (adjacent public ROW). The clearance relationship between proposed buildings and existing streetlight poles is not explicitly documented with dimensions.","reasoning":"The item applies when new buildings or structures are proposed adjacent to existing streetlight poles. While the site abuts Valley View Road where streetlights may exist, the specific clearance relationship is not dimensionally documented on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near Valley View Road ROW where existing streetlights may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If existing streetlight poles are located near proposed buildings, clearance dimensions must be provided showing building location and pole proximity."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4, vision analysis) confirms existing power poles with at least one guy wire visible on the plan. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed driveways, sidewalks, and accessible routes. However, guy wire locations and accessible path alignments are not explicitly cross-referenced or dimensioned to show conflicts or clearances.","reasoning":"The item applies when down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible paths or driveways. The grouping guidance notes that 'electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.' While the survey shows at least one guy wire, the detailed conflict analysis between guy wire locations and proposed accessible routes/driveways is not documented. Without explicit dimension annotations or conflict resolution notes, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wire locations relative to proposed driveways and accessible paths"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wire locations and anchors must be clearly identified on the site plan relative to all proposed accessible paths and driveways. Any conflicts must be resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting steel poles, with details and relocation notes provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Easement exhibits (facts document, Sheet 4) reference plat-dedicated easements but no angled guy anchors or transmission structures with guy easement requirements are identified on the property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist or will exist on site. The property has distribution-level electric facilities, not transmission structures.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4, vision analysis) shows at least one existing power pole with a guy wire, indicating potential down guy anchors. Easement exhibit (facts document, Sheet 4) shows utility easements. However, dedicated easement boundaries for down guy anchors are not clearly identified with specific dimensions showing 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past ground entry.","reasoning":"The item applies when down guy anchors from distribution poles exist or will exist on site. While guy wires are shown on the survey, the specific easement documentation for these anchors (showing 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry per Austin Energy standards) is not visible in the submitted easement exhibits.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations identified on existing survey"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dedicated easements for down guy anchors must be clearly shown on the easement exhibit, displaying 10-foot width and minimum 5-foot extension past where the guy wire enters the ground, per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows pole-mounted and pad-mounted transformers. No overhead electric lines above these transformer locations are documented. The OHE line shown on Sheets 4 and 31 runs along the southern boundary, separate from transformer equipment locations.","reasoning":"This item applies when transformers are shown and overhead lines exist above or adjacent to them. The transformers on this site appear to be underground or pad-mounted in areas not directly beneath overhead distribution lines.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and electrical infrastructure. No niche service configurations (covered, recessed installations with overhead structures above equipment) are identified on the site plan.","reasoning":"This item applies only to transformers and switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). Standard pad-mounted or pole-mounted transformer installations do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Construction staging and sequence is referenced in general notes (Sheet 3, referenced in guide). Overhead electric line is confirmed on property (Sheets 4, 31). However, no site logistics plan, construction phasing plan, or staging area exhibit showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines is provided in the submitted 39 sheets or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"The code requires construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms to maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines during construction. This is separate from permanent clearance requirements and is a critical safety requirement for construction operations. The absence of a construction phasing/logistics plan with staging area boundaries documented against overhead line locations constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging and equipment operation zones relative to OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A site logistics plan or construction phasing plan must be submitted showing staging areas, equipment laydown zones, crane swing radius, material storage, and scaffold locations, with explicit notation that all construction activities maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of cover sheet (Sheet 1), general notes (Sheet 3), and site plan release notes (Sheets 1, 9) finds no note stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. The required notation per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is absent.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires a plan note regarding the 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. This is a mandatory disclosure on construction documents when overhead electric facilities exist and construction activities are proposed. The complete absence of this note from all sheets is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A plan note must be added to the cover sheet or general notes stating: 'The owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevation sheets are not included in the submitted site plan set. Without elevation documentation, service-mast through-roof installations cannot be assessed. Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service distribution.","reasoning":"This item applies only when service-mast through-roof installations are shown on building elevations. No building elevation sheets are provided, and the electrical design appears to be underground distribution to the buildings, not overhead service masts.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":""}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c4dff542-8fc5-4db6-b738-bb97c1ad0fc2"}
