{"level":30,"time":1778187908709,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":35,"prompt":"Extract the complete plant schedules shown on this sheet, including: (1) Shade Trees schedule - list all shade tree species proposed, quantities, and planting specifications; (2) Ornamental Trees schedule - list all ornamental tree species proposed, quantities, and specifications; (3) Shrubs schedule - list shrub species, quantities, and maximum spacing. For trees specifically, include the species name, quantity, and container/caliper specifications. Format as a clear, readable table or list.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan document, here are the complete plant schedules extracted exactly as they appear in the \"PLANT LIST\" section.\n\n### (1) SHADE TREES\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [blank] | [blank] | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PRESERVED | [blank] |\n| + | 2 | LIVE OAK,<br>QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL.,<br>16' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n| * | 10 | CEDAR ELM,<br>ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL.,<br>16' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n\n### (2) ORNAMENTAL TREES\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [icon] | 2 | TEXAS MOUNTAIN LAUREL,<br>SOPHORA SECUNDIFLORA | 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL.,<br>8' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n| [icon] | 8 | MEXICAN REDBUD,<br>CERCIS CANADENSIS VAR. MEXICANA | 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL.,<br>10' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n\n### (3) SHRUBS\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. CONTAINER | MAX. SPACING |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [icon] | 12 | DWARF PALMETTO, SABAL MINOR | 5 GALLON | 4' O.C. |\n| [icon] | 24 | BIG MUHLY (1 gal), MUHLENBERGIA LINDHEIMERI | 1 GALLON | SEE PLANS |\n| [icon] | 28 | GULF MUH