of these have adjacent text labels indicating their type (e.g., \"M\", \"P\", \"SY\").\n    *   **Existing Trees (to be preserved):** Along the bottom right edge near the OHE line, there are circles that contain a distinct \"+\" symbol floating in the center of the circle, along with a small circle at the center point.\n*   **Locations Relative to OHE Lines:** There is a significant concentration of trees located directly along the bottom boundary line where the \"- OHE -\" line runs.\n    *   A row of proposed trees (circles with crosshairs) is planted in the buffer strip running parallel to the \"- OHE -\" line.\n    *   Near the bottom right corner, there are at least three existing trees (circles with the \"+\" symbol in the center) located directly adjacent to or overlapping the \"- OHE -\" line. These are labeled with letters such as \"M\" and \"P\".\n\n**(3) Clearance Dimensions, Notes, or Call-outs:**\n*   There are **no** clearance dimensions (e.g., dimension lines with distance measurements), specific notes, or textual call-outs on this plan indicating required distances from tree canopies or trunks to the overhead conductors or utility poles. The \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", general \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\" sections do not mention electrical clearances.\n\n**(4) Depiction of Utility Poles or Electric Equipment:**\n*   **Utility Poles:** Along the \"- OHE -\" line at the bottom of the plan, there are small symbols resembling an asterisk or a crossed circle (* / ⊗) placed directly on the line. While not explicitly defined in the provided legend, in standard drafting conventions, these specific symbols situated on an OHE line represent utility poles. One is visible near the bottom left, one near the middle-bottom, and one near the bottom right.\n*   **Other Equipment:** There are no obvious ground-mounted electrical transformers or equipment pads depicted in the immediate vicinity of the OHE line on this landscape plan.\n\n**(5) Trees Positioned Within Clear Sight of OHE Lines (Clearance Zones):**\n*   **Yes.** Based on the physical drawing, numerous tree canopies (represented by the drawn circles) are positioned immediately adjacent to, and in several cases physically overlap, the line marked \"- OHE -\".\n*   Given the graphical scale at the bottom right (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the centers (trunks) of the proposed and existing trees along the southern boundary are positioned within just a few feet of the overhead electric line route, placing their depicted canopies directly underneath or extending into the path of the OHE lines."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778187986290,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR243T532C0RQ8B8PSGSERBA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C2S7kFv6DnTkTbDW2AShxR","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads as dashed rectangular outlines at identified locations (NW of Bldg 1, W of Bldg 2, E of Bldg 4, SW of Bldg 8, S of Bldg 7), but no specific dimensions or clearance callouts are provided to buildings or structures.","reasoning":"While the pads are graphically represented, exact dimensions of the pad footprints and horizontal clearances to adjacent buildings cannot be determined from the submitted plans. The required 5-foot clearance from buildings per UCM § 1.10.4 cannot be verified without labeled dimensions showing pad size and distance to nearest building edges.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations shown but pad dimensions and horizontal clearances to buildings not dimensioned on plans. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) and grading plan (Sheet 11) were examined for retaining walls. Retaining walls are present on the site (noted on site plan north of detention pond and around perimeter), but none are located immediately adjacent to the 5 transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"While retaining walls exist on the property, they do not appear to be positioned adjacent to any of the transformer pads based on the graphic layouts. Since the applicability condition (retaining walls present adjacent to transformer pads) is not met, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls located adjacent to transformer pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 and Sheet 9 show transformer pads and general fence/gate locations, but no specific horizontal clearances are dimensioned between any transformer pad and adjacent fences or gates. No notes identify which transformer pads have operator/control features or which sides face removable ventilated obstructions.","reasoning":"Without labeled clearance dimensions and without identification of which transformer sides have operators/controls (requiring 5-foot clearance) versus sides without operators (requiring 3-foot clearance), compliance cannot be determined. The required clearance (5 feet or 3 feet depending on side function) cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations if fences are adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearances from transformer pads to any adjacent fences not dimensioned; transformer operator/control designations not identified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No clearances to buildings (reduced or otherwise) are labeled on the electrical plan (Sheet 21). No architectural specifications, fire rating documentation, or Austin Energy Design written approvals are provided in the site plan set or supplementary documents.","reasoning":"The plans do not show any clearances less than the standard 5-foot requirement, and provide no evidence of the four conditions required for reduced clearance (not in confined space, 10 ft+ to windows/doors/ducts, 15 ft+ vertical clearance, 3-hour fire rating). Without these documents, compliance with reduced clearance conditions cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances shown; documentation of AE Design approval and required conditions not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations, and building locations with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) data are noted on Sheet 21. However, no building elevation drawings, section drawings, or callouts show balconies, overhangs, or other structures above or lateral to transformer pads, and no clearance dimensions are provided.","reasoning":"Building elevations and cross-sections are not provided in the submitted plan set. Without these drawings showing building features above or adjacent to transformer pads, and without labeled clearance dimensions, the required 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies and prohibition on overhead structures cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to building features"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations and sections not provided; no clearances shown from balconies or overhangs to transformer pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation drawings are provided showing window, door, or ventilating duct locations relative to transformer pad locations. No transformer equipment specifications (oil-filled vs dry-type) are documented. No horizontal clearances or lateral separation measurements are shown on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The required 12-foot horizontal clearance for oil-filled equipment when windows/doors/ducts are less than 12 feet from grade or have less than 5 feet lateral separation cannot be verified without: (1) building elevations showing these openings, (2) transformer type specifications, and (3) measured clearances on the plan.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to building apertures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations not provided; window/door locations unknown; transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type) not specified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows sidewalks on the western perimeter labeled '5' Concrete Sidewalk' and internal sidewalks labeled '4' Concrete Sidewalk'. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. However, no horizontal clearance dimensions are provided between any transformer pad and the back-of-sidewalk location.","reasoning":"While sidewalks exist on the site and transformer pads are shown, the required 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalk cannot be verified without labeled dimensions. The exact position of the back-of-sidewalk relative to each pad footprint is not dimensioned.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads adjacent to sidewalks (western perimeter and internal paths)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk locations noted but clearances from transformer pads to back-of-sidewalk not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"No stairwell locations are identified on the site plan (Sheet 9) or electrical plan (Sheet 21). Building floor plans are not provided in the submitted set to show interior or exterior stairwell locations.","reasoning":"Without building floor plans or elevation drawings showing stairwell locations relative to transformer pads, the proximity of stairwells to transformer pads cannot be assessed, and compliance with clearance requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building floor plans not provided; stairwell locations unknown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows fire hydrant locations and fire lanes but does not explicitly label fire escape locations. No building elevations showing fire escapes are provided. Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The 20-foot horizontal/radial clearance requirement for oil-filled equipment cannot be verified without: (1) fire escape locations identified on site or elevation drawings, (2) transformer type specification, and (3) measured clearances from pad edges to fire escapes.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to fire escapes (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire escape locations not shown; transformer type (oil-filled vs dry-type) not specified; clearances not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads with dashed rectangular outlines at identified locations. However, no labels or callouts indicate which side is the access door side, and no 10-foot clearance dimensions are shown from any pad's access side to open areas or adjacent structures.","reasoning":"The hot-stick use area clearance requirement (10-foot minimum to open area or adjacent building/structure on access door side) cannot be verified without: (1) identification of access door orientation for each pad, (2) definition of 'open area' vs obstacles on the plan, and (3) labeled clearance dimensions.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Access door orientations not identified; hot-stick clearance dimensions not shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not identify any pads as being in a confined space, niche, vault, or notched-out building configuration. No building cross-sections or elevation details showing enclosed areas are provided.","reasoning":"The 15-foot clearance requirement for transformer pads facing confined spaces cannot be verified without architectural drawings showing building configurations and niche details. The absence of such documentation does not confirm compliance, as the pads might be in confined spaces not yet detailed.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads if located in confined spaces (not identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche/enclosed area configuration not documented; building cross-sections not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) identifies 2 proposed private fire hydrants on the site (one south of Building 7, one west of Building 6) and 1 existing public fire hydrant (NW corner, in ROW). However, no horizontal clearance dimensions are shown from these fire hydrant locations to any transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without labeled clearance dimensions between fire hydrants and transformer pads, the required 5-foot clearance cannot be verified. The graphic proximity on the plan is insufficient without specific measurements.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to fire hydrants"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant locations shown but clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 32 (Tree List) identifies tree species and their Appendix F utility-compatible status (marked as 'Y' for most trees). Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows planting locations but does not correlate specific tree locations to transformer pad locations. The Appendix F utility-compatible designation in the tree list is present, but no cross-reference to specific trees within 10 lateral feet of each transformer pad is provided.","reasoning":"While tree species are listed and utility-compatibility status is documented, the spatial relationship between specific trees and transformer pads cannot be verified without: (1) building numbers on the landscape plan, (2) transformer pad identifications on the landscape plan, or (3) a table correlating tree numbers to proximity of utilities. Thus, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed tree planting locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree species and utility-compatibility status documented but spatial proximity of specific trees to transformer pads not correlated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows planting areas and landscape zones (marked as H-3 for street yard and H-4 for parking lot) but does not specifically identify shrub or low-lying vegetation locations relative to transformer pad access door orientations. No landscape details showing specific shrub/groundcover planting locations near transformer pads are provided.","reasoning":"The required clearances (10 feet from access door side, 5 feet from other sides) cannot be verified without: (1) identification of transformer access door orientations on the landscape plan, (2) specific shrub planting locations, and (3) measured clearances. Landscape details sheets showing these relationships are absent.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to proposed shrub planting"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrub/vegetation planting locations not correlated to transformer pad locations or access door orientations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 32 (Tree List) shows surveyed trees with species and utility status. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows tree planting symbols. However, no root barrier details are shown anywhere in the plan set, and no identification is made of which trees are within 20 lateral feet of the 5 transformer pads to require root barriers.","reasoning":"Root barrier compliance cannot be verified without: (1) identification of trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads, (2) detail sheets showing root barrier specifications (4-foot depth, 5-foot distance from equipment), and (3) dimensional correlation between tree locations and transformer pads. Detail sheets are not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads (not identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier requirements and details not shown; trees within 20-foot proximity of pads not identified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) and trash collection notes reference trash collection areas and notes in the administrative blocks. The note mentions 'curbside unattended container restrictions' but does not identify permanent dumpster enclosures on the site plan relative to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"While trash collection is addressed, no dumpsters or dumpster enclosures are explicitly identified on the site plan or the electrical plan in proximity to transformer pads. In the absence of a dumpster shown, this applicability condition is not met.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters identified on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) shows bicycle parking locations as an administrative requirement ('Bicycle Parking: 5 required; 41 provided'). However, no specific bike rack locations are graphically shown on the site plan in proximity to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Bicycle parking is required on the project, but specific bike rack locations are not identified on the plans near transformer pads. Without shown bike racks adjacent to transformer locations, the applicability condition is not met.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Specific bike rack locations not shown on plan near transformer pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. The site plan (Sheet 9) notes that site lighting must comply with full cut-off and fully shielded requirements per Subchapter E 2.5, but no photometric plan or light pole locations are provided to determine proximity to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Without a photometric or lighting plan showing specific light pole locations relative to transformer pads, and without labeled clearance dimensions, the required 5-foot clearance from light poles cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to light poles (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Photometric/lighting plan not provided; light pole locations unknown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows fire lanes with widths of 20-27 feet and includes signage requirements ('NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE'). However, no specific 15-foot clearance dimensions are shown from transformer pad locations to fire lane boundaries.","reasoning":"While fire lanes are designated on the plan, the 15-foot clearance requirement from transformer pads to fire lanes cannot be verified without labeled dimensions showing the distance from each pad's edge to the nearest fire lane boundary.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads in relation to designated fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes designated but clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads at distinct locations (NW of Bldg 1, W of Bldg 2, E of Bldg 4, SW of Bldg 8, S of Bldg 7). While multiple pads are present, they are widely distributed across the site and do not appear to be immediately adjacent to each other.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires multiple transformer pads to be proximate to one another. These 5 pads are at opposite corners and separate building areas, suggesting the 5-foot inter-pad clearance is not a constraining requirement. The condition of 'multiple transformer pads adjacent to each other' does not appear to apply.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple transformer pads shown but widely distributed; no inter-pad clearance concern identified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows proposed water line routing from the existing 8-inch main at the southwest corner of the property, with branches serving all eight buildings. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. However, no horizontal clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and the water line routing paths.","reasoning":"The required 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts showing the distance from each transformer pad edge to the nearest point of the water line. The utility notes on Sheet 19 require contractor field verification but do not provide plan-based dimension proof.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to proposed water line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing shown but horizontal clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows proposed wastewater line routing from the existing main at the northwest corner, with service lines branching to buildings. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. However, no horizontal clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and wastewater line paths.","reasoning":"The required 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts on the plan showing distances from each transformer pad to the wastewater lines. Field verification noted in utility notes is insufficient for plan review compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to proposed wastewater line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater line routing shown but horizontal clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows proposed storm drain routing along western and southern site boundaries with inlet structures in drive aisles. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. However, no horizontal clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and storm drain line routing.","reasoning":"The required 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts showing distances from each transformer pad edge to the nearest point of the storm drain system. The graphic proximity alone is insufficient.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to proposed storm drain routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain routing shown but horizontal clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan and utility documents (Sheet 19 and supplementary utilities description) make no reference to gas service to any building on the property. The utility routing shown includes only water, wastewater, and storm drain lines.","reasoning":"Without evidence of gas service infrastructure on the site, the applicability condition for gas line separations is not met. This is a discretionary utility; its absence from the plans indicates it was not proposed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service proposed on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows routing of water, wastewater, and storm drain utilities. Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and references underground electric lines. However, no horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and any utility lines, and no legend or note specifies 12-inch clearances.","reasoning":"The 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from other underground utilities cannot be verified without explicit dimension callouts on the plan. The utility notes require contractor field verification but do not provide plan-based compliance evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utility routing shown but horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines. Sheet 21 shows proposed underground electric lines and transformer pad locations. However, no cross-section drawings or vertical utility separation callouts are provided showing whether utilities cross over/under each other or transformer locations.","reasoning":"Without cross-section drawings or profile views showing vertical separation between utilities and transformer locations, or between underground facilities and building foundations/structures, the prohibition on utilities crossing over/under cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer and underground facility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section/profile drawings not provided; utility crossing relationships not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads located on the site with note referencing underground electric lines and pull boxes. No overhead distribution lines are identified on the site plan or electrical plan. The utility symbols legend on Sheet 19 and plan graphics do not depict overhead distribution lines crossing the property.","reasoning":"Without evidence of overhead distribution line facilities on the site, the applicability condition is not met. The project appears to utilize underground electrical service, not overhead distribution.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution lines identified on site; underground service appears to be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) do not identify any overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors on or crossing the property. The project infrastructure is entirely underground-based for electrical service.","reasoning":"Without overhead distribution primary/neutral conductors present on the site, the 15-foot radius clearance requirement is not applicable. Underground service eliminates this overhead conductor clearance concern.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution conductors identified on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads as surface installations with dashed rectangular outlines. No notching, niching, or enclosed configurations are indicated. The pads appear to be located in open areas adjacent to buildings, not within building footprints or enclosed areas.","reasoning":"All transformer pads are shown as surface-mounted installations in exterior locations. No niche service installations (where equipment is accessible from outside but within building footprint) are indicated on the plans. The applicability condition for niche installations is not met.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads shown as surface-mounted; no niche installations indicated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads as surface installations. No niche service installations are proposed, indicated, or referenced in any plan sheet or supplementary document.","reasoning":"Since no niche service installations are indicated on the project (EL-13.29 determined no niches are proposed), the requirements for niche fire walls, ventilation, and AE Design coordination do not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) shows no parking garages, underground parking structures, or enclosed overhead structures above transformer locations. The site layout indicates surface parking and external transformer pad installations.","reasoning":"Cross-section drawings are required only when overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas exist above or adjacent to transformer locations. None of these conditions are present on this site. The applicability condition is not met.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas above transformer locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows surface drainage patterns with flow arrows and spot elevations indicating drainage direction (generally toward western entrance and eastern boundary). However, no transformer pad locations are identified on this grading plan, and no transformer equipment type specifications (oil-filled vs dry-type) are provided on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The requirement to slope drainage away from buildings for oil-filled transformer equipment cannot be verified without: (1) identification of which transformers are oil-filled, (2) location of those pads on the grading plan, and (3) documented drainage slope direction at those specific locations. Transformer type is not specified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations (if oil-filled equipment is used)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type) not specified; transformer locations not shown on grading plan; surface drainage direction not documented at transformer locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads at various locations on the site. Sheet 2 (Plat) shows property boundary and right-of-way limits. However, no specific dimension callouts or property line labels are provided on the electrical plan showing that each transformer pad is 100% on private property, and none indicate whether any pad straddles property lines.","reasoning":"The requirement that transformers be located entirely on private property cannot be verified without specific dimension callouts from transformer pad corners to the property line, or explicit labeling confirming each pad is entirely within the property boundary. The graphic proximity alone is insufficient.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentRef