asement label, and no widths or accessibility specifications are documented. The plans do not demonstrate that adequate easements exist for all transformer locations.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements not shown for 4 of 5 pads; easement widths and accessibility requirements not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer locations and references to underground electric lines and pull boxes. However, no specific routing callouts or property line clearance dimensions are provided showing that electrical service routing from transformer to meter locations is entirely on private property.","reasoning":"The requirement that electrical routing from transformer to meter be 100% on private property cannot be verified without specific dimension callouts or routing notes confirming the electrical service path does not cross public right-of-way. The graphic layout alone is insufficient.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from each transformer pad to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical service routing from transformer to meter not verified as 100% on private property; no routing callouts or property line clearance dimensions provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows 5 transformer pads as dashed rectangular outlines but does not provide specific dimensions for any pad. No service type specifications (single-phase vs three-phase) are documented on the electrical plan or in supplementary documents. No Austin Energy Design-approved pad detail sheets are included in the submission.","reasoning":"Compliance with transformer pad dimensions matching AE Design-approved specifications for the specified service type cannot be verified. The plans lack: (1) pad dimensions, (2) service type designation, and (3) reference to or inclusion of AE Design pad detail sheets.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions not shown; service type (single-phase vs three-phase) not specified; AE Design pad detail sheets not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows surface parking areas adjacent to central drive aisles, and Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations including Pad 2 (W of Bldg 2) and Pad 5 (S of Bldg 7) which appear to be near parking areas. However, no explicit clearance dimensions from pads to parking are labeled, and no bollard details or specifications are shown.","reasoning":"The requirement for bollards (4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal posts) when pads are within 4 feet of parking areas cannot be verified without: (1) specific distance measurements from each pad edge to parking areas, and (2) bollard detail specifications. No bollard locations or details are provided on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearances from transformer pads to parking areas not dimensioned; bollard details and specifications not shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) show all electrical infrastructure as underground service; no overhead distribution lines are visible on the site plan or referenced in plan notes.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibiting customer facilities under or over overhead distribution facilities does not apply when no overhead distribution facilities are present. The project utilizes underground electrical service exclusively, so this overhead-related requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities present on site; underground service provided."}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf4cadeb-5bcf-4243-9f2a-f46b39f4aa86","uuid":"e5fea35a-e806-4045-9df7-6b717d10213a"}
