ricted zone adjacent to overhead electric distribution lines. No Austin Energy approval is documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) are positioned along the overhead electric distribution line boundary on the landscape plan without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy written approval. Provide documented Austin Energy approval authorizing these species within the restricted zone, or relocate trees to beyond 15 lateral feet from the outside conductor."}]},{"text":"Large trees (Cedar Elm 40–50 ft, Live Oak 50–80 ft, Hackberry 40–60 ft mature height per ECM Appendix F) are positioned within the 25-foot minimum clearance zone from distribution conductors.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with mature heights 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) shown directly on distribution OHE line on landscape plan, violating 25-foot minimum clearance from distribution conductors."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are proposed within 25 feet of overhead electric distribution lines without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy approval."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees (Cedar Elm at 40-50 feet, Live Oak at 50-80 feet, Hackberry at 40-60 feet mature height) are positioned along the overhead electric distribution line without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy approval. Provide clearance calculations or documented Austin Energy approval for trees within 25 feet of the distribution conductor, or relocate large trees to beyond 25 lateral feet from the outside conductor."}]},{"text":"Six mitigation trees are shown directly on the overhead electric line with no documented written Austin Energy approval authorizing species, locations, or sizes within restricted zones.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.15","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Six trees positioned directly on overhead electric line without documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing the clearance variance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones (non-UC Cedar Elm and Live Oak within 15 feet of overhead distribution line). No documented Austin Energy written approval is provided. Applicant must obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy or modify tree species/locations to comply with clearance requirements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees are positioned within prohibited electrical clearance zones without documented written approval from Austin Energy. Obtain and submit explicit written approval from Austin Energy authorizing the proposed tree placement (species, locations, and sizes) within restricted zones, or relocate all trees to comply with minimum clearance distances (15 feet from distribution conductors for non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for large trees, 10 feet from utility poles)."}]},{"text":"Trees are positioned directly on the OHE distribution line indicating zero clearance; no clearance distances documented or dimensioned on the landscape plan.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.14","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees are shown directly on overhead electric line, indicating zero clearance maintained from distribution conductor. No clearance distances documented or dimensioned."}]}]},{"headline":"Tree clearances from utility poles undocumented","summary":"Clearance distances between proposed trees and utility poles are not dimensioned on the landscape plan, preventing verification that trees meet the 10-foot minimum lateral clearance requirement from poles.","sheets":[21,31],"applicableArea":"Southern property boundary","severity":2,"confidence":2,"c