rovide root barrier details on landscape detail sheets (minimum 4-foot depth, 5-foot offset from equipment), or document that all trees are beyond 20 feet from underground equipment.","details":[{"text":"Underground electric equipment locations from the electrical plan (Sheet 21) are not shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). Clearance dimensions from proposed and retained trees to all underground equipment are not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Distances between proposed trees and underground electrical equipment not documented on plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Specific locations of underground electrical equipment are not dimensioned relative to tree placements. Clearance verification cannot be determined from available documentation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground electric equipment locations from electrical plan (Sheet 21) are not shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31). Provide landscape plan with underground equipment (pull boxes, vaults) overlaid and labeled, with clearance dimensions from proposed and retained trees to all underground equipment, or add dimension callouts demonstrating trees are at least 5 lateral feet from all underground equipment."}]},{"text":"Pad-mounted equipment locations are not dimensioned relative to proposed tree placements on the landscape plan. Clearance verification cannot be completed from available documentation.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.7","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Pad-mounted equipment locations are not dimensioned relative to proposed tree placements on the landscape plan. Clearance verification cannot be completed from available documentation."}]},{"text":"Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment are not identified on the landscape plan. Root barrier specifications (minimum 4-foot depth, 5-foot offset from equipment) are not provided on landscape detail sheets.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.9","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Root barrier specifications, depths, and positions not documented for trees within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trees within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment are not identified on the landscape plan, and root barrier specifications for such locations are not shown on landscape details."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"For any trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, provide root barrier details on a landscape detail sheet specifying minimum 4-foot depth and 5-foot offset from equipment. Alternatively, provide landscape plan documentation showing all trees are beyond 20 feet from underground equipment."}]}]},{"headline":"Tree species and sizes not differentiated on plans","summary":"Large trees (mature height ≥40 feet) are not visually distinguished on the landscape plan, and tree species are not keyed by legend or labeled directly on the plan. The plant schedule lists installation heights only, not mature heights, making it impossible to identify which trees are subject to large-tree clearance restrictions.","sheets":[31,35],"applicableArea":"Landscape plan","severity":1,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Adding mature height notes to the plant schedule and using distinct symbols or notation on the landscape plan to identify large trees (Cedar Elm ~40–50 ft, Live Oak ~50–80 ft, Hackberry ~40–60 ft) will facilitate verification of electrical clearance compliance.","details":[{"text":"Large trees (Cedar Elm ~40–50 ft, Live Oak ~50–80 ft, Hackberry ~40–60 ft per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape plan or identified in the plant schedule by mature height, only by installation size (16' minimum).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.11","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Live Oak and Cedar Elm are large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) but plant schedule does not differentiate or identify them as large trees; only planting size (16' minimum) is documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not visually differentiated on the landscape plan. Plant schedule lists installation heights (16'), not mature heights, making it difficult to identify trees subject to large-tree clearance restrictions."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees (mature height ≥40 feet) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. Add a note to the plant schedule specifying mature height for each proposed tree species, and use a distinct symbol or notation on the landscape plan to identify large trees (Cedar Elm ~40-50 ft, Live Oak ~50-80 ft, Hackberry ~40-60 ft) to allow verification of electrical clearance compliance."}]},{"text":"Trees proposed near electric facilities on the landscape plan are not identified by species using a keyed legend; species identification requires manual cross-reference to a separate plant list rather than direct labeling on the plan.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.10","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees proposed near electric facilities on the landscape plan are not identified by species using a keyed legend. Species identification requires manual cross-reference to a separate plant list rather than direct labeling on the plan."}]}]},{"headline":"Clearance distances from trees not dimensioned","summary":"No dimension lines are provided on the landscape plan showing clearances from trees to overhead electric conductors. Measurement reference points (trunk center vs. canopy edge) and measurement methodology cannot be verified from available documentation.","sheets":[21,31],"applicableArea":"Landscape plan trees near overhead electric line","