{"level":30,"time":1778188305597,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24G78D9QN5WR19RPNMYF1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully synthesized your electrical clearance and documentation findings into a consolidated review output.\n\n## Summary of the Review Synthesis\n\n**Total Input Findings:** 30 items across 3 independent review runs\n**Output Comments:** 9 consolidated comments\n**Consolidation Ratio:** 3.3:1\n\n### Key Thematic Groupings:\n\n1. **Building Elevation Documentation** — Missing surveyed building elevations with overhead conductor locations and clearance dimensions (7 findings consolidated)\n\n2. **Vertical Clearances** — Driveway and parking area vertical clearances from overhead conductors requiring surveyor mid-span measurements (3 findings)\n\n3. **Fence & Perimeter Elements** — Fence face and post clearances from overhead conductors and utility poles (3 findings)\n\n4. **Retaining Walls** — Section views with clearance verification from overhead lines (2 findings)\n\n5. **Landscape & Decorative Features** — Tree utility compatibility and decorative lighting clearances (2 findings)\n\n6. **Electrical Equipment** — Meter access clearances and transformer clearances (2 findings)\n\n7. **Down Guy Wires** — Guy anchor conflicts and easement documentation (2 findings)\n\n8. **Utility Coordination** — Water line clearances, building foundation setbacks, easement protection, pole conflicts (7 findings)\n\n9. **Construction Safety** — Staging area clearances and mandatory utility notification (2 findings)\n\nAll 30 input findings are preserved as individual details within the 9 comments, maintaining citation specificity, run-by-run comments verbatim, and specific measurements/locations. Cross-departmental coordination requirements and attention flags are noted where applicable."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc4d35b1-896c-4182-be6b-ea8d895e76fd","uuid":"a3535085-3536-47e7-8efa-5f68c2617c14"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188305602,"pid":122,"hostname":"13276d9b-948","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":229589,"duration_api_ms":229493,"num_turns":3,"result":"Perfect! I've successfully synthesized your electrical clearance and documentation findings into a consolidated review output.\n\n## Summary of the Review Synthesis\n\n**Total Input Findings:** 30 items across 3 independent review runs\n**Output Comments:** 9 consolidated comments\n**Consolidation Ratio:** 3.3:1\n\n### Key Thematic Groupings:\n\n1. **Building Elevation Documentation** — Missing surveyed building elevations with overhead conductor locations and clearance dimensions (7 findings consolidated)\n\n2. **Vertical Clearances** — Driveway and parking area vertical clearances from overhead conductors requiring surveyor mid-span measurements (3 findings)\n\n3. **Fence & Perimeter Elements** — Fence face and post clearances from overhead conductors and utility poles (3 findings)\n\n4. **Retaining Walls** — Section views with clearance verification from overhead lines (2 findings)\n\n5. **Landscape & Decorative Features** — Tree utility compatibility and decorative lighting clearances (2 findings)\n\n6. **Electrical Equipment** — Meter access clearances and transformer clearances (2 findings)\n\n7. **Down Guy Wires** — Guy anchor conflicts and easement documentation (2 findings)\n\n8. **Utility Coordination** — Water line clearances, building foundation setbacks, easement protection, pole conflicts (7 findings)\n\n9. **Construction Safety** — Staging area clearances and mandatory utility notification (2 findings)\n\nAll 30 input findings are preserved as individual details within the 9 comments, maintaining citation specificity, run-by-run comments verbatim, and specific measurements/locations. Cross-departmental coordination requirements and attention flags are noted where applicable.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cc4d35b1-896c-4182-be6b-ea8d895e76fd","total_cost_usd":0.24535295,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65343,"cache_read_input_tokens":92002,"output_tokens":30888,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":65343},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":30888,"cacheReadInputTokens":92002,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65343,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24535295,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing surveyed building elevations with conductor clearance data","summary":"Building elevation drawings with registered surveyor data showing overhead conductor locations and clearance dimensions must be provided to verify required clearances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial). All dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor, not pole center.","sheets":[4,9,21,31],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordinate with registered surveyor and utility for conductor elevation data","attn":"Verify surveyor will conduct site survey to obtain existing pole locations and mid-span conductor elevations","details":[{"text":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and labeled clearance dimensions must be provided showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductors to all building faces.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and labeled clearance dimensions are required to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Surveyed elevations of existing overhead conductors and building elevation drawings showing clearance dimensions are required to verify 7'6\" sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from conductors to building faces and projections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions must be provided to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from all buildings to existing overhead electric conductors."}]},{"text":"Plans must show 15-foot radial clearance dimension lines from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to all proposed buildings and customer facilities in both plan and section views.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearance dimension lines showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to all customer facilities must be provided on site plan and section views."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans must specify whether existing overhead lines are distribution primary/neutral conductors, and provide 15-foot radial clearance dimensions from outside conductor to all customer facilities in plan and section views."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans must show radial clearance dimensions from the outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to all proposed buildings, parking areas, and site facilities, demonstrating minimum 15-foot radial clearance is maintained."}]},{"text":"Building elevation sheets must show all building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) with clearance dimensions demonstrating both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets showing all building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) with dimensions and clearance verification from overhead electric conductors are required."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and dimension annotations showing clearances from conductors to all building projections (roofs, parapets, overhangs, decks, patios) must be provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation drawings must show all building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, patios) with clearance dimensions to overhead electric conductors demonstrating both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained."}]},{"text":"Building elevations with labeled clearance dimensions from overhead electric facilities in adjacent Valley View Road ROW must be provided for structures near property boundary, demonstrating both clearance requirements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevations with labeled clearance dimensions from overhead electric facilities in adjacent ROW must be provided, demonstrating both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Austin Energy utility plan showing exact location of overhead facilities in adjacent ROW with clearance dimensions from buildings must be provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets must show surveyed overhead conductor elevations with clearance dimensions demonstrating buildings maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from electric facilities in adjacent right-of-way."}]},{"text":"Building elevation sheets prepared by registered surveyor must include surveyed elevations and locations of existing overhead conductors with dimension annotations showing clearances. Sheets must be sealed by both registered surveyor and engineer.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Building elevation sheets must be submitted, including registered surveyor data showing surveyed conductor elevation and clearance dimension annotations for all buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation sheets prepared by registered surveyor must include surveyed elevations and locations of existing overhead conductors with dimension annotations showing clearances to building components."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Building elevation sheets showing surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimension annotations must be provided to demonstrate required clearances are met. These sheets must be sealed by a registered surveyor and engineer."}]},{"text":"Section and plan view exhibits must show dimension lines originating at the outside conductor location and extending to the outermost edge of each building and building projection, with dimension lines extending from the conductor, not pole center.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits must be added showing dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of each building and building projection for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3. Dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor location, not pole center."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Provide enlarged plan details and section views with dimension lines extending from outside conductor to outermost edges of all buildings and building projections, demonstrating required clearance envelopes are maintained."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits with dimension lines from the outer conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections must be provided for all proposed structures within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities."}]},{"text":"All clearance dimension annotations must explicitly show that dimensions are measured from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from utility pole centerline. Dimension lines must originate clearly at the outer conductor location.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"All clearance dimension lines must originate at the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from pole center or centerline of multi-conductor installations. On three-phase installations, the conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension line endpoints must clearly show measurement origin at the conductor location."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"All clearance dimension annotations must explicitly originate at the outside conductor location, not at the utility pole centerline or pole face. Dimension lines and callouts must clearly show measurement origin point (e.g., '15'-0\" from outside conductor')."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Any clearance dimension annotations must explicitly show that dimensions are measured from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from utility pole centerline. Dimension lines must originate at the outer conductor location."}]}]},{"headline":"Driveway vertical clearances and surveyor mid-span measurements required","summary":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance measurements must be provided showing vertical distance from lowest point of overhead facilities (including conductors, attachments, and telecommunications cables) to finished driveway grades and parking areas, with section views demonstrating 16-foot (parking only) or 18-foot (truck traffic) clearance.","sheets":[9,11],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordinate with surveyor on pole and conductor elevation data; verify anticipated vehicle types (trucks vs. passenger vehicles only)","attn":"Clarify whether parking areas will accommodate trucks; if yes, 18-foot clearance required per UCM § 1.10.6.2","details":[{"text":"Vertical clearance dimensions must be provided for the driveway where the OHE line crosses, showing minimum 16-foot clearance (no truck traffic) or 18-foot (with truck traffic) from lowest point of overhead electric line including all attachments to finished driveway grade.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions must be provided for the driveway where the OHE line crosses, showing minimum 16-foot or 18-foot clearance from the lowest point of the overhead electric line (including any attachments) to the finished driveway grade. Registered surveyor data for mid-span clearance verification is required."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data must be provided showing vertical clearance from lowest point of overhead facilities (including all conductors and attachments) to finished driveway grades. Section views must show 16-foot clearance for parking without truck traffic or 18-foot for areas with truck traffic."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading plan and section views must show vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead electric facilities (including telecommunications attachments) to finished driveway grade, demonstrating 16-foot minimum (18-foot if truck traffic)."}]},{"text":"If parking or vehicle display areas are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, section views with labeled vertical clearance dimensions must be provided showing the required clearance (16 feet for residential/pedestrian parking, 18 feet if truck traffic anticipated).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"If parking or vehicle display areas are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, section views with labeled vertical clearance dimensions must be provided to demonstrate the required clearance (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet for parking without trucks, 18 feet with truck traffic)."}]},{"text":"Registered surveyor clearance survey showing pole locations and mid-span clearances from overhead facilities to driveways, parking areas, and buildings must be provided to verify all vertical clearance requirements (7.5-foot, 16-foot, 18-foot) are satisfied.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Registered surveyor data must be provided showing pole locations, overhead conductor elevations, and mid-span clearance measurements for the driveway crossing. This data is essential to verify the minimum 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance requirement per UCM § 1.10.6.2."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Registered surveyor must provide documented mid-span clearance measurements for existing overhead facilities showing vertical distance from lowest point of conductors and attachments to highest proposed site features (building roofs, HVAC equipment, etc.) to demonstrate code-required clearances are maintained."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Registered surveyor clearance survey showing pole locations and mid-span clearances from overhead facilities to driveways, parking areas, and buildings must be provided to verify all vertical clearance requirements (7.5-foot, 16-foot, 18-foot) are satisfied."}]}]},{"headline":"Fence and perimeter element clearances from overhead lines","summary":"Fence face alignment and fence post locations must maintain minimum clearances from overhead electric conductors and utility poles: 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductor to fence face, and 10-foot clearance from fence posts to pole centerlines. Dimension annotations must be provided on site plan.","sheets":[4,9],"applicableArea":"Valley View Road Frontage","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Verify whether fences along southern property boundary (near ROW) will obstruct existing pole maintenance access","details":[{"text":"Plan must include dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from outside conductor to fence face, measured from conductor location not from pole centerline.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan must include dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from outside conductor to fence face, measured from conductor location not from pole centerline."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan dimensions must show fence alignments maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor (not from pole centerline) of existing overhead electric facilities."}]},{"text":"Dimension annotations must show fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric utility pole centers. Pole locations must be clearly identified on site plan.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Dimension annotations must be provided showing fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric poles."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan must clearly identify existing utility pole locations and provide dimension annotations showing minimum 10-foot clearance from fence posts to pole centerlines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan view dimensions must demonstrate fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric utility pole centers."}]},{"text":"Enlarged plan details must show existing power pole locations at property ends and verify that proposed sidewalk alignments maintain adequate clearance from pole structures, or document if poles must be relocated.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Enlarged plan details must show existing power pole locations at property ends and document that proposed sidewalk alignments maintain adequate clearance from pole structures, or note if poles are to be relocated."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan view must clarify that new or modified sidewalks at each end of the property along right-of-way frontage are cleared of existing power poles, or if poles must be relocated to accommodate sidewalk."}]}]},{"headline":"Retaining wall clearances from overhead conductors","summary":"Section views for retaining walls must be provided with dimension annotations showing vertical and/or clearance spacing from outside conductor to wall face, demonstrating compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement where walls are near overhead electric lines.","sheets":[9,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Verify which retaining walls are located within potential clearance distance of OHE line at southern site boundary","details":[{"text":"Section views showing retaining wall elevations with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall must be provided to demonstrate compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Section views showing retaining wall elevations with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall must be provided to demonstrate compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"If retaining walls are located near overhead electric lines, provide section views with dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to wall face."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan and section views must show dimensions from the outermost electric line to retaining wall faces, demonstrating minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained."}]},{"text":"Section exhibits for retaining walls must show dimensions from the outer conductor to the outermost edge of each wall for clearance verification per UCM § 1.10.3.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Section views for retaining walls near any overhead electric lines must include dimension annotations showing clearance from outside conductor to wall face."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Section exhibits must show dimensions from the outer conductor to the outermost edge of each retaining wall for clearance verification."}]}]},{"headline":"Tree species and landscape feature clearances from overhead lines","summary":"All trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be verified as utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F (marked 'UC', generally ≤20 feet mature height). Currently proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are not utility-compatible. Trees must be relocated beyond 10 feet or replaced with utility-compatible species. Decorative lighting fixtures require clearance verification if positioned beneath overhead lines.","sheets":[9,31,35],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordinate with landscape architect on tree relocation or species substitution","attn":"Confirm whether proposed tree species have been reviewed for utility compatibility; ECM Appendix F required for verification","details":[{"text":"All trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC'). Currently proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are not utility-compatible. Trees must be relocated beyond 10 feet of conductors or replaced with utility-compatible species per ECM § 2.4.1.D and UCM § 1.10.10.4.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"All trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors must be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, marked 'UC'). The currently proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are not utility-compatible. Trees must either be relocated to positions more than 10 feet from conductors, or replaced with utility-compatible species verified in ECM Appendix F 'UC' column."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Plant schedule must specify which tree species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F for planting within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Tree species must be marked or noted as 'UC' (Utility Compatible, generally ≤20' mature height). Plan must include dimension annotations showing lateral distance (horizontal) from each tree location to the overhead conductor and note species compliance with utility compatibility requirement."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan must verify that all trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors (per more restrictive UCM 50-foot standard) are species marked 'UC' (Utility Compatible) in ECM Appendix F, generally mature height ≤20 feet. Annotate lateral distances."}]},{"text":"If decorative lighting fixtures are positioned beneath overhead electric lines, photometric plan or enlarged detail must show locations with dimension annotations verifying 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance requirements are met, or provide relocation notes.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.36","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Photometric plan or enlarged lighting detail must show locations of all decorative light fixtures near overhead electric lines with dimension annotations verifying clearance requirements are met (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial), or notes indicating fixtures are relocated away from lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Photometric plan or site plan must show decorative lighting fixture locations with clearance verification demonstrating 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from overhead lines, or relocation notes if conflicts exist."}]}]},{"headline":"Electrical equipment clearances and working space deficiencies","summary":"Electrical meter locations and transformer equipment require detailed documentation of working clearances and clearance from overhead conductors. Meter locations must maintain 30-inch-wide clear access space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom with no obstructions. Transformers must maintain 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance from overhead conductors.","sheets":[21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Coordinate with electrical engineer and utility on meter location requirements and transformer specifications","attn":"Verify utility meter access requirements; confirm whether pad-mounted or pole-mounted transformers are proposed","details":[{"text":"Enlarged meter detail views must show 30-inch front width, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances around each meter location, confirming no site features, fences, walls, vegetation, or building projections obstruct access per UCM § 1.9.3.1.","citation":"UCM § 1.9.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.38","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Enlarged detail drawings of proposed meter locations must be provided showing no obstructions to meter access and working clearances: minimum 30 inches wide, 36 inches deep front access space, and 6.5 feet headroom per UCM § 1.10.9."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Enlarged meter detail views must show 30-inch front width, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances around each meter location, confirming no site features, fences, walls, vegetation, or building projections obstruct access."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan details must verify that meter access areas maintain required working clearances: 30-inch-wide clear space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom, with no obstructions from fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, or building projections."}]},{"text":"Electrical plan section views must show vertical clearance dimensions from overhead line conductors to the top of all proposed transformer equipment, demonstrating 7.5-foot minimum sky-to-ground clearance.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.43","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan must specify transformer types (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) and provide section views with dimension annotations showing vertical clearance from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment, verifying 7.5-foot minimum clearance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan section views must show vertical clearance dimensions from overhead line conductors to the top of all transformer equipment, demonstrating 7.5-foot minimum sky-to-ground clearance."}]}]},{"headline":"Down guy wire anchor conflicts and easement documentation","summary":"Down guy wire anchor locations from existing utility poles must be clearly identified on site plan. Anchors must not conflict with proposed accessible paths and driveways; if conflicts exist, poles must be relocated or converted to self-supporting structures. Dedicated easements (10-foot-wide, extending minimum 5 feet past where guy wire enters ground) must be shown on easement exhibit.","sheets":[2,3,4,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Coordinate with utility company on pole relocation or self-supporting conversion if guy wire conflicts arise","attn":"Verify whether utility pole modifications (relocation or conversion) require utility coordination; confirm down guy anchor locations from site survey","details":[{"text":"Site plan must show down guy wire anchor locations from existing distribution poles and verify they do not conflict with proposed accessible paths or driveways. If conflicts exist, plans must show pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting steel poles.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy wire locations and anchors must be clearly identified on the site plan relative to all proposed accessible paths and driveways. Any conflicts must be resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting steel poles, with details and relocation notes provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan must clearly identify existing down guy wire anchor locations and document resolution of any conflicts with proposed accessible routes and driveways through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles, or provide plan notes confirming no conflicts exist."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan must show down guy wire anchor locations from existing poles and verify they do not conflict with proposed accessible paths or driveways. If conflicts exist, plans must show pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting steel poles."}]},{"text":"Easement exhibit and plat must identify and show 10-foot-wide dedicated down guy anchor easements extending minimum 5 feet past where each guy wire support cable enters the ground, per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Dedicated easements for down guy anchors must be clearly shown on the easement exhibit, displaying 10-foot width and minimum 5-foot extension past where the guy wire enters the ground, per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Easement exhibit and plat must identify and show 10-foot-wide down guy anchor easements extending minimum 5 feet past ground entry point for each down guy support cable on property."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Easement exhibit must show dedicated easements for any down guy anchors from existing distribution poles, 10 feet wide extending minimum 5 feet past where anchor enters ground."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility infrastructure coordination and clearance documentation","summary":"Water line routing, water meter locations, building foundations, utility pole positions, and elevated walkways must maintain documented clearances from overhead electric facilities. Site plan must show utility pole locations with clearance dimensions to driveways (30-foot separation preferred). Water lines and meters require clearance verification from overhead service drops. Electric easement boundaries must be shown with confirmation that no structures/features are proposed over easement; items within easement must maintain 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor.","sheets":[4,9,19,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Water utility must provide location data for existing service lines and meters; ROW/right-of-way management for easement coordination","attn":"Verify whether water service drops exist beneath or near driveway; confirm electric easement boundaries with utility","details":[{"text":"Site plan must clearly show the location of all existing utility poles and provide dimension annotations indicating clearance from driveway edges. If any poles are within 30 feet of driveway edge, relocation plans must be noted.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan must clearly show the location of all existing utility poles and provide dimension annotations indicating clearance from driveway edges. If any poles are within 30 feet of driveway edge, relocation plans must be noted."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans must clearly indicate whether existing electric poles conflict with proposed driveway alignments. If conflicts exist, relocation notes or revised pole locations must be shown with minimum 30-foot separation from driveway edge."}]},{"text":"Plans must include Austin Energy electric easement exhibit showing easement boundaries with notes confirming no buildings or permanent structures are proposed under or over overhead distribution facilities. Items within easement boundaries must maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans must include Austin Energy easement exhibit showing electric easement boundaries with notes confirming no buildings or permanent structures are proposed under or over overhead distribution facilities, and that items within easement boundaries maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor."}]},{"text":"Utility plan must show locations of overhead electric service-drop lines with dimension annotations verifying 7.5-foot clearance from service drop conductors to water meter locations.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3; UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility plan must show locations of overhead electric service-drop lines with dimension annotations verifying 7.5-foot clearance from service drop conductors to water meter locations."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility plan must show clearance dimensions from water meter locations to existing overhead electric service drop conductors, demonstrating minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance."}]},{"text":"Utility plan must show clearance dimensions between proposed water line routing and existing overhead distribution poles and conductors, documenting adequate separation.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.29","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearance dimensions must be provided showing water line routing maintains adequate separation from overhead distribution poles and conductors."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility plan must include dimension annotations showing clearance distances from water line routing to all overhead electric poles and conductors."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility plan must show clearance dimensions between proposed water line routing and existing overhead distribution poles and conductors."}]},{"text":"Plans must verify that permanent structure foundations within 5 feet of property line allow adequate clearance space (typically 5-7 feet from property line) for installation and maintenance of electric facilities in adjacent ROW or easement areas.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.30","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"If any building foundations are located within 5 feet of the property line, detailed dimensions showing clearance space for electric facility access and maintenance must be provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans must verify that permanent structure foundations within 5 feet of property line allow adequate clearance space (typically 5-7 feet from property line) for installation and maintenance of electric facilities in adjacent ROW or easement areas."}]},{"text":"Site plan must clearly document clearances from proposed buildings and structures to existing streetlight pole locations, verifying poles do not conflict with proposed construction.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.39","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"If existing streetlight poles are located near proposed buildings, clearance dimensions must be provided showing building location and pole proximity."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan must clearly document clearances from proposed buildings and structures to existing streetlight pole locations."}]},{"text":"Section views and plan dimensions must demonstrate that elevated walkways and platforms maintain minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor of overhead distribution facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"If any elevated walkways, stairs, or platforms are proposed, provide section views with dimension annotations showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Section views and plan dimensions must demonstrate that elevated walkways and platforms maintain minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor of overhead distribution facilities."}]}]},{"headline":"Construction safety clearances and utility notification requirement","summary":"Site logistics or construction phasing plan must document staging areas, equipment operation zones, crane swing radius, and work platforms with verified 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and Texas law. Cover sheet or general notes must include statement requiring owner/contractor to notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before construction near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","sheets":[1,3,5,8],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Contractor and site safety manager responsible for maintaining clearances and providing utility notification","attn":"Verify construction phasing plan accounts for overhead line constraints; confirm Austin Energy contact information for cover sheet note","details":[{"text":"Site logistics plan or construction phasing plan must show construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platform locations with verified 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and Texas law requirements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"A site logistics plan or construction phasing plan must be submitted showing staging areas, equipment laydown zones, crane swing radius, material storage, and scaffold locations, with explicit notation that all construction activities maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Construction logistics plan or site phasing plan must document staging area boundaries, crane swing radius zones, equipment laydown areas, and work platforms with dimension annotations verifying 10-foot radial clearance from all overhead electric lines. Construction management notes must address overhead line safety during all phases."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site logistics or construction phasing plan must show construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platform locations with verified 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines per OSHA and Texas law requirements."}]},{"text":"Cover sheet or general notes must include statement: 'Owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2; Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003","sourceId":"1:EL-1.46","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"A plan note must be added to the cover sheet or general notes stating: 'The owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Add note to cover sheet or general notes: 'Owner/contractor shall notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before beginning any construction activities or operations near overhead electric lines. Contact Austin Energy at [number] per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.'"},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Plans must include a note stating: 'Owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"906deabe-f647-472b-ad56-e21bbed3f892"}
